body:
[Lemma 7 (Approximation by squared projections) of arXiv:2608.22179, '\bf Token-Level Likelihood-Array Regression for Membership Inference and AI-Generated Text'] For every \(\Theta,Q\in\mathbb Q_d\),
\begin{align}
\E_{\mathcal R}
\ip{\boldsymbol\beta_R(\Theta)}{\mathcal R_R(Q)}
&=
\ip{\Theta}{Q},
\\
\E_{\mathcal R}
\left|
\ip{\boldsymbol\beta_R(\Theta)}{\mathcal R_R(Q)}
-\ip{\Theta}{Q}
\right|^2
&\leq
\frac{C}{R}\norm{\Theta}^2\norm{Q}_{\mathcal G}^2,
\\
\E_{\mathcal R}\norm{\boldsymbol\beta_R(\Theta)}^2
&=
\sum_{j=1}^{d_v}
\ip{\mathcal G_d^{-1}(\Theta_j)}{\Theta_j}_{\rm F}
\leq
\frac32\norm{\Theta}^2,

\end{align}
where
\[
\norm{Q}_{\mathcal G}^2
=
\sum_{j=1}^{d_v}
\ip{Q_j}{\mathcal G_d(Q_j)}_{\rm F}.
\]
The expectation is over the random spherical directions.

