[Col cor_global_energy of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] The unique kinetic solution to (equation Eq_SPME_intro of the paper) with initial value $u_0$ { satisfying (equation assumption_m_plus_one of the paper) admits the estimate} 
    \begin{align}
        \begin{split}
&
 \mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(
        \sup_{t\le {T}} \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}  u^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\, \int_0^{T} \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}   | \nabla (u^{(\alpha+m )/2 })|^2\,\mathrm{d} x\, \mathrm{d} t \biggr)^p
        \biggr]^{1/p}
        \\&\quad \lesssim_{(\alpha,m,n,p,\psi)} \,\int_{\mathbb{T}^d}  u_0^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\,T\bigl(\|u_0\|_{L^1(\mathbb{T}^d)} \,+\,
        \|u_0\|_{L^1(\mathbb{T}^d)}^{\alpha+m}\bigr).
        \end{split}
    \end{align}

[Definition Renewal process of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $\Phi\neq0$ is a stationary point process on $\R$, and that $\BQ$ is a probability distribution on $[0,\infty)$. Further, suppose that $X_1,X_2,...$ are random variables on $[0,\infty)$ such that $X_1\leq X_2\leq\ldots$ and
    \begin{equation}
        \Phi|_{[0,\infty)} = \sum_{n=1}^\infty \delta_{X_n}.
    \end{equation}
    Then $\Phi$ is called a \textit{(stationary) renewal process} with renewal distribution $\BQ$ if $(X_{n+1}-X_n)_{n\in\N}$ is a family of independent random variables with the common distribution $\BQ$.

