[Lemma FFV of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ be even and let \(M\) be an \(m\times n\) random matrix, $n/2 \leq m \leq n$, whose rows are independent and uniformly distributed over the set of \(\{-1,0,1\}\)-vectors with exactly \(n/2\) zero coordinates. There exists a constant $c_4>0$ such that the following holds for any fixed $v \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1}$
\begin{align*}
\textbf{P}\left(\|M v\|_2 \leq \sqrt{n}/4\right) \leq 2 e^{-c_4 n}.
\end{align*}

