body:
[Lem 12 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] For a random variable $\go$ supported on $(0,1)$ and for $k\ge 1$, we have
 \begin{align*}
 \abs{\log \E(1-\go)^k + k\E \go} \le \max\{k(k-1)/2, k/(1-\E \go)\}\cdot \E\go^2.
 \end{align*}

