[Proposition 28 (High-temperature expansion) of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $\sigma$ be an abstract Ising model on $(E, \F)$ with coupling constants $J$. Then for every $F\subseteq E$
\begin{equation}
	\big\langle\sigma(F)\big\rangle_J = \frac{\sum_{\eta\in\F}w(\eta\Delta F)}{\sum_{\eta\in\F}w(\eta)},
\end{equation}
where for $F'\subseteq E$
\begin{align*}
	w(F')= \prod_{e\in F'} \tanh(J_e).
\end{align*}

