[Lemma lem: asymp of dimension ratio with r K f of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $r,K,f$ be three integers such that $0\leq K \leq r\leq f/2$. As $n\to \infty$, uniformly over all $\lambda \vdash n$ such that $r(\lambda)= r$ and all $\mu \vdash f$ such that $\mu \subset \lambda$ and $r(\mu) = r - K$, we have
    \begin{equation}
     \frac{d_{\mu}}{d_\lambda} \asymp_r \left(\frac{f}{n} \right)^r f^{-K};
    \end{equation}
and moreover, if $K=0$ (that is, if $\mu^* = \lambda^*$), we have, denoting $k = n-f$, 
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d_{\mu}}{d_\lambda} = \left( \frac{f}{n} \right)^r \left( 1 - T(r)\frac{k}{fn} + O_r\left( \frac{1}{f^2}\right) \right).
\end{equation}

