[Corollary Zm-singlecross of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] The map $Z_{m}^{i}:[0,1]\rightarrow \lbrack 0,1]$ is
continuous and strictly increasing, and exactly one of the following holds:

\begin{enumerate}
\item (\emph{Single-crossing (SC)}) There exists a unique fixed point $
p_{m}^{i}\in (0,1)$ such that 
\begin{equation}
Z_{m}^{i}(x)>x\quad \text{for }x<p_{m}^{i},\qquad Z_{m}^{i}(x)<x\quad \text{
for }x>p_{m}^{i}.  
\end{equation}

\item (\emph{Strictly overdiagonal (SO)}) $Z_{m}^{i}(x)>x$ for all $x\in
(0,1)$.
\end{enumerate}

[Corollary factorization sy of arXiv:2609.03428, 'A New Sufficient Condition for Oriented Graphs Determined by Their Generalized Skew Spectr'] Let $S$ be a symmetric matrix over $\mathbb{F}_p$ and let $U$ be an $S$-invariant subspace of $\mathbb{F}_p^n$. Then
\begin{equation}
   \chi(S;x) = \chi(S|_U;x)\, \chi(S|_{U^\perp};x).
\end{equation}

