body:
[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite graph with coupling constants $J=(J_e)_{e\in E}$, let $F\subset E$ be a subset of edges, and let $p\in[0,1]^E$ be a parameter. Writing $q=e^{-2J}$ and $r=1-p$, we have \begin{equation}
\en_{J,p}(\A_F) = \frac{\sum_{\eta\in\F^*_G}q_\eta \times r_{F\backslash\eta}}{\sum_{\eta\in\F^*_G}q_\eta}.
\end{equation}
\par Furthermore, when $p=p^\dagger=1-q^2$, one has \begin{equation}
\edag_J(\A_F)=\en_{J,p^\dagger}(\A_F)= \Big(\prod_{e\in F}q_e\Big)\langle\sigma(F)\rangle_{J^*},
\end{equation}
where $\sigma$ is an abstract Ising model on the dual HT structure $(E,\F_G^*)$, and the coupling constants $J^*$ are dual to $J$, i.e. defined by $\tanh(J^*)=e^{-2J}$.

