[Defn of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] Suppose $Y_i$ are independent and identically distributed random variables with $P(Y_i = 1) = \frac{1}{2}$ and $P(Y_i = -1) = \frac{1}{2}$. For each $t$, let
    \begin{equation*}
        X_t = \sum_{i=1}^{t}Y_i, \quad X_0 = 0.
    \end{equation*}
    $X_0$, $X_1$, $X_2$, $X_3$, ... is called \textit{simple random walk}.

