[Lemma lem:smallset of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] Let $\psi$ and $\phi$ be convex functions on $\mathbb{R}^d$. For every $t \in \mathbb{R}$, the set
	\begin{equation}

		\cbr{ 
			x \in \operatorname{dom} \nabla\psi \cap \operatorname{dom} \nabla\phi \mid 
			\psi(x) - \phi(x) = t \text{ and } \nabla\psi(x) \ne \nabla\phi(x)
		}
	\end{equation}
	has Hausdorff dimension at most $d-1$.

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.22438, 'A deterministic scalar reduction for the phase transition in two interacting urns'] The zeros of \(\Phi_p\) in \((1/2,3/4)\) are in one-to-one correspondence with the equilibria in \(\Omega_+\). The correspondence is
\begin{equation*}
 z\mapsto (x,y)=(2z-q_p(z),q_p(z)).
\end{equation*}

