[Prop macroscopic coupling of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] {prevost2023phase}, [CT16]}]

    Let $\delta \in (0,1)$. For every $u>0$, $\rho \in (0,1)$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, there exists a coupling $\widetilde{\mathsf{P}}$ between the random walk under $\mathsf{P}$ and the random interlacements $\mathcal{I}^{u(1\pm\rho)}$ such that
    \begin{equation}

        \widetilde{\mathsf{P}}\Big(\mathcal{I}^{u(1-\rho)} \cap Q_\delta \subset X[0, uN^d] \cap \boldsymbol{Q}_\delta \subset \mathcal{I}^{u(1+\rho)} \cap Q_\delta \Big) \geq \;1-CN^{2d} \lceil uN^{d-2}\rceil \exp\Big(-c\rho\sqrt{uN^{d-2}}\Big)
    \end{equation}
    holds for some constants $c,C \in (0, \infty)$ depending only on $\delta$ and $d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

