[Lemma lem:generalisation of stark lem2.2 of arXiv:2603.10738, 'Pairwise Negative Correlation for Uniform Spanning\\ Subgraphs of the Complete Graph'] Let $p,q$ be two  integers satisfying $1\;\leqslant\; q\;\leqslant\; p$,  and let $\{m_i\}_{i=1}^{p}$  be a sequence of integers with $m_i>0$ for $1\;\leqslant\; i \;\leqslant\; q$ and $m_i=0$ for $q+1\;\leqslant\; i\;\leqslant\; p$, such that $d\coloneq \sum_{i=1}^{q}m_i\;\leqslant\; n$. Suppose $S_i \subseteq V(K_n)$ are mutually disjoint subsets with $\left| S_i \right|=m_i$ for all $1\;\leqslant\; i \;\leqslant\; q$. Let $k_1,\ldots,k_p$ be $p$ integers at least $-1$. Then the number of subgraphs of $K_n$ with $p$ components that satisfy the following three conditions:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item for each $i\in[1,q]$, each vertex in $S_i$ is contained in the same component;
		\item for $i \neq j$, the vertices in $S_i$ and $S_j$ are contained in distinct components;
		\item for each $i\in[1,p]$, the component containing $S_i$ has excess $k_i$;
	\end{itemize}
	is
	\begin{equation}
	\frac{(n-d)!}{(p-q)!}\big[z^{n-d}\big]\prod_{q+1\;\leqslant\; i\;\leqslant\; p}W_{k_i}(z)\prod_{1\;\leqslant\; j\;\leqslant\; q}W_{k_j}^{(m_j)}(z),
	\end{equation}
	where $W_{k_j}^{(m_j)}(z)$ is the $m_j$-th derivative of $W_{k_j}(z)$.

