[Lem element estimates bfM-n-R of arXiv:2608.23156, 'Disc counting statistics of the real Ginibre ensemble'] Suppose that $R\equiv R_N>0$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
    R_N\to r\in(0,\infty]
    \qquad
    \text{as }N\to\infty.
\end{equation}
For $j,k\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$, set
\begin{equation} 
    x:=\frac{2j-1}{NR^2},
    \qquad
    y:=\frac{2k-1}{NR^2}.
\end{equation}
Then, for every fixed $\epsilon\in(0,1)$, as $N\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
    [\mathbf{M}_N(R)]_{j,k}
    =
    \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi}}\,
    \frac{(xy)^{1/4}}{\sqrt{N}R(x+y)} 
    \exp\bigg[
        -\frac{NR^2}{2}
        \Big(
            x\log x
            +
            y\log y
            -
            (x+y)\log\frac{x+y}{2}
        \Big)
        +
        O\Big(
            \frac{1}{j}
            +
            \frac{1}{k}
        \Big)
    \bigg].
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
The error term is uniform over all $j,k\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$
satisfying $ 0<x,y\leq1-\epsilon.$

