[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2607.16502, 'Asymptotic Behavior of Path Functionals for Vector-Valued Gaussian Processes at High Level'] The conditional mean vector
  \begin{equation*}
    \bm{d}_\tau ( t ) 
    = ( I - R ( \tau + t, \tau ) \, \Sigma^{-1} (\tau) ) \, \bb
  \end{equation*}
  admits the following asymptotic formula
  \begin{equation*}
    \bm{d}_\tau (t)
    =
    \Big[ (\tau+t)^\beta - \tau^\beta \Big] \, A \, \bm{w}
    + t^\alpha \, V \bm{w}
    + o ( ( \tau + t )^\beta + \tau^\beta + t^\alpha )
    \quad \text{as} \quad
    \tau, t \to 0^+.
  \end{equation*}

