body:
[Cor 87 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $\alpha>1,\;\kappa\in (1/2,1]$ and set $r_n=n^{\theta},\;\theta\ge 0$.
  For $\zeta,\;\eta\ge 0$ satisfying $\zeta+\eta<\alpha$, we have that
  \begin{align*}
    \bbE[d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu^{(r_n)},\mu_n^{(r_n)})^{\zeta}\mu_n([-r_n,r_n])^{\eta}]
    \lesssim
     \begin{dcases}
    n^{-\zeta(1-\frac{1}{\alpha}-\theta)+\eta\theta}, & \alpha\in (1,2),\\
    n^{-\zeta(\frac{1}{2}-\theta)+\eta\theta}(\log n)^{\zeta/2}, & \alpha=2,\\
    n^{-\zeta(\frac{1}{2}-\theta)+\eta\theta}, & \alpha\in (2,\infty).
    \end{dcases}  
  \end{align*}

