body:
[Prop thm:injection-hbc-cbc of arXiv:2608.26876, 'Local Bousfield classes via homological support'] Let $\cat T$ be a rigidly-compactly generated tensor-triangulated category and let $A \in \cat T$. For each $x\in \LA\cat T$ we have
	\begin{equation}
		\mathinner{\left\langle x \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}= \mathinner{\langle I_A(x) \rangle}^{\mkern-2mu *} \quad\text{in }\LA\cat T.
	\end{equation}
	Consequently, there is an injective map
	\[
		\left\{\begin{array}{c}
		\text{homological Bousfield classes}\\
		\text{of }\LA\cat T
		\end{array}\right\}
		\hookrightarrow
		\left\{\begin{array}{c}
		\text{cohomological Bousfield classes}\\
		\text{of }\LA\cat T
		\end{array}\right\}
	\]
	given by $\mathinner{\left\langle x \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\longmapsto \mathinner{\langle I_A(x) \rangle}^{\mkern-2mu *}.$

