body:
[Lemma lem: relative compactness of projections by test functions of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] For each $\varphi \in C_b(\mathbbm{R}_+^3)$, the sequences
	\begin{equation*}
		\asetc{\bar\boldsymbol{A}^N(\varphi)}{N \geq 1}, \quad \asetc{\bar\boldsymbol{D}^N(\varphi)}{N \geq 1} \quad \text{and} \quad \asetc{\bar\boldsymbol{D}^{N, c}(\varphi)}{N \geq 1}
	\end{equation*}
	are tight in $D_\mathbbm{R}[0, \infty)$. Therefore, the corresponding measure-valued processes are $\mathcal{H}_3$-weakly tight. Also, the sequence $\setc{\langle\phi, \bar\boldsymbol{\mu}^N\rangle}{N \geq 1}$ is tight in $D_\mathbbm{R}[0, \infty)$ for each $\phi \in C_c^1(\mathbbm{R}_+^2)$, and thus the corresponding sequence of measure-valued processes is $\mathcal{H}_2$-weakly tight.

