body:
[Defn of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $M_{\mathord{\scalebox{0.45}{$\square$}}}$ be a manifold with fences and windows.
    \begin{itemize}
        \item A standard neighborhood of the annular fence $\mathcal{A} \subset \partial_{\mathord{\scalebox{0.45}{$\square$}}} M_{\mathord{\scalebox{0.45}{$\square$}}}$ is a neighborhood $N(\mathcal{A})$ of the form $S^1 \times [-1,2]^2 \setminus (S^1 \times (0,1)^2)$ with smooth coordinates $(x, y, z)$. It only intersects $\partial M$ along $\mathcal{A}$.
        \item A standard neighborhood of the boundary square window $\mathcal{W} \subset \partial_* M_{\mathord{\scalebox{0.45}{$\square$}}}$ is a neighborhood $N(\mathcal{W})$ of the form $[-1,2] \times I \times [-1,2]$ with coordinates $(x,y,z)$, in which $\mathcal{W}$ corresponds to $[0,1] \times \{1\} \times [0,1]$. It only intersect $\partial M$ along $[-1,2] \times \{1\} \times [-1,2]$ and is contained in the component of $\partial_*M$ containing $\mathcal{W}$ there.
        \item A standard neighborhood of the boundary toroidal window $\mathcal{W} \subset \partial_* M_{\mathord{\scalebox{0.45}{$\square$}}}$ is a neighborhood $N(\mathcal{W})$ of the form $\mathcal{W} \times [0,1]_y \cong \mathbb{T}_{x,z}^2 \times [0,1]_y$ in which $\mathcal{W}$ corresponds to $\mathcal{W} \times \{1\}$ 
    \end{itemize}

[Lem lem gamma' of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Under the assumption of Theorem (Thm main2 of the paper), For $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_{q,\|u_0\|_\infty} > 0$ such that for $0<\eta<\frac{1}{q}$, the following inequality holds:
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{P}\left( \sup_{t\in [0,T\wedge\tau]}\|u(t)\|_{q}^{q}\geq R\right)\leq \frac{C_{q,\|u_0\|_\infty}}{R^\eta}.
\end{equation*}

[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] There exists $n_{0}$ such that, if $p_{0} \leq \frac{1}{100}$ for some choice of $\ell \geq n_{0}$, then
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{k \geq 0} p_{k} < \infty.
    \end{equation}

