[Proposition 123 (Third-chaos spectral bounds) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] For every $\eps>0$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{\Lambda\ge1}\sup_{t\le T}
  q_{a,\Lambda}^{(3)}(t,\xi)
  \lesssim_{T,\eps}\la\xi\ra^{-3+2\beta_{\Gamma,a}+\eps}.
\end{equation}
For every $0<\theta<\frac12-\betasum$,
\begin{equation}
  q_{a,\Lambda}^{(3),\Delta}(t,t';\xi)
  \lesssim_{T,\eps,\theta}
  |t-t'|^{2\theta}\la\xi\ra^{-3+2\beta_{\Gamma,a}+2\theta+\eps}.
\end{equation}
The cutoff-difference densities tend pointwise to zero and satisfy the weighted
tail condition in \eqref{eq:path-criterion-tail} for every target exponent
$s<-\beta_{\Gamma,a}$.

