body:
[Proposition prop:CFRRZ of arXiv:2604.10214, 'Large deviations for maximum local time of simple random walk in dimensions \texorpdfstrin'] Let
\(
t_y:={\mathbb P}\big(y\in S[0,\infty)\big),\  y\in\mathbb Z^d\setminus\{0\}.
\)
Then $\xi(\infty,0)+\xi(\infty,y)$ has geometric distribution on $\mathbb N^+$ with success probability $\gamma/(1+t_y)$. Namely, for all $u\in\mathbb N$,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb P}\big(\xi(\infty,0)+\xi(\infty,y)>u\big)
=\Big(1-\frac{\gamma}{1+t_y}\Big)^u.
\end{align}
Consequently, there exists $\delta\in(0,1)$ such that for all $u\in\mathbb N$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{y\in \mathbb Z^d\setminus\{0\}}
{\mathbb P}\big(\xi(\infty,0)+\xi(\infty,y)>2u\big)
\le (1-\gamma)^{(1+\delta)u}
={\mathbb P}\big(\xi(\infty,0)>u\big)^{1+\delta}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

