body:
[Proposition 6 (Closing conditions for a nut-type collapse) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] In case (2) of Lemma \ref{lem:bolt-nut-dichotomy}, a smooth closing at $s = 0$ requires:

	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $H$ and $F_1$ extend to smooth \textbf{odd} functions of $s$, and each $F_k$ with $k \geq 2$ extends to a smooth \textbf{even} function with $F_k(0) > 0$;
		\item $H'(0) = 1$ and $F_1'(0) = \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$.
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[The 21 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let \( \phi\in\text{\rm SCL}(\T^n) \) and $H:\T^n\times\R^n\to\R$ be a Tonelli Hamiltonian. Then we have
\begin{align*}
	\reg(\phi,H) = \reg(\phi), \qquad
	\cut(\phi,H) = \cut(\phi).
\end{align*}
In other words,
\begin{align*}
	\reg(\phi,H)=\big\{x\in\T^n:\partial_P \phi(x)\neq\varnothing\big\},\qquad \cut(\phi,H)=\big\{x\in\T^n:\partial_P \phi(x)=\varnothing\big\}.
\end{align*}

