[Definition Def: reduction chain of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For any $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and $\rho\in{\mathcal T} _b$ with $k+1$ leaves we define a \emph{reduction chain} as a collection of $k$ binary trees $(\rho^0,\rho^1,\ldots \rho^k)$ such that 
		\begin{equation*}
			\rho^0=\rho\,,\qquad\rho^i\in{\mathcal R}^-(\rho^{i-1})\,,\qquad i=1,\ldots, k\,,
		\end{equation*}
		see Definition (Def: operations binary trees1 of the paper) for ${\mathcal R}^-$.

