body:
[Thm 12 of arXiv:2608.30380, 'Morita Induction and Geometric Ideals in $\ell^p$ Roe-Type Algebras'] Let $I\triangleleft B$ and set $J=\Ind_B^A(I)$.  With
\[
 X=E_I^{>},\qquad Y={}_I E^{<},
\]
the following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $I^2=I$;
\item $J^2=J$;
\item with the restricted actions and pairings, ${}_IY_J$ and ${}_JX_I$ form a Morita equivalence between $J$ and $I$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:morita}.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, if either $I$ or $J$ has a bounded approximate identity, then $I$ and $J$ are Morita equivalent via the restricted bimodules.

