{"artifact_digest":"sha256:a8a9e67cefcf759a05f22df439a39fa520608386e4f7a424216cd94553d8c581","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/a8/a8a9e67cefcf759a05f22df439a39fa520608386e4f7a424216cd94553d8c581.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:2f929ab83f6cacac5ceff60e7299084b652e69d53d51cd2acaf34749b168ad0e","bundle_entry_key":"2412-08236-theorem-64-precompactness-of-transition-d","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_125","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_125.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2412-08236-prop-64-precompactness-of-transition-d","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Fix $T > 0$ and $r>0$.
  Note that the local Gromov-Hausdorff-vague convergence 
  and $\mu$ being of full support imply that 
  \begin{equation}
    c_{1} 
    \coloneqq
    \inf_{n \geq 1} 
    \inf_{x \in D_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, r)} 
    \mu_{n}(D_{R_{n}}(x, r)) 
    > 0
  \end{equation}
  (cf.\ [Athreya_Lohr_Winter_16_The_gap]).
  By [Kigami_12_Resistance],
  it holds that, for any $t \geq T$ and $x \in D_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, r)$,
  \begin{equation}
    p_{n}(t, x, x) 
    \leq 
    2r t^{-1} + \sqrt{2} \mu_{n}(D_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, r))^{-1} 
    \leq 
    2rT^{-1} + \sqrt{2} c_{1}^{-1}.
