[Thm 12 of arXiv:2609.03268, 'Poincare Polynomials of Heavy-Light Hassett Spaces'] The ordered $r$-Bell numbers $b(n,r)$ defined above satisfies the recurrence 
                $$b(n,r) = r^{n-1}+\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} {n\choose i} r^{i-1}b(n-i,r)$$
                for $n\ge 2$; with the initial condition $b(1,r)=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:thm1a0 of arXiv:2608.18990, 'Proving Lehner's formulas via RDT -- indefinite and asymmetric scenarios'] Assume the setup of Theorem (thm:thm1 of the paper) with $A_0=0$. For $m,n\in{\mathbb N}$ such that $\alpha=\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{m}{n}$, let $G_{i}^{(4)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_1\times m}$ and $G_{i}^{(5)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_2\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be two matrices comprised of independent standard normals. Moreover, let $G_{i}^{(4)}$ and $G_{i}^{(5)}$ be independent of all other randomness. Set
\begin{eqnarray}

 L_{l,Y} & = &  
   \max_{Y\in{\mathbb R}^{m\times k_1}, Y^TY =I} \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(4)} Y F_{i,Y}F_{i,Y}^T \right )   \nonumber \\
    L_{l,X} & = &  
   \max_{X\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k_2}, X^TX =I} \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(5)} X F_{i,X}F_{i,X}^T \right )      .
\end{eqnarray}
Let $\xi_{l,Y}$ and $\xi_{l,X}$ be as in ((eq:hrd0a0a0 of the paper)).  One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_a  
 \geq 
 \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_{l,Y}
+
 \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_{l,X}
