[Definition of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] The (real) \emph{Veronese map} is the map $\nu_\alpha:\mathbb{R}^m\to S(\mathbb{R}_{>0}^A)$ given for every $x\in \mathbb{R}^m$ by:
  \begin{equation}
    \nu_\alpha(x):=\left(\sqrt{\lambda_a(x)}\right)_{a\in A}.
  \end{equation}

