[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2604.07275, 'Some probabilistic properties and time-changed versions of a renewal process based on Mitt'] Consider two independent inverse subordinators  $\{Y_{f_1}(t)\}_{t\ge 0}$ and $\{Y_{f_2}(t)\}_{t\ge 0}$ with associated  Bern\v{s}tein functions $f_1(s)$ and $f_2(s)$, respectively. Then
		\begin{equation}
			Y_{f_1}(Y_{f_2}(t)) \overset{d}{=} Y_{f_1 \circ f_2}(t), \ t \ge 0,
		\end{equation}
		where $(f_1 \circ f_2)(s) = f_1(f_2(s))$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

