[Lemma lem:spatial_triangle of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] If Cases 2 or 3 of (equation HD+ of the paper) hold then
\begin{multline*}
  \sum_{x,y\in \mathbb Z^d} \|x\|_2^2 \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(0\leftrightarrow x) \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(x\leftrightarrow y) \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(y \leftrightarrow z),\\\sum_{x,y\in \mathbb Z^d} \|y-x\|_2^2 \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(0\leftrightarrow x) \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(x\leftrightarrow y) \mathbb P_{\beta_c,r}(y \leftrightarrow z)
   \preceq \begin{cases}
  1 & d > 8\\
  \log r & d=8\\
  r^{\alpha/2} & d=7 \\
  \frac{r^\alpha}{(\log r)^2} & d =6 
  \end{cases}
\end{multline*}
for every $r\geq 2$ and $z\in B_r$.

