[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03958, '2609.03958'] Let $n\geq 2$, $K\geq 0$, $u\in C^4(B_{10})$ and $f\in C^2(B_{10})$ with $D^2u\geq -KI$ and $\inf_{B_{10}}f >0$. If $M=\{(x,u(x)):x\in B_{10}\}\subset\R^{n+1}$ is a smooth 2-convex graph satisfying the scalar curvature equation \eqref{eq:intro-main}, then there exists some constant  $C>0$ depending only on $n$, $K$, $\inf_{B_{10}}f$, $\sup_{B_{10}}f$, $\|Df\|_{L^{\infty}(B_{10})}$ and $\|Du\|_{L^{\infty}(B_{10})}$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \int_{M\cap\{x\in B_{5/4}\}}b(1+H)\,d\mu_g
 \le C.
\end{equation}

