(y+1)e^{-y}-1.
}
Since $e^y>1+y$ for all $y>0$, we obtain $(y+1)e^{-y}<1$. Hence the numerator is strictly negative, so that $f'(x)<0$ for all $x>0$. This proves the monotonicity assertion.

