body:
[Definition eq:master_equation_formal_revised of arXiv:2507.22577, 'A Mean-Field Theory of $\Theta$-Expectations'] The value function $u: [0,T] \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^k) \to \mathbb{R}$ is conjectured to formally solve the terminal-value problem:
\begin{multline} 
    \partial_t u(t,\mu) - \mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim\mu}\left[ \scpr{ G\big(t, \tilde{y}, \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}), \mu\big) }{ \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}) } \right] \\
    + \frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim\mu}\left[ \mathrm{Tr}\left( \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}) \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y})^T D_y\big(\partial_\mu u(t, \mu, \tilde{y})\big) \right) \right] = 0,
\end{multline}
for $(t,\mu) \in [0,T) \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^k)$, with the terminal condition $u(T,\mu) = \int_{\mathbb{R}^k} \xi(y) \mathrm{d}\mu(y)$. The driver $G$ is given by $G(t,y,z,\mu) = \sup_{a \in \mathcal{U}_{g(\mu)}} F(t,y,z,a,\mu)$.

