[Theorem thetaseriesfneq of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] \(\vartheta_{\Delta}(x)\) defined as in (equation eq:theta of the paper) for \(\Delta = Dl^2\) satisfies the functional equation given by
\begin{equation}
    \vartheta_{Dl^2}(x) = \frac{1}{(|D|l^2x)^{\delta_D+1/2}} \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} v_{n,l} \: \chi_D\left(\frac{n}{v_{n,l}^2}\right) \: n^{\delta_D} e^{-\frac{\pi n^2}{D^2l^4x}} 
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation*}
    v_{n,l} = \begin{cases}
        0 \qquad & \text{there does not exist any \(v\) such that }\left(\frac{l}{v},\frac{n}{v^2} \right) =1 \\
        v_{n,l} & \text{ unique \(v_{n,l}\) such that } \left(\frac{l}{v},\frac{n}{v^2} \right) =1 
    \end{cases}
\end{equation*}

