[Definition def:linearized-amp-matrix of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Let $V=\sqrt{B}\in\RR^{L\times L}$ denote the symmetric square root of
    $B$. We define the linearized AMP matrix as
    \begin{equation}
        H = (V \otimes I_n) \Diag\rbr{\sqrt{\frac{\lambda_1}{n}} A^{(1)} - \lambda_1 I_n,\ldots,\sqrt{\frac{\lambda_L}{n}} A^{(L)} - \lambda_L I_n} (V \otimes I_n) \in \RR^{Ln \times Ln}.
    \end{equation}

[Theorem 27 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let $\alpha>-1$, $\beta>0$ and $\mu$ be a positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$. Then $\mathcal C_{\mu,\beta}^{\xi}: A_{\alpha}^1(\mathbb{B}_n)\to H^{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_n)$ is bounded if and only if $\mu$ is a $(\beta+n+1+\alpha)$-Carleson measure on $[0,1)$, that is
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{r\in [0,1)}\frac{\hat{\mu}(r)}{(1-r)^{\beta+n+1+\alpha}}<\infty.
\end{equation}

