[Theorem thm:1.10 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] In the limit when $q$ approaches 1 whilst $k$ is fixed,
\begin{align}
P_k(q) \sim \frac{\lambda_q^k}{k!}\, P_0(q), \quad \lambda_q= \frac{\log (1-q)}{\log q },
\end{align}
and, moreover, for every $t>0$ and $k\ge 1$
 \begin{align}
\lim_{q\to 1^{-}} \frac{P_{k}(t;q)}{P_{k-1}(q) } =
 e^{t}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathcal{L}$ be the generator of Feller process $\Phi$. If there exists a function $V:\X\to\R_+$ with  $\lim\limits_{\rho(x,x_0)\to\infty}V(x)=\infty$ for some $x_0\in\X$ and
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathcal{L}V(x)\le-\varphi(V(x))+C,
    \end{equation*}
    where $\varphi\in C^1(\R_+)$ is an  increasing nonnegative concave function, $C\ge0$. Then $$ \sup_{t\ge0}\E \varphi(V(\Phi_t))< \infty.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

