[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] For any $m,k \geq 0$, there exists $C = C(m,k,S,t_1,t_2) > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\big\| \hat{h}_j \big\|_{C^{m,k}([0,S]\times[t_1,t_2])} + \big\| \hat{f}_{i_0, j}^2 \big\|_{C^{m,k}([0,S]\times[t_1,t_2])} + \big\| \hat{f}_{1, j}^2 \big\|_{C^{m,k}([0,S]\times[t_1,t_2])} \;\leq\; C.
\end{equation}

