[Lemma lem:Tlowerbdd of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For any $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3$ and $t\geq 0$, we have \begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}\left(T_n^{\varepsilon,x}\leq t\right)\leq \mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{i=1}^n \tilde{\sigma}_i^{\varepsilon,0}\leq t\right),
\end{align*}
where $\left\{\tilde{\sigma}_n^{\varepsilon,0}\right\}_{n\geq 1} $ is an i.i.d.~random variable with the distribution $\mathbb{P}\left(\tilde{\sigma}_1^{\varepsilon,0}\geq 0\right)=\frac{H(t+\varepsilon^2,0)}{H(\varepsilon^2,0)}$.

