[Lemma lem: disconnected three of arXiv:2603.10738, 'Pairwise Negative Correlation for Uniform Spanning\\ Subgraphs of the Complete Graph'] Recall that $x_n=\big(\frac{1}{2}\big)^{n-1}$, and let  $e,f$ be two non-adjacent edges  of $K_n$ (i.e., they share no common vertex). Then we have the following estimate:  
	\begin{equation}
	{\ensuremath{\mathbb P}} _{1/2}\big[ \omega \notin {\ensuremath{\mathscr C}}  \mid \omega(e)=\omega(f)=1\big] 
	=(n-4)x_n+8x_n^2+o(1)x_n^2
	\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:gs-upper of arXiv:2608.09465, 'Balancing fractional Brownian motion'] Let $H\in(0,1)$ and let $f_1,\ldots,f_n$ be independent fBm sample paths with Hurst exponent $H$. There is a randomized polynomial-time algorithm in the finite retained-coefficient real-arithmetic input model which returns $\sigma\in\{\pm1\}^n$ such that, with probability $1-o(1)$ over the sample paths and the internal randomness of the algorithm,
\begin{equation}
\left\|\sum_{i=1}^n\sigma_i f_i\right\|_\infty
\lesssim_H
\begin{cases}
n^{1/2-H}\sqrt{\log n},&0<H<1/2,\\
(\log n)^{3/2},&H=1/2,\\
\sqrt{\log n},&1/2<H<1.
\end{cases}

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:unlabelled_Pol of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Expanding the non-linearity in (equation eq:Pol_nonlinearity of the paper) evaluated on (equation eq:defFmu_1 of the paper) gives

\begin{equs}
{}&\text{$\mathrm{D}$}A_{{\eps,\mu}}\big[v,\dot G_\mu A_{{\eps,\mu}}[v] \big](t)\\
&=
\sum_{\tau \in \text{\scriptsize{$\mathfrak{T}$}}}
\int_{\R^{\text{\tiny{$\mathfrak{s}$}}(\tau)}}
\Big\langle \sum_{\tau_1, \tau_2 \in \text{\scriptsize{$\mathfrak{T}$}}} 
\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}_{\eps,\mu}\graft^\mu \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}_{\eps,\mu} \big)^\tau  (t,s^{\tau}),\Upsilon^{\tau}[v+{\tt u}](s^{\tau}) \Big\rangle_{\mathcal{H}^{\tau}} \mathrm{d} s^{\tau}\,.
