[Thm 30 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] \cite[Freedman, Theorem 1.6]{freedman}
If $|Y_{n+1} - Y_n| \le 1$ for all $n$, then for any $a, b>0$,
$$\mathbb P\left(\exists n: Y_n \ge a \text{ and } \sum_{j=1}^n V_j \le b\right) \le \exp\left(-{a^2 \over 2(a+b)}\right).$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 44 of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] Let us define the deduction rules of $\RS_H$ as follows:
    \begin{center}
    \vspace{1em}
    \begin{mathprooftree}
        \def\fCenter#1#2{\sststile{#1}{#2}}
        \AxiomC{}
        \RightLabel{$(\mathrm{Ax}) \quad (x\in y\in u)$}
        \UnaryInfC{$H[\ttX]\fCenter{\rho}{\alpha} \Gamma,\ x\in y$}
    \end{mathprooftree}
    \hspace{3em}
    \begin{mathprooftree}
        \def\fCenter#1#2{\sststile{#1}{#2}}
        \AxiomC{}
        \RightLabel{$(\mathrm{Ax}) \quad (x\notin y\in u,\ y\in u)$}
