[Lemma L:Second-der-X-W1-W2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the process $D_{r_1,r_2}^{W_1 W_2} X_t^\varepsilon$ be the solution of equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W1-W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2$, there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
\begin{multline*}
\mathbb{E} \left[\left|D_{r_1,r_2}^{W_1 W_2} X_t^\varepsilon\right|^{2p} \right] \le K \left[\frac{\varepsilon^p}{\eta^p} + \varepsilon^p \eta^p \right] e^{- (2p)\alpha (t-r_1 \vee r_2)} e^{- (2p)\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r_1 - r_2)}\mathds{1}_{(r_1 \ge r_2)} \\
 + K  \left[ \varepsilon^p \eta^p + {\varepsilon^{2p}} \right] e^{-(2p) \alpha (t - r_1 \wedge r_2)}.
\end{multline*}

