body:
[Proposition prop:Random normal is non-almost-constant of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $\delta, \rho \in \left(0, \frac{1}{12}\right)$. Assume that $n$ is sufficiently large.
\begin{align*}
\textbf{P}(\exists v \in\operatorname{Cons}(\delta,\rho) \text{ and } v\bot H_n)\le\textbf{P}(\inf_{v\in\operatorname{Cons}(\delta,\rho)}\|M_n'v\|_2\le\frac{\sqrt{n}}{16})\le e^{-c_5n},
\end{align*}
where the $(n-1)\times n$ random matrix $M_n'$ is composed of the first $n-1$ rows of the random matrix $M_n$, i.e., the submatrix of $M_n$ obtained by removing the last row.

