\]

[Theorem eq:time-reversed-detailed of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] Let $p(s,x;t,y)$ denote the transition density of the forward process. If:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The coefficients $b_i$ and $\sigma_{ij}$ are bounded and Lipschitz continuous
\item The diffusion matrix $a_{ij} = \sum_k \sigma_{ik}\sigma_{jk}$ is uniformly elliptic
\item The transition density satisfies $\int p(0,x;t_*,y)\mu_0(dx) = \mu_{t_*}(dy)$
\end{enumerate}
Then the time-reversed process $\tilde{X}_i(s) = X_i(t_* - s)$ satisfies:
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{d} \tilde{X}_i(s) = \tilde{b}_i(s,\tilde{\mathbf{X}}(s))\mathrm{d} s + \sum_{j=1}^K \sigma_{ij}(t_*-s,\tilde{\mathbf{X}}(s))\mathrm{d} \tilde{B}_j(s)
\end{equation}
where $\tilde{B}_j$ are independent Brownian motions and
\begin{equation}
\tilde{b}_i(s,x) = -b_i(t_*-s,x) + \sum_{j=1}^K \sum_{k=1}^K \frac{\partial}{\partial x_k}[a_{ij}(t_*-s,x)] + 2\sum_{j=1}^K a_{ij}(t_*-s,x)\frac{\partial \log \rho_{t_*-s}}{\partial x_j}(x)
\end{equation}
with $\rho_t$ the marginal density at time $t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ be as defined in Corollary~\ref{cor-1.3}. Then for all $n\ge1$,
\begin{equation}

\bigl(\ell_{\tau_\varrho}(x_0),\dots,\ell_{\tau_\varrho}(x_n)\bigr)\text{\rm\ under }P^\zero
\,\,\,\laweq\,\,(T_0,\dots,T_n).
\end{equation}
In addition,
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k \to \infty} \inf_{n \ge k}\,P\biggl(\,\bigcap_{j=k}^n\bigl\{T_j\le\alpha j\log(j)\bigr\}\biggr)=1
\end{equation}
holds true for each~$\alpha>1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

