body:
[Definition def:production of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] Let $f:\mathbb R_{++}^n\to\mathbb R_{++}$ be $C^2$. We call $f$ a \emph{weighted-homogeneous production function} here if $f_i>0$ for all $i$ and
\begin{equation}
f(D_tx)=t^qf(x),\qquad q>0,
\end{equation}
for a positive diagonal dilation family. For $c>0$, the level set $M_c=f^{-1}(c)$ is called the \emph{isoquant} at output $c$; compare [VilcuVilcu2019,NeacsuEtAl2024,Lloyd2012]. Its nonemptiness and regularity are consequences recorded in Lemma~(lem:isoquanttransport of the paper).

[Proposition 12 (Geometric meaning of the quadrisecant sign) of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] \begin{multline*}
\sgn\Delta_4(\alpha_1,\alpha_2,\alpha_3,\alpha_4)=\\
or(\alpha_{12\underline{3}},\alpha_{12\underline{4}})\cdot or(\alpha_1,\alpha_2)\cdot\sgn[(z_1-z_3)(z_2-z_3)(z_1-z_4)(z_2-z_4)].
\end{multline*}

