[Lemma 12 (Selected residual mean) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] For every full-column-rank $X$, $m>d$, and $d\le s\le m$,
\begin{equation}
  \E_XL_S=\beta\lossstar.

\end{equation}
This identity does not require $\lossstar>0$.

[Theorem 4 (Combined mode evidence) of arXiv:2609.01043, 'From Truncation to Commitment:\\ Persistent Context in Uniform Discrete Diffusion'] Let $w[A,u]$ be the posterior mode law after observing $X\in A$ and
$U_{1:H}=u_{1:H}$. Then
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1-w_{m^\star}[A,u]}{w_{m^\star}[A,u]}
 \le
 \frac{1-w_{m^\star}}{w_{m^\star}}
 e^{-(S(A)+T(u_{1:H}))}.

\end{equation}
With
\begin{equation}
 a:=\frac{1-w_{m^\star}}{w_{m^\star}},
 \qquad
 \varepsilon(S,T):=\frac{ae^{-(S+T)}}{1+ae^{-(S+T)}},
 \qquad
 \bar\varepsilon:=\min\{\varepsilon(S(A),T(u_{1:H})),1-1/K\},

\end{equation}
we have
$1-w_{m^\star}[A,u]\le\varepsilon(S(A),T(u_{1:H}))$ and
\begin{equation}
 \Ent(w[A,u])
 \le h_2(\bar\varepsilon)+\bar\varepsilon\log(K-1).

\end{equation}
If $Q_{\mathrm{mix}}^{w[A,u]}$ is the mixture of the product laws of $Y$ under
$w[A,u]$ and $Q_{\mathrm{prod}}^{w[A,u]}$ is the product of its coordinate
marginals, then
\begin{equation}
 \KL(Q_{\mathrm{mix}}^{w[A,u]}\kldiv Q_{\mathrm{prod}}^{w[A,u]})
 \le(n-1)
 \left[h_2(\bar\varepsilon)+\bar\varepsilon\log(K-1)\right].

\end{equation}

