[Lemma 8 (Poisson local expansion) of arXiv:2608.24552, 'Asymptotic Rounding Laws for Optimal Thresholds in Secretary Problems'] Let \(\ell=1/\e\). Uniformly for bounded \(u\) such that
\(\ell\lambda+u\) is an integer threshold,
\begin{equation}
D_\lambda(\ell\lambda+u)
=
-\frac1\ell
\left(
u-c_{\mathrm P}
\right)
+
o(1)
\qquad
(\lambda\to\infty),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
c_{\mathrm P}
=
\frac12-\frac2{\e}
\in(-1,0).
\end{equation}

[Lm Concentration for specific functionals of theta of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] There is a $C=C(T,k)>0$ such that on a set $A_k$ with $\mathbb{P}(A_k)>1-C'(T,k)n^{-2}$, the following holds. 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item For any deterministic unit vector $v \in V_{k}:=\mathrm{Span}(\{e_j\}_{j=1}^k)$ and $x(t) \in \{\theta_j(t)\}_{j\leq k} \cup\{M(t)^{j_1}e_{j_2+2}\}_{0 \leq j_1 \leq k, 0 \leq j_2 \leq k-1}$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]} |\langle x(t),v \rangle| \leq \frac{C\log(n)}{\sqrt{n}}.

    \end{equation}
    \item For $j, \ell =0,1,\dots,k$,
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]} |\theta_j(t)^T\theta_{\ell}(t)-\delta_{j,\ell}| \leq \frac{C\log(n)}{\sqrt{n}}.

    \end{equation}
    \item 
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]} \max(\|M(t)\|_{op},\|\tilde{M}(t)\|_{op}) \leq C\log(n).
    \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

