[Lemma lem:fluid of arXiv:2607.12061, 'Models for species evolution with random deaths'] Suppose $f > f^\dagger_c$. If $\mathbf{X}^n(0) \to (m_0,\ell_0)^\top$, where $m_0 \geq \ell_0>0$, then for every $\delta,t>0$ 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\ \mathbb{P}\!\left\{\ \sup_{0\le s\le t}\ \|\mathbf{X}^n(s)-\mathbf{x}(s)\|>\delta\ \right\}=0,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{x}(s) = \begin{bmatrix}
m_0 + (p-q)s \\[+1mm]
\ell_0 \left( \frac{m_0}{m_0 + (p-q)s} \right)^{\alpha} + \left(\frac{f-f^\dagger_c}{1-f^\dagger_c}\right) \left( m_0 + (p-q)s - \frac{m_0^{\alpha +1}}{(m_0 + (p-q)s)^{\alpha}} \right)
\end{bmatrix}
\end{equation}
and $\alpha=\frac{q(1-r)}{p-q}$.

