[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] If $-\alpha<u<0$ and $v>u$ then,   as $N\to\infty$, we have
 \begin{equation}

     \GG_N(\alpha,u,v)\sim \Gamma(\alpha-u)^{N}\Gamma(\alpha+u)^N \tfrac{\Gamma(\alpha+v)}{\Gamma(\alpha-u)}\EE[R^{-u-v}],
 \end{equation}
 where $R$ is  given by \eqref{Rseries}.

If $-\alpha<v<0$ and $u>v$, then, as $N\to\infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
  \GG_N(\alpha,u,v)\sim
  \Gamma(\alpha+v)^N\Gamma(\alpha-v)^N
  \tfrac{\Gamma(\alpha+u)}{\Gamma(\alpha-v)}
  \EE[(R')^{-u-v}],
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  R'  =1+\zeta_1'+\zeta_1'\zeta_2'
  +\ldots+\zeta_1'\dots\zeta_n'+\dots,
\end{equation}
and $(\zeta_i')_{i\ge1}$ are i.i.d.\ $\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha+v,\alpha-v)$ random variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma strict-hessian-interior of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Let $\sigma\ge1$ and let $\chi_\ast\in(-1,0)^L$ be a local minimizer of $\cR(\cdot,\sigma)$. If
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\partial\cR}{\partial\chi}(\chi_\ast,\sigma)=0,
    \end{equation}
    then
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\partial^2\cR}{\rbr{\partial \chi}^2}(\chi_\ast,\sigma)\succ0.
    \end{equation}

