[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] For complex $x$ with sufficiently large absolute value, the function $\Sigma(x)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
x=\frac{\Sigma(x)}{\Sigma(x)-1}\exp \left(-\frac{\gamma}{\beta+\Sigma(x)}\right).
\end{equation}

