[Proposition prop: dth Ar power of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ be a finite set and let $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{>0}^A$. For every admissible random field $\mathcal{X}\randin C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^m,\mathbb{R}^{m-1})$ independent of $\mathcal{E}_\alpha$, every positive integer $d$ and every $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$, we have 
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\# \sol{ \left( \mathcal{E}_\alpha\right)^{\odot d},\mathcal{X}; U}=\sqrt{d}\,\mathbb{E} \# \mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}_\alpha,\mathcal{X}; U\right\}
  \end{equation}

