[Definition 3 (Partition-constrained compression) of arXiv:2604.10820, 'A Strict Gap Between Relaxed and Partition-Constrained\\ Spectral Compression in a Six-Sta'] Let $\mathcal A=\{A_1,A_2,A_3\}$ be an unordered partition of the six-state space into three nonempty cells. Choose any ordering of the three cells and define
\begin{equation*}
h_\alpha:=\frac{\mathbf 1_{A_\alpha}}{\sqrt{|A_\alpha|}},
\qquad
H_{\mathcal A}:=[h_1,h_2,h_3],
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
Q_{\mathcal A}(T):=H_{\mathcal A}^*TH_{\mathcal A}.
\end{equation*}
If a different ordering is chosen, then $Q_{\mathcal A}(T)$ is conjugated by a $3\times 3$ permutation matrix, so its determinant is unchanged. Hence $\det Q_{\mathcal A}(T)$ depends only on the underlying unordered partition.

[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.04012, 'Hölder regularity for backward stochastic Volterra integral equations and applications to '] Let $0\leq r\leq s\leq v\leq T$, and define $\delta_j(r,s)\coloneqq |[r,s]\cap[t_j,t_{j+1})|$, where $|\cdot|$ denotes Lebesgue measure. Then there exists a constant $C>0$, independent of $\pi$, $r$, $s$ and $v$, such that, for every $0 \leq k \leq N-1$,
    \begin{flalign}
      \mathbb{E}_r \Big[ \big| U^\pi(s,v)_{k,k} - U^\pi(r,v)_{k,k} \big|^2 \Big]
      \leq C |s-r|.  
    \end{flalign}
    Moreover, for every $0\leq k<j\leq N-1$,
    \begin{flalign}
      \mathbb{E}_r \Big[ \big| U^\pi(s,v)_{k,j} - U^\pi(r,v)_{k,j} \big|^2 \Big]
      \leq C\Big( \Delta_j^2 |s-r| + \delta_j(r,s)^2 \Big).
    \end{flalign} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

