[Proposition 12 (Quadratic-moment estimate from score control) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There is $C_{\gamma,Q}<\infty$ such that every $\psi\in C_c^\infty(\C\setminus\{y_j\})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\C}|x|^2|\psi|^2\,\D x
 \le C_{\gamma,Q}\left(
 \int_{\C}|\nabla\psi|^2+\int_{\C}|F|^2|\psi|^2+\int_{\C}|\psi|^2\right).
\end{equation}

