[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] For any $\gamma \in \ov\Gamma(\mu,\nu)$ and $\gamma_i =(\pi_i,\ov\zeta)\# \gamma$, there holds the equality,
	\begin{equation*}
		Z_2(\mu,\nu) = \int_X \frac{1}{2} W_2^2(\gamma_x,\gamma^1_x) \,\mu(dx) + \int_Y\frac{1}{2} W_2^2(\gamma_y,\gamma^2_y) \,\nu(dy).
	\end{equation*}

