By the admissibility of $\ov{u}$ in the Zolotarev problem \eqref{eq:Z2_again} we have  $\mathrm{lip}(\nabla \ov{u}) \leq 1$. Then, from \eqref{eq:u_adm_char} we deduce that the map $\frac{\abs{\argu}^2}{2}  - \ov{u}$ is convex. Therefore, $T_x$ is a cyclically monotone map for every $x$. Since it is also continuous (even 1-Lipschitz), Brenier theorem \cite{brenier1991} states ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:4528ced47c5851149b1f758634dab68c5d39e7c219e65a41d172d43d107afe60","revision_digest":"sha256:3eb9453799d6238473f9f63b2f21aaefda8fffa0cf3041f9f3751f2ed532b6cc","source_id":"arxiv:2510.27451","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

