[Thm Theorem 8.1 of arXiv:2609.03411, 'Adjacent vertex distinguishing total chromatic number of graph products'] {\em Let $G_1$ and $G_2$ be graphs of order $m$ and $n$ respectively such that
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $m>n+1$,
        \item $\Delta(G_2)\geq\Delta(G_1)$, and
        \item $G_2$ is a total colorable graph.
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, $G=G_1\blacktriangledown G_2$ satisfies the AVDTCC.    
    }

[Lemma exponential_bound_Nt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $S \subset V$ be a finite set containing the origin. For $x \in S$ define $D_x := d_{\vec{G}}(x, S^c).$ We have that for any $t > 0$ and $x\in S:$
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E_x\left[ N(t) \, \big\vert \, \tau_{S^c} \le t \right] \leq \Delta^{D_x} (t + D_x) \, .
\end{equation}

