[Theorem 13 (Courant--Fischer \cite{MR1547416, MR1544417}) of arXiv:2609.02837, '2609.02837'] Let $A \in \h_n$. For any subspace $\V \subset \C^n$ of dimension $k$, 
\begin{equation*}
\lambda_k(A) 
\geq \min_{\substack{\vec{x} \in \V \\ \|\vec{x}\|=1}}  
\langle A \vec{x},\vec{x} \rangle.
\end{equation*}
Moreover, there is a subspace $\V_0 \subset \C^n$ of dimension $k$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\lambda_k(A) = \min_{\substack{\vec{x} \in V_0 \\ \|\vec{x}\|=1}} \langle A \vec{x},\vec{x} \rangle.
\end{equation*}

