[Prop 21 of arXiv:2609.01932, 'Essential dimension and faithful rank of finite $p$-gerbes'] If $\mu_p\subset k$ and $\band$ has $p$-primary descent, then
\begin{equation}
\rdim(\cG)=
\min_{\mathcal B\text{ basis of }\fC^*}
\sum_{\chi\in\mathcal B}m_\chi(\cG).
\end{equation}

[Proposition 24 (Rigidity under the principal orthogonal response laws) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Every orthogonally natural quadratic coefficient architecture is unique.  For
every finite-dimensional real Hilbert space $E$,
\begin{equation}
 \kappa_A^E(K)=\|K\|_{\mathcal S_2},\qquad
 \kappa_Q^E(S)=\|S\|_{\rm op}.
\end{equation}
Consequently its dual response gauges on finite-rank state coordinates are
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\kappa_A(K)\le1}|\operatorname{Tr}(K^*a)|=\|a\|_2,
 \qquad
 \sup_{\kappa_Q(S)\le1}|\operatorname{Tr}(Sq)|=\|q\|_1.
\end{equation}
For a separable Hilbert space $H$, compatible finite-dimensional exhaustion
therefore produces the principal response completion
\begin{equation}
 H\times\mathcal S_2(H)_{\rm sk}\times\mathcal S_1(H)_{\rm sa}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:hamilton_heatkernel of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let $(M,\mathfrak{g})$ be a compact smooth Riemannian manifold. Then there is a constant $C$ depending on the Ricci curvature and on the dimension of $M$ only such that 
\begin{equation}
t^2|\nabla_M\log \mathrm{p}_t(x,\cdot)(y)|^2 \leq 
C(1+\kappa^- t)(1+t), \qquad \forall x,y \in M,\, \forall t > 0\,,
\end{equation}
where $\kappa \in \mathbb{R}$ is a lower bound for the Ricci curvature. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem lem-boltzmann-ldp-lower of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] With probability tending to one as $A\to\infty$, uniformly in the choice of $r$, 
\begin{equation}   
 \operatorname{LDP}_{\widehat M(r)} \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(  x_0 , x_{r} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright)  \geq A^{-1}  r^{3/2} .
\end{equation}

