[Theorem 7 (\cite{zhu2016a}, \cite{zhu2016b}) of arXiv:2605.09459, 'Multipoint connectivity in the branching interlacement process'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$. There exist positive constants $c_1, c_2$, such that for any nonempty $K \subset \mathbb{Z}^d$ and any $x \in \mathbb{Z}^d$, with $\mathrm{d}(x,K) \geq \varepsilon \cdot \mathrm{diam}(K)$, one has,
  \begin{equation}

    c_1\frac{\mathrm{BCap}(K)}{\mathrm{d}(x,K)^{d-4}} \leq \P(\mathcal{T}_-^x \cap K \neq \emptyset) \leq c_2\frac{\mathrm{BCap}(K)}{\mathrm{d}(x,K)^{d-4}}.
  \end{equation}
  \begin{equation}

    c_1\frac{\mathrm{BCap}(K)}{\mathrm{d}(x,K)^{d-2}} \leq \P(\mathcal{T}_c^x \cap K \neq \emptyset) \leq c_2\frac{\mathrm{BCap}(K)}{\mathrm{d}(x,K)^{d-2}}.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

