[Thm 4 ({\hspace{1pt}\cite[Corollary~1.4) of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] {DumPan24Perco}}] Let $d>6$. There exist $L_0\geq 1$ such that the following holds. For every $L\geq L_0$, there exist $c_1,C_1>0$ such that, and for every $p\leq p_c$,
	\begin{equation}
		c_1(p_c-p)^{-1}\leq \chi(p)\leq C_1(p_c-p)^{-1},
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		c_1(p_c-p)^{-1/2}\leq L(p)\leq C_1(p_c-p)^{-1/2}.
	\end{equation}
	Moreover, for every $n\geq 0$,
	\begin{equation}
		\varphi_p(\mathbb H_n)\leq C_1\exp\left(-c_1(p_c-p)^{1/2}n\right).
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

