[Corollary cor: almost_constant_fraction_good_vertex of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \geq 2$, $\lambda > 0$, $\alpha > 0$, and $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$. Then, there exists positive constants $C_1 = C_1(K, \alpha, d, \lambda)$ and $C_2 = C_2(d)$ such that for any $r \ge R_0$,
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb P \left( \, \left| \mathrm{Good}_{H(r)}^{\lambda, \ell(r)} \right| < \frac{r^d}{C_1 \log r} \, \right) \le C_2 \, r^{-d},
\end{align*}
where \( \ell(r) \) is defined in (equation def: s(r) of the paper) and \( R_0 \) is the same constant as in Proposition~(prop: BernPerc_internal_1 of the paper).

