[Theorem thm:thm1 of arXiv:2608.18990, 'Proving Lehner's formulas via RDT -- indefinite and asymmetric scenarios'] Let $k_1,k_2,l\in{\mathbb N}$ be fixed and let $n,m\in{\mathbb N}$ be large such that $\alpha=\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{m}{n}$ remains constant. let $G_{i}\in{\mathbb R}^{m\times n}$, $G_{i}^{(1)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_1\times m}$, and $G_{i}^{(2)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_2\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be independent  standard normal matrices. For deterministic $A_i\in{\mathbb R}^{k_1\times k_2}$  and fixed $R_X\in{\mathbb R}^{k_2\times k_2}$ and $R_Y\in{\mathbb R}^{k_1\times k_1}$ such that $\mbox{Tr}(R_X^TR_X)=\mbox{Tr}(R_Y^TR_Y)=1$, let $F_{i}$, $F_{i,X}$, and $F_{i,Y}$  be as in 
((eq:inteq1ab0b0 of the paper)) and ((eq:inteq1ab0b0a0 of the paper)). Set $\varphi = \sqrt{n} \mbox{Tr}(A_0^TR_Y^T Y^TX  R_X) $ and 
\begin{equation}

 L_a  =   
\max_{X^TX=Y^TY=I} 
 \left ( \varphi +
 \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} 
 \sum_{i=1}^{l} \left (  \mbox{Tr}(Y^T G_i^{(1)} Y F_{i,Y} F_{i,Y}^T ) +\mbox{Tr}(X^T G_i^{(2)} X F_{i,X} F_{i,X}^T ) \right ) 
  \right ).
\end{equation}
Let $\xi_a$ be defined through ((eq:inteq1ab0 of the paper)), ((eq:inteq1ab0b0 of the paper)), and  ((eq:kronrep6 of the paper)).  One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_a   \geq  \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} L_a,
\end{eqnarray}
with the righthand side being the (complementary) random dual.

