[Lem element estimates bfE-n-R-1 of arXiv:2608.23156, 'Disc counting statistics of the real Ginibre ensemble'] Under the assumptions of
Lemma~(lem: element estimates bfM-n-R of the paper), as $N\to\infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
    \big|[\mathbf{E}_{N,1}(R)]_{j,k}\big|
     \leq
    \frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi N}R}
    \Big(\frac{k}{j}\Big)^{1/4}
    \exp\bigg[
        -\frac{NR^2}{2}
        \bigl(y\log y-y+1\bigr)
        +
        O\Big(
            \frac{1}{j}
            +
            \frac{1}{k}
        \Big)
    \bigg],
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
where $y$ is given by (equation def of x and y of the paper).  
The error term is uniform for all
$j,k\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$.

