[Cor eq:right-derived-rep of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ be a locally fibrant simplicial model category, and let $G\colon\textbf{\textup{C}}\to\textbf{\textup{SSet}}$ be a functor that is corepresented (in the enriched sense) by a cofibrant $X\in\textbf{\textup{C}}$. Then $G$ is right Quillen and
    \begin{equation}
        \textbf{\textup{C}}[{\mathcal{W}}^{-1}]\xrightarrow{\;\textbf{\textup{R}}G\;}\textbf{\textup{SSet}}[{\mathcal{W}}_\textup{Quillen}^{-1}]\simeq\Spc
    \end{equation}
    is corepresented (in the $\infty$-categorical sense) by the same $X$; here the unlabelled equivalence in $(\textup{(eq:right-derived-rep of the paper)})$ is the unique one.
    \begin{proof}
        As the mapping space functor for $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ is a right Quillen bifunctor, $G$ is indeed right Quillen. It then suffices to show that the two functors $\textbf{\textup{C}}[{\mathcal{W}}^{-1}]$ agree after restriction to the full subcategory of $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ spanned by the cofibrant-fibrant objects, where this follows by the same argument as in the previous lemma.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2608.30551, 'Critical Discrete Hardy Inequalities in $L^p$'] Let \(p\in(1,\infty)\), let \(k\) be uniformly summable, and let
\(w\in\ell^\infty(X)\) be real-valued. Then the following statements are
equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For every \(u\in\ell^p(X)\),
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal E_p^{X,k}(u)
    \geq
    \sum_{x\in X} w(x)|u(x)|^p.
\end{equation}
\item The semigroup \((P_t^{k,w})_{t\geq0}\) is contractive on
\(\ell^p(X)\).
\end{enumerate}

