[Lem CM mom UB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For any $r \in (0, e^{-1} \wedge r_*)$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$, and $t \in (0, \infty)$,
  \begin{equation}
    \sup_{\bm{x} \in M^k} \sup_{y \in M}
    \hat{E}_{\bm{x}}\!\left[\Pi_t(B(y, r))^n\right]
    \leq 
    \begin{cases}
      n!\, \bigl( \tilde{c}(t)\, r^{d_{\mathrm{cp}}} \bigr)^n,& \text{if}\quad \hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}} > 2,\\
      n!\, \bigl( \tilde{c}(t)\, r^{d_{\mathrm{f}}} \log(1/r) \bigr)^n,& \text{if}\quad \hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}} = 2.
    \end{cases}
  \end{equation}

[Definition DO noise def of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] Let $H\in (0,1)$. The Dobri\'c-Ojeda noise is a centered Gaussian noise with covariance function given by 
\begin{align*}
        E[\dot{W}(s,x)\dot{W}(t,y)] = s^{H-1/2}t^{H-1/2}\delta_0(t-s)f(x-y),
\end{align*} 
where $t,s > 0$, $x,y \in {\mathbb R}^d$. More rigorously, the Dobri\'c-Ojeda noise is defined similarly as $W_0$, but where the inner product $\langle \cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}$ is replaced by
\begin{equation} 
 \langle \varphi , \psi \rangle_{\mathcal{H}}:=
\int_{[0,\infty)} \int_{{\mathbb R}^{2d}}
\varphi(s,y)\psi(s,z) s^{2H-1} f(y-z) \, dy dz ds.   
\end{equation}

