[Corollary cor:frontier-ledger of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] Writing $\Delta_{\rm rev}=V_B(\mathscr G)-V_B(\mathscr H)$,
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
V_P(\hat\pi_A)-V_R(\hat\pi_F)
=
\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A+R_F-R_A.
}

\end{equation}
If resources $K_A,K_F$ are priced by $\lambda$, then net value satisfies
\begin{equation}
N_A-N_F
=
\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A+R_F-R_A
+\lambda^\top(K_F-K_A).
\end{equation}
At equal resource cost, a sufficient condition for active victory is $\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A>R_A-R_F$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

