body:
[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2604.07275, 'Some probabilistic properties and time-changed versions of a renewal process based on Mitt'] The state probabilities $\bar{p}_\alpha(m,t)
		= {\Pr}\{\hat{Z}_\alpha(t) = m \}$ satisfies the following system of differential equations:
		\begin{align*}
			&\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2\alpha}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2\alpha}}\bar{p}_{\alpha}(0,t)+2\lambda\frac{\mathrm{d}^{\alpha}}{\mathrm{d}t^{\alpha}}\bar{p}_{\alpha}(0,t)=-\lambda^{2}\bar{p}_{\alpha}(0,t), \\
			&\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2\alpha}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2\alpha}}\bar{p}_{\alpha}(m,t)+2\lambda\frac{\mathrm{d}^{\alpha}}{\mathrm{d}t^{\alpha}}\bar{p}_{\alpha}(m,t)=-\lambda^{2}\Big(\bar{p}_{\alpha}(m,t)-\sum_{j=1}^m{\Pr}\{X_1 = j\}\bar{p}_\alpha(m-j,t)\Big), \text{ for $m \ge 1$ }.
		\end{align*}

