[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Let $(w,z)\in E$ be any edge of the graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximal degree $\Delta$. Assume that Assumption \ref{thiasssumptionnew} holds for the given $p_0\in(0,1)$, then we have, for any $m\geq 1$,
    \begin{equation}\begin{aligned}&
\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{\theta\in[0,\theta_*],\Lambda,\tau_0\in\Omega(\Lambda)}
\sum_{(uv)\in E}|\operatorname{Cor}_{(1-\theta)\otimes\mu^{\tau_0}}^{(2)}(uv,wz)|\geq 2\Delta m\right)\\&\leq \frac{2}{(1-e^{-\alpha_*})(1-e^{-2\alpha_*})}e^{2\gamma_*}e^{-\alpha_*m}.\end{aligned}
    \end{equation}

[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] If $\inf\sigma_{ess}(A) > \lambda$, then there exist constants $C_{Q} >0$ and $\delta_{Q} > 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\|Q_{+}S_{A-\lambda}(t) u\|_{L^{1}} \le C_{Q} e^{-\delta_{Q} t} \|Q_{+}u\|_{L^{1}}, \quad t \ge 0,
\end{align*}
for $u\in L^{2}(\R^{N})\cap L^{1}(\R^{N})$.

