[Lemma lem:moment_bound_empirical of arXiv:2608.23938, 'Generalization, memorization, and overfitting \\for diffusion models trained in the lazy h'] Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:high_dim of the paper) and~(ass:input_dist of the paper) hold. Then, for every \(\zeta\in (0,1)\),
    \[
        \left\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{{\boldsymbol z}\sim \mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_d)}[(\rho{\boldsymbol x}_{0,i}+\sigma{\boldsymbol z})^{\otimes k}]\right\|_\mathrm{F} \lesssim C_{\zeta,k} d^{\frac{k-1}{2}}
    \]
    for every \(k\in \mathbb{N}\) with probability at least \(1-\zeta\), where
    \begin{equation}
        C_{\zeta,k}:= (2C_{\mathrm{LSI}}^2((4k-\ln\zeta+2)k)^2)^{k/2}(4k-\ln\zeta).
    \end{equation}

