[Lemma 86 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $M \subset H_0$, its open covering $V=\{S_i \subset M\ |\ i \in I \}$, and locally defined tangent cones 
\begin{equation*}
\prod_{i \in I} (Cone\ A_i, S_i) \in \prod_{i \in I} CONE(S_i).
\end{equation*}
Then, 
\begin{equation*}
\left\{\Psi (Cone\ A_i, S_i)\ |\ i \in I \right\} \text{ is consistent  if } \prod_{i \in I} (Cone\ A_i, S_i) \text{ is closed}
\end{equation*}
(Definition \ref{def_consistancy21}). The opposite is not true.

