[Theorem 39 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Bakry-Emery (Theorem 21.2, \citet{villani2009}, Corollary 5.7.2, \citet{bakry:gentil:ledoux2014})}


    Let the probability measure $\nu$ on $\R^n$ have density $\nu(x) \propto \exp(-V(x))$ for all $x \in \R^n$. Suppose there is $\alpha > 0$ \st{} $\nabla^2 V(x) \succeq \alpha I_n$ for all $x \in \R^n$. Then, the following holds: 
    \begin{align*}
