[Corollary 23 (Sound computable pre-response certificates) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] For every full-column-rank $X$ with $m>d$, the general spectral certificate
$c_X$ defined in Appendix~\ref{app:pre-response-certificate} satisfies
$0\le c_X\le\nu_A$; under the assumptions of
Theorem~\ref{thm:critical-geometry}, the critical-coherence certificate
defined there satisfies $0\le t_\rho(A)\le\nu_A$.  More generally, every
verified $t(A)$ satisfying~\eqref{eq:pre-response-certificate-interface}
obeys, on the no-coloop positive-loss strict-interior domain of
Theorem~\ref{thm:robust-pre-response-phase},
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \alpha_s-\mathsf T_{\mathrm{spec}}^{\mathrm{RU}}(A,s)
  \ge \beta_s\gamma_s t(A).}

\end{equation}
Thus any pass with $t(A)>0$ certifies strictness uniformly over every
compatible residual direction.  Failure or abstention does not imply
$\nu_A=0$, envelope attainment, or the absence of another sound route. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

