[Corollary cor:pathwise_den of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $d=d_0$ and let Assumptions (assump:hor of the paper), (assum:sigma_0 of the paper) and (assum:b_0 of the paper)-(a) be in force. Furthermore, assume 

$\sigma_0(t, \cdot)$ is Lipschitz-continuous on $\mathbb{R}^{d_0}$, uniformly with respect to $t\in (0,T)$. 
Then:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] Under Assumption (assum:b_0 of the paper)-(b),  Kin-D-MKV$(B,b_0,\sigma_0)$ is pathwise well-posed (see Definition (def:sol_kinetic_density_MKV of the paper)).

\item[(ii)] Under Assumption (assum:b_0 of the paper)-(b-loc), for any \textcolor{black}{$\xi\in m\mathcal{F}_0$} 
with a density $v_0 \in L^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)\cap L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and for any $(W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t )$ $d_0$-dimensional Brownian motion, there exists a (pathwise) unique solution $X$ to D-MKV$(b_0,\sigma_0;\xi, W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t)$ (see Definition (def:weak_path_sol_den_MKV of the paper))  
whose flow of time-marginal densities belongs to $L^{\infty}_{T}L^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)$.
\end{itemize}

