[Definition def:sol_nl_fp_den of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $\nu\in \mathcal{M}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A 
function $v:(0,\infty)\to L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ is a (weak) solution to D-NL-FP$(b,\sigma;\nu)$ if it is a (weak) density solution to FP$(b_v,\sigma_v;\nu)$ (see Definition (def:sol_lin_fp of the paper)) with
\begin{equation}
b_v(t,x):= b\big( t, x , v_t(x) \big), \quad \sigma_v(t,x):= \sigma\big( t, x , v_t(x) \big), \qquad (t,x)\in[0,\infty)\times\mathbb{R}^d.
\end{equation}

