    \varepsilon \coloneqq \frac{1}{2} \wedge \frac{1}{2\kappa_a},
    \qquad
    \kappa_a \coloneqq \sum_{n \ge 1} q_n\,n^2\cosh(n/a)
    = \frac{1}{2N_a}\sum_{n\ge1} \frac{1 + e^{-2n/a}}{n^{2}} < \infty.
\end{align*}
The variable $X$ is integrable, with $\E[|X|] = 2\varepsilon\sum_{n\ge1} n\,q_n = (2\varepsilon/N_a)\sum_{n\ge1} n^{-3}e^{-n/a} < \infty$, and symmetric, hence ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:9e1777136eea6332f92fb01da49e047ac14fcdbc2903ff1b88d146f888229438","revision_digest":"sha256:45abfa2cf5eb9cd5d127e65e0d34f4a5d71651ccf1576ae909269a5bb898d993","source_id":"arxiv:2609.02398","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

