[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2607.08696, 'Spectrum of Directed Inhomogeneous Random Graphs'] Let $A > 1$ and $C_2>0$ and $\alpha$ be such that Assumptions \ref{ass:rank-one} and \ref{assumption:bulk-poly} hold. Then there are positive constants $B$ and $C_3$ depending on $A$, $C_2$ and $\alpha$, such that for every deterministic matrix $M_n$ with $\|M_n\|\le n^{C_2}$ we have
