[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2604.00742, 'Delayed Logistic equation as a limit\\ of long memory Markov chains'] For each $p\geq 1$ and $q \geq 1$, there exists a constant $C_{p,q,T}>0$ depending only on $p,q$ and $T$ such that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\E\left[\left( \widetilde{Z}^{N}(s)\right)^{p} \right] \;\leq\; C_{p,q,T} N^{-q/2}
	\end{equation*}
	for all $s \in [0,T]$.

