[Proposition prop:stat_meas_map of arXiv:2412.04032, 'Cutoff for the mixing time of the Facilitated Exclusion Process'] The process $(X(t), \sigma(t))_{t\ge 0}$ is a Markov chain, with stationary measure
\eqs{\nu_{N,K}^{\hbox{\tiny c},\textsc{ssep}} := \mathcal{U}(\mathbb{T}_N) \otimes \pi^{\textsc{ssep}}_{K,2K-N}.} 

Furthermore, if $(X, \sigma) \sim \mathcal{U}(\mathbb{T}_N) \otimes \pi^{\textsc{ssep}}_{K,2K-N}$, then 
\eqs{\Phi^{-1}(X,\sigma) \sim \mathcal{U}(\mathbb{T}_K) \otimes \pi^{\textsc{fep}}_{N,K} =: \mu_{N,K}^{\hbox{\tiny r},\textsc{fep}}.}

