[Definition 4 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $q \in (0,1)$, $c \in [0, q^{-1})$, $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $\lpplen = \{\lpplinen_{i}\}_{i \geq 1}$ be as in (\ref{Eq.Deflpplen}). We define the constants
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\sigma = \frac{q^{1/2}}{1- q}, \hspace{2mm} f = \frac{q^{1/3}}{2 (1 + q)^{2/3}},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
and the rescaled processes
\begin{equation}
\lpplenc_i(t) = \sigma^{-1} N^{-1/3} \cdot \left(\lpplinen_i(tN^{2/3}) - \frac{2qN}{1-q} - \frac{qtN^{2/3}}{1-q}\right) \mbox{ for } i \in \mathbb{N}, t \in [0,\infty).
\end{equation}

[Prop normalitycriterion of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(Y\) be a real-valued random variable.  Let \(\alpha>0\), let \((B_s)_{s\ge1}\) be a nonnegative sequence, and let \(c>0\) be some constant.  Assume that for every real \(u\) with \(S_\alpha(|u|)\ge1\),
			\begin{equation}
				|\mathbb E e(uY)|\le \exp(-cB_{S_\alpha(|u|)}).
			\end{equation}
			Assume also that
			\begin{equation}
				\sum_{s\ge1}s\exp(-cB_s)<\infty.
			\end{equation}
			Then \(Y\) is almost surely absolutely normal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:resolvent of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] Let $\alpha \in (0,2)$, $\lambda >0$ and $f\in C_b(\mathbb{R}_*)$. Then, $u = U_\lambda f$ is the solution of the following Neumann problem for the fractional Laplacian
    \begin{align*}
        \begin{cases}
            \big[(-\Delta)^{\alpha/2} + \lambda \mathrm{I}\big] u &= f, \quad \mathrm{in }~D, \\
            \phantom{\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,}\big[\mathcal{N}_{\alpha/2} + \lambda \mathrm{I}\big] u &= f, \quad \mathrm{in }~\overline{D}^c.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem LSI of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] For reversible chains, the following  are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item The \red[log-Sobolev inequality] holds with constant $\beta$:
\begin{eqnarray}

\forall f\in\mathcal {F}^{++},\quad \mathscr {E}(\sqrt{f},\sqrt{f}) & \ge & \beta\mathrm{Ent}(f).
\end{eqnarray}
\item  The semi-group is \red[hypercontractive] at rate $4\beta$, i.e. 
\begin{eqnarray}
\forall f\in\mathcal {F},\quad\forall t\ge 0,\quad \|P_tf\|_{1+e^{4\beta t}} & \le & \|f\|_2.
 \end{eqnarray} 
 \end{enumerate}

