[Proposition prop-exponential-tightness of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] Let $\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon) $ and $\theta_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}$ satisfy the conditions in Lemma (exponential-estimate-lemma2 of the paper). Then under the scaling regime (equation scaling-delta of the paper),  there exists a sequence of compact set $\{K_n\}_{n\geqslant1}\subset\mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\beta}$, such that the laws $\{\mu_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}\}$ of $\{\theta_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}\}$ satisfy   
	\begin{equation*}
		\limsup_{n\rightarrow\infty}\limsup_{\varepsilon\rightarrow0}\varepsilon\log\mu_{\varepsilon,\delta(\varepsilon)}(K_n)=-\infty. 
	\end{equation*}

