[Thma 1 (Ground state - Biggins \cite{biggins76}) of arXiv:2608.18276, 'The branching random walk in a uniform magnetic field : magnetization concentration and ov'] The ground state is given by
\begin{equation}

\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \, \max_{ \sigma \in \Sigma_n} H_n(\sigma,h)= \gamma_{\max}(h) :=\beta_c + h \tanh(\beta_c h), \quad \text{a.s. and in } L^1,
\end{equation}
where $\psi_h(t):=  \frac{t^2}{2} + \log 2 + \log (\cosh(ht))$, for all $t \in \R$, and  $\beta_c=\beta_c(h)>0$ is the unique positive real number satisfying
\begin{equation}

\beta_c \psi'_h(\beta_c)- \psi_h(\beta_c)=0,
\end{equation}
(see Lemma \ref{lem:Psi-h} for existence and uniqueness of $\beta_c$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

