body:
[Prop 12 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M,J,\omega)$ be a non-K\"ahler lcK manifold. Suppose that $\omega$ is Gauduchon, $\|\theta\|$ is constant and $dRic^{t,2}=0$, then there only are two possibilities 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $t=-1$ and $\omega$ is Vaisman;
        \item $t=2n-1\pm2\sqrt{n(n-1)}$ and $dJ\theta = (1-n)\theta\wedge J\theta$. 
    \end{itemize}
    In both cases $\Ric^{t,2}=\Ric^{t,1}$, and so in particular it is cohomologous to $\Ric^{Ch,1}$ with difference given by a multiple of $dJ\theta$.

