[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2608.27166, 'Well-posedness and regularity of stochastic heat equations on moving domains'] For every $p>0$ and $T_0>0$, there exists
$C=C(n,\lambda,\Lambda,B,T_0,p,D)$ such that
\begin{align*}
\E\norm{u}_{L^\infty([T_0,2T_0]\times D)}^p
&\leq
C
\left(
\norm{u_0}_{L^2(D)}
+
\norm{K}_{L^\infty(D)}
\right)^p .
\end{align*}

