body:
[Theorem markov of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $f: S'(M) \rightarrow \mathbb R$ bounded and $M_\ell$-measurable,  
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E_{\nu}[f \mid \mathcal F_{M_\ell^c}](\varphi^c) = \mathbb E_{\nu^\ell({\Large \boldsymbol{\cdot} }\,\mid \varphi_-,\varphi_+)}[f],
\end{equation}
where $\varphi_-,\varphi_+$ are the restrictions of $\varphi^c$ to the components of the boundary $\partial M_\ell$ which exists $\nu$-almost surely and are i.i.d. according to $\nu^0$ . (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] Let $H\subset G\subset F$ be a chain of order dense sublattices and let $B\subset G$ be solid. The following sets are equal:
\item[(i)] The set of all $f\in F$ such that there is $Q\subset B_{+}$ with $Q\uparrow\left|f\right|$;
\item[(i')] The set of all $f\in F$ such that there is $Q\subset B_{+}\cap H$ with $Q\uparrow\left|f\right|$;
\item[(ii)] The order adherence of $B$ in $F$;
\item[(ii')] The order adherence of $B\cap H$ in $F$;
\item[(iii)] Order adherence of $\Sol B$ in $F$;
\item[(iii')] Order adherence of $\Sol\left(B\cap H\right)$ in $F$;
\item[(iv)] Sets similar to (ii)-(iii') with uo adherence replacing order adherence.\medskip

This set is solid and its intersection with $G$ and $H$ is the common order and uo adherence of $B$ in $G$ and of $B\cap H$ in $H$, respectively. The order and uo closures of $B$ and $B\cap H$ also coincide, and are a solid set. Both the adherence and the closure are convex, whenever $B$ is. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

