[Lemma lemma-product-estimate of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] [Res95]
	Suppose that $s>0$ and $p \in(1, \infty)$. For any $f, g \in C^{\infty}\left(\mathbb{T}^2\right)$, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\left\|\Lambda^s(f g)\right\|_{L^p(\mathbb{T}^2)} \leqslant C\left(\|f\|_{L^{p_1}(\mathbb{T}^2)}\left\|\Lambda^s g\right\|_{L^{p_2}(\mathbb{T}^2)}+\|g\|_{L^{p_1}(\mathbb{T}^2)}\left\|\Lambda^s f\right\|_{L^{p_2}(\mathbb{T}^2)}\right),
	\end{equation*}
	where $p_1, p_2\in(1, \infty)$ satisfy		$	\frac{1}{p}=\frac{1}{p_1}+\frac{1}{p_2}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

