body:
[Lemma lem:primitlgamma of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{L}_S$ be given in (equation def:lsbip of the paper) for a primitive QMS generator $\mathcal{L}^A$. Suppose that (asspA2 of the paper) holds. Then, it holds that
\begin{align*}
   \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S) = \ker(\mathcal{L}^A) \otimes \mathcal{M}_B = {\bf 1}^A  \otimes \mathcal{M}_B\,,
\end{align*}
and 
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_\gamma) =  \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S)\cap \{X \in \mathcal{M}_{AB}\,;\ [H, X] = 0\}\,.
\end{equation*}
    Moreover, suppose that (condeq:php of the paper) holds. Then, 
    \begin{align*}
       \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_\gamma) = {\bf 1}^A  \otimes \left\{X^B \in \mathcal{M}_B\,;\ \left[G_j^B, X^B\right] = 0 \ \text{for all $j \ge 1$}  \right\}\,.
    \end{align*}
    The condition $\dim \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S) > \dim \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_\gamma)$ is equivalent to that $\{G_j^B\}_{j \ge 1}$ are not all zero.

