[Lemma lem:decoupling of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] For each $k \ge 0$,
  \begin{equation}
    p_{k+1} \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:decoupling of the paper)}} \ell_k^{2d+2} (p_k^2 + \varepsilon_k),
  \end{equation}
  where the decoupling error $\varepsilon_k$ satisfies
  \begin{equation}
    \varepsilon_k \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:survival_eps_decay of the paper)}} T_{k+1}^{d+1} \parens*{ \rho_0 \exp\braces*{ -c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:survival_eps_decay of the paper)}} L_k^{1/3} } + \exp\braces*{ -c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:survival_eps_decay of the paper)}} \rho_0 L_k^{2/15} } }
  \end{equation}
  for constants $C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:survival_eps_decay of the paper)}}, c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:survival_eps_decay of the paper)}} > 0$ depending only on the dimension.

