[Theorem T:exact of arXiv:2412.09655, 'The Critical Beta-splitting Random Tree III: The exchangeable partition representation and'] Define $Y_t := - \log  P_{t,1}$.
Then $(Y_t, 0 \le t < \infty)$ is the subordinator 
given by (equation muinf3 of the paper).
Moreover, for $t\ge0$ and complex $s$ with $\Re s>-1$,
\begin{align}
\operatorname{\mathbb E}{} [P_{t,1}^s] =\operatorname{\mathbb E}{} [ e^{-s Y_t}]  
=e^{-t(\psi(s+1)-\psi(1))}
\end{align}
where $\psi(z):=\Gamma'(z)/\Gamma(z)$ 
is the digamma function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition Estimate_derivative_Pg0 of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_g \underset{g \to +\infty}{\rightarrow}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c - \mu_g = o(g^{-2})$ and any $p_1,\cdots,p_k \ge 1$, $n \ge 0$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \alpha_{n,g,\mathbf{p}} (\mathbf{M}) \underset{g \to +\infty}{\sim} \varphi(n,g,\mathbf{p}).
    \end{align*}

