[Theorem thm:CLT of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let $ \mathsf{M}$ a weakly stationary random measure~ in dimension $ d\geqslant 2$ having finite moments of all orders on a compact set.   
 Assume that for some $ m_{ 0}\geqslant 3$, for $ m\geqslant m_{ 0}$, the cumulants have Poisson / sub-Poisson decay
 \begin{align}
 \kappa _{ m}(\mathsf{M}(B_{ R})) =& O(R^{ d}) .
\end{align}
Then we have the CLT for some sequence $ R_{ n}\to \infty $
\begin{align*}
\widetilde{ \mathsf{M}(B_{ R_{ n}})}\to   \mathscr  N(0,1).
\end{align*}
In   dimension $ 1$, if (equation eq:subpoisson-cumulant of the paper) holds  and $  \textrm{Var}\left(\mathsf{M}(B_{ R})\right)\geqslant cR^{  \alpha }$ with $ \alpha >0,$  as $ R\to \infty ,$
\begin{align*}
  \widetilde{ \mathsf{M}(B_{ R})}\to   \mathscr  N(0,1).
\end{align*}

