	\begin{equation}   \mathbb{E}\left[ \sup_{x\in \mathbb{X}}  \frac{\sum_{k\geq 0}(k+1)\log^+(k+1)^{1+\varepsilon}{\mathbb P}\left[F_{x,\xi_0}= k|{\bar{\xi}}\right]}{f_{x,\xi_0}}\right] <\infty, \end{equation}

	\begin{equation}   \mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{x\in \mathbb{X}}  \frac{\sum_{k\geq 0}\log^+(k+1)^{1+\varepsilon} {\mathbb P}\left[F_{x,\xi_0}\geq k|{\bar{\xi}} \right]}{f_{x,\xi_0}}\right] <\infty. \end{equation}
	Then (ass: LlogL of the paper) holds. If additionally $\lambda>0$, then the conclusions of Theorem (thme:nondegenerescence of the paper) hold. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

