[Prop var-lb of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Assume $n/\ell\to\infty$ and $\go_e\stackrel{\mathrm{d}}{=}\mathrm{Exp}(1)^{1/\theta}$. 
Then there exists $c>0$ such that, for all sufficiently large $n$, we have
\begin{align}
 \var(T_{[n]})\geqslant c \left( \frac{n}{\ell^{2+2/\theta}} \vee \frac{1}{\ell^{2/\theta}} \right).
\end{align}
Similarly, we have
\begin{align}
 \var\bigl(T_n\bigr)
 \geqslant c\left( \frac n{\ell^{2+2/\theta}} \vee \frac{1}{\ell^{2/\theta}} \right).
\end{align}

