[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2609.00988, 'Covering Projective Height Balls by Subspaces in Rigid Adelic Spaces'] There exists a constant $C_2\geq 1$, effectively computable from $d, r_2,|D_K|, R_K$ with the following property. For every rigid adelic space $F$ over $K$ and every $0\neq x\in F$ there is $a\in K^\times$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \|ax\|_{F,v}\le
\begin{cases}
1,& v\nmid\infty,\\
C_2H_F(x),& v\mid\infty.
\end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $G$ be a $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function defined in the open right half-plane. Then it is analytic and contractive in $\mathbb C_r$ if and
    only if the kernel
    \begin{equation}

\frac{I_m-G(z)G(w)^*}{2\pi(z+\overline{w})}
\end{equation}
is positive definite in $\mathbb C_r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition Def: branched rough paths of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For $\alpha\in(0,1]$, $N:=\lfloor\frac{1}{\alpha}\rfloor$ and $T>0$, a branched $\alpha$-rough path is a map $\mathbb X:[0,T]_\leq^2\to \mathcal{H}^\ast_N$ such that 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item For any $(s,u,t)\in[0,T]_\leq^3$, $\mathbb X$ satisfies Chen's relation in $\mathcal{H}_N^\ast$
			\begin{equation}
				\mathbb X_{st}=\mathbb X_{su}\star\mathbb X_{ut}\,.
			\end{equation}
			\item For any $\tau\in{\mathcal T}$
			\begin{equation*}
				|\mathbb X_{st}(\tau)|\lesssim |t-s|^{|\tau|\alpha}\, ,
			\end{equation*}
			uniformly on $0\le s\le t\le T$.
			\item For any forest $w=\tau_1\cdots\tau_k\in{\mathcal F}^{\leq N}$,
			\[\mathbb X_{st}(w)=\prod_{i=1}^k\mathbb X_{st}(\tau_i)\,.\]
		\end{itemize}
		If in addition $\mathbb X_{st}(\bullet_i)=\delta X^i_{st}$ for a path $X:[0,T]\to \mathbb{R}^d$, we say that $\mathbb X$ is an $\alpha$-branched rough path lift of $X$.

[Prop 36 of arXiv:2609.01932, 'Essential dimension and faithful rank of finite $p$-gerbes'] A vector bundle on $\cX$ is $f$-faithful if and only if its
restriction to $\fC_f$ is faithful.  Consequently
\begin{equation}
\rdim(f)=
\min_{\mathcal B\text{ basis of }\fC_f^*}
\sum_{\chi\in\mathcal B}m_\chi(\cX).
\end{equation}

[Thm 4 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] Let $m\geq2$, and let 
\begin{equation}
\Omega_{m}=\left\{ 0,\ldots,m-1\right\} ^{\mathbb{N}}
\end{equation}
with its product Borel structure. If $E$ is a POVM on $\Omega_{m}$,
write 
\begin{equation}
E_{w}=E\left(\left[w\right]\right),\qquad H_{w}=\overline{ran}\,(E^{1/2}_{w})
\end{equation}
for each finite word $w$ in the alphabet $\left\{ 0,\ldots,m-1\right\} $.
Then, for every $w$, there are unique positive contractions 
\begin{equation}
A^{\left(0\right)}_{w},\ldots,A^{\left(m-1\right)}_{w}\in B\left(H_{w}\right)
\end{equation}
such that 
\begin{equation}
\sum^{m-1}_{j=0}A^{\left(j\right)}_{w}=I_{H_{w}}
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
E_{wj}=E^{1/2}_{w}A^{\left(j\right)}_{w}E^{1/2}_{w}.
\end{equation}

Conversely, suppose that $E_{\varnothing}=I$, and that the cylinder
values are defined recursively by positive contractions $A^{\left(j\right)}_{w}\in B\left(H_{w}\right)$
satisfying \prettyref{eq:2-13} and \prettyref{eq:2-14}. Then there
is a unique POVM $E$ on $\Omega_{m}$ with these cylinder values.

