body:
[Lemma lem:scale of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Fix $K \geqslant 1, s>0$ and $\beta>0$ and let $\left\{X_{n}\right\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of nonnegative random variables satisfying $X_{n} \leqslant \mathcal{O}_{s}\left(K 3^{-n \beta}\right)$ for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Then, there exists a constant $C:=C(s, \beta, K)>0$ such that the random scale 
		\begin{align*}
			\mathcal{M}:=\sup \left\{3^{n} \in \mathbb{N}: X_{n} \geqslant 1\right\},
		\end{align*}
		satisfies the estimate 
		\begin{align*}
			\mathcal{M} \leqslant \mathcal{O}_{\beta s}(C).
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:99 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] For $j,k,i,\Delta\in [\![-2\varepsilon n^{1/3},2\varepsilon n^{1/3}]\!]$ additionally satisfying $\Delta\geq 0$ and $i\geq 1$, consider the event $E_{i,\Delta}$ defined by
  \begin{equation}

    E_{i,\Delta}=\{\Gamma_{u_j}^{v_k}\subseteq L_{u_{j+i/2}}^{v_{k+(\Delta+i)/2}}, \Gamma_{u_{j+i}}^{v_{k+\Delta+i}}\subseteq R_{u_{j+i/2}}^{v_{k+(\Delta+i)/2}}\}.
  \end{equation}
  Then for some positive constants $C,c_1,c_2$, and all $n$, we have
   \begin{equation}

    \mathbb{P}(E_{i,\Delta})\geq 1-C\min(e^{-c_1\Delta^2},e^{-c_2i^3}).
  \end{equation}

