[Theorem 47 (Estimate for Projected Payoffs) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. Define the dynamic obstacle $\Phi(x) := g(\langle h, x \rangle_H)$, where $g: \R \to \R$ is concave and $L$-Lipschitz, and $h \in \mathrm{Dom}(A^*)$. Let $u_\varepsilon$ be the unique mild solution to \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized}. Then, the penalty term $\Pi_\varepsilon$ defined in \eqref{eq:yosida_penalty} satisfies:
\begin{equation}

    0 \le \Pi_\varepsilon(t, x) \le C w_m(x), \quad \forall (t,x) \in [0,T] \times H,
\end{equation}
for a constant $C > 0$ independent of $\varepsilon$. Consequently, $\Phi$ is an admissible obstacle in the sense of Definition \ref{def:admissible_obstacle}.

