[Lemma lem:fpbound of arXiv:2605.06887, 'Law of large numbers for activated random walk on villages'] Under the assumption of Proposition (thm:fpsol of the paper), for any $m \in \mathbb{R}_+^V$ we have
\begin{equation}
\Vert m - m_*\Vert_\eta \leq \frac{1}{1-\mu} \Vert m - \phi(m)\Vert_\eta, \end{equation}
where $\mu < 1$ is the principal eigenvalue of $P$ (cf.\ Definition (def_eta_norm of the paper)).

[Lemma lem_regular_estimate_localized_eigenvalue of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under the assumptions of (theorem_localized_eigenvalue of the paper), the following bounds hold uniformly in $t\in[0,1]$:
    \begin{align}
    \Delta(t)&=\mathrm{O}\left({\left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle}\right),\\       
\langle \mathsf M_0{\widehat{\Lambda}}_t\mathsf M_1E_a \rangle&=\mathrm{O}\left({\im m_t(z_t)\cdot \left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle}\right)
        \end{align}
for any $a\in [\![{D}]\!]$ and $\mathsf M_0,\mathsf M_1\in\ha{M_t\left({z_t}\right),M_t^*\left({z_t}\right)}$, where ${\widehat{\Lambda}}_t$ is defined by ${\widehat{\Lambda}}_t=\Lambda-\Delta\left({t}\right)$.

