[Lemma LEM:MUS of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q\in \mathbb{Z}$ with $|Q|=k$. Then we have 
\begin{align*}
E(m_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k})&=\sum_{j=1}^k E(m_{\xi_j})+O(e^{-c \min_{i \neq j}|\xi_i-\xi_j|  })
\end{align*}

\noindent
as $\min_{i \neq j}|\xi_i-\xi_j| \to \infty$, where $c>0$ only depends on $|Q|$.

[Lemma lem:sharp-hitting-magnetization-zero of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Initialized from $\pi^+$, the hitting time to the set $\{m=0\}$, denoted $\tau_{m=0}$ satisfies 
     \begin{align*}
         \mathbb P( \tau_{m=0} \ge \exp( (1+\varepsilon) \Delta_{\alpha,\theta} N ) \le e^{- \Omega(N)}\,
     \end{align*}
    for every $\varepsilon>0$.

