body:
[Theorem 50 (Intersection-profile coefficient equivalence) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $m\ge1$, $2\le r<\infty$, and $1\le p<\infty$.  Put
\begin{equation}

 d_{m,p}:=
 \begin{cases}
  1,&p\ge2,\\
  c_m,&1\le p<2,
 \end{cases}
 \qquad c_m=4\sqrt2\,3^{2m}.
\end{equation}
Then every $K\in\mathfrak T_{m,r}$ satisfies
\begin{equation}

 d_{m,p}^{-1}\Prof_{m,r}(K)
 \le\norm{\cT_K^{(m)}}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \le C_m(p+r)^{m/2}\Prof_{m,r}(K),
\end{equation}
and every $K\in\mathfrak W_{m,r}$ satisfies
\begin{equation}

 \frac{m!}{d_{m,p}m^{m/2}}
 \norm K_{\mathfrak W_{m,r}}
 \le\norm{I_m(K)}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \le A_m(p+r)^{m/2}\norm K_{\mathfrak W_{m,r}}.
\end{equation}
Thus both evaluators are Banach-space isomorphisms onto their images, and
their images are closed.

