[Lemma lem:sigma_k of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $\{\sigma_k\}_{k\ge1}$ be any orthonormal basis of $U_0=H^{\frac d2 +\alpha}_{\div}$. Then, for every $x,y \in \mathbb{R}^d$ we have
	\begin{equation*}
		Q(x-y)=\sum_{k\ge1} \sigma_k(x) \otimes \sigma_k(y),
	\end{equation*}
	where the series converges absolutely and uniformly on compact sets, and
	\begin{equation*}
		|Q(x-y)| \leqslant |Q(0)| < \infty.
	\end{equation*}

[Proposition P:negative_gamma of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$. There exists a constant $A = A(\varepsilon) > 0$ such that for any $\gamma < 0$ there is an $n_0 = n_0(\gamma, \varepsilon)$ with
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E}\Big[ \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mathrm{P}}}_{\ensuremath{\mathcal T}}  \big( A^{-1} \sqrt{n} \leq \operatorname{diam}({\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} ) \leq A \sqrt{n} \big) \Big] \geq 1 - \varepsilon
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n \geq n_0$.

