\begin{equation*}
    \Omega_1= \{ (x,y)\in (1, \infty)^2 : \frac{1}{\mathrm m} < \frac{y-1}{x-1}< \mathrm m\} 
    \quad\text{and}\quad
    \Omega_2= \{ (x,y)\in {\mathbb R}_+^2 : \frac{1}{\mathrm m} < \frac{y}{x}< \mathrm m\} .
\end{equation*}
Under the same assumptions of Theorem (thm:LLN of the paper), we conjecture that (equation eq:CLLN of the paper) holds with 
\begin{equation} 
    	h(x,y)= \begin{cases}
    \ell + \bar{\mathcal{L}}_{(a,b)}(xa, yb)   \quad &\text{for }(x,y)\in \Omega_1\\
    \frac12 \left[ (\ell+a-b)x +(\ell-a+b)y - |x-y|\sqrt{D} \right] \quad &\text{for } (x,y)\in \Omega_2\setminus \Omega_1\\
   \bar{\mathcal{L}}(xa, yb) \quad &\text{for } (x,y)\in {\mathbb R}_+^2\setminus \Omega_2.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

