[Lemma L:cT_exc_dia_C1 of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Let $\operatorname{Exc}_{\max}$ and $\operatorname{diam}_{\max}$ be the maximum excess and diameter of the connected components in the Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi  random graph $\mathbb{G}(n,1/n)$, respectively. Then, with $\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mathrm{P}}}$-probability at least $1 - n^{-1}$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
    \operatorname{diam}({\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} ) \leq 2 \max_{u \in V} d_{\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} (u, \mathcal{L})
    + 2 \max_{2 \leq i \leq k}  d_{\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} ({\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} _i, {\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} _1) + 12( \operatorname{Exc}_{\max} + 2) \operatorname{diam}_{\max}.
\end{equation*}

