[Proposition prop:basic-facts-homogeneity of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let gamble space $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ and variable $X:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ be given.
  Then
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $\overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}(cX) = c\, \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$ for all $c\geq 0$ (1-homogeneity) when $\mathcal{Z}$ is arbitrage-free and scalable.
  \end{enumerate}
  When $\mathcal{Z}$ is scalable, the statement holds for $c>0$ (positive homogeneity).

[Definition def_eq_cup_cdf of arXiv:2412.07258, 'Permuton limit of a generalization of the Mallows and $k$-card-minimum models'] A permuton $\mu$ is a probability measure on $[0,1]^2$ such that both marginal distributions are uniform on $[0,1]$.
    If $(X,Y) \sim \mu$ then $F_\mu$ denotes the joint cumulative distribution function of $(X,Y)$. Let us define the $\cup$-c.d.f.\ of $\mu$ by
        \begin{equation}
        V_\mu(x,y)=x+y-F_\mu(x,y)=\mathbb{P}\left(\{X \leqslant x\} \cup \{ Y \leqslant y \}  \right).
    \end{equation}

