[Proposition 4 (Alternating subset formula) of arXiv:2606.29635, 'Extremality and Limit Laws for the Siblings of the Coupon Collector'] Let $p_B=\sum_{i\in B}p_i$. Then, for every $j\ge2$,
\begin{equation}
        \E_pU_j^N=\sum_{\varnothing\ne B\subseteq[N]}(-1)^{|B|-1}\sum_{k\in B}\left(\frac{p_k}{p_B}\right)^j.
\end{equation}

