body:
[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2607.26564, 'Stochastic Scalar Conservation Laws on Moving Hypersurfaces'] Assume that $u^\epsilon$ solves the stochastic viscous conservation law \eqref{eq75}.

Then for any $M>0$ and small $\Delta t > 0$, there exist a constant $C_M>0$ independent of $\epsilon$ and $\Delta t$ such that
\begin{eqnarray*}
\mathbb{E}[I_{\Omega_{M}}\int_{0}^{T-\Delta t}\|\widetilde{u}^\epsilon(t+\Delta t) - \widetilde{u}^\epsilon(t)\|_{L^1(\Gamma_0)}dt]
\leq C_M(\sqrt{\Delta t} +  \Delta t).

\end{eqnarray*}

