[Lemma restr-gl-sp-right-Quillen of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be a homomorphism of compact Lie groups. Then
    \[
        \alpha_!\colon\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}_\textup{$G$-global}\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G'}$-OrthSp}_\textup{$G'$-global} 
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 \alpha^*
    \]
    is a Quillen adjunction with homotopical right adjoint.
    \begin{proof}
        It is clear from the definitions that $\alpha^*$ preserves weak equivalences, while the construction as a transferred model structure in the proof of Theorem~(thm:G-gl-Sp-model-struct of the paper) makes it clear that $\alpha^*$ also preserves fibrations.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Defs 9 (Liftings) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] A \emph{lifting} is a map~$\ell\colon \mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$
satisfying
\begin{enumerate*}[$(a)$]
\item $\tclass{\ell(f)}=\class{f}$; 
\item if $\class{f}=\class{g}$, then~$\ell(f)=\ell(g)$;
\item $\ell(\car)=\car$;
\item if~$f\geq 0$, then~$\ell(f)\geq 0$;
\item $\ell(a f+b g)=a\ell(f)+b\ell(g)$ for~$a,b\in \R$;
\item $\ell(fg)=\ell(f)\ell(g)$.
\end{enumerate*}

A lifting is \emph{strong} if, additionally,
\begin{enumerate*}[$(a)$]\setcounter{enumi}{6}
\item $\ell(\phi)=\phi$ for~$\phi\in\Cb(X)$.
\end{enumerate*}

A \emph{Borel} \emph{lifting} is a lifting with~$\A=\Bo{\T}$.

As a consequence of~\iref{i:d:Liftings:1}, a lifting~$\ell\colon \mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$ descends to a (linear multiplicative order-preserving) right inverse~$\ell\colon L^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$ of the quotient map~$\class[\mssm]{\emparg}\colon\mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar L^\infty(\mssm)$.
As customary, by a (\emph{strong}/\emph{Borel}) \emph{lifting} we shall mean without distinction either~$\ell$ or~$\ell$ as above.

[Theorem wlln of arXiv:2604.12815, 'On ergodicity of the SAGA-LD algorithm\thanks{The author gratefully acknowledges the suppo'] Let $W_{n}$, $n\in\mathbb{N}$ be a real-valued process with $\alpha_{W}(n)\to 0$, 
$n\to\infty$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{V\to\infty}\sup_{n\geq 1}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}E[|W_{j}|1_{\{|W_{j}|\geq V\}}]\to 0,\ V\to\infty.	
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
E\left[\left|\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{n}[W_{j}-E[W_{j}]]}{n}\right|\right]\to 0,\ n\to\infty.	
\end{equation}
\hfill $\Box$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

