[Lem 8 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] Let $\Phi(x) = d(x,\bigcup_{j=1}^m P_j)$ be the distance function and let $0 < \rho < r$. For any collection $\cU = \sbrac{u_i: i\in[m]}\subseteq \mathbb{S}^{d-1}$, there exists a set $\cZ = \sbrac{z_i: i \in [m]} \subseteq B_{1/4}(0)$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \cD_{\cZ} := \frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^m\int_{\R^d} \int_{-1}^1  |g(s)||\Phi(x + s\rho u_j) - \rho|s||\,ds\,d\la_{(u_j,z_j,r)} \leq C_{g,d} m\rho^2 r^{d-1}
    \end{equation}
    where $C_{g,d}$ is a constant depending on $g$ and $d$.

