[Proposition dd-opt-prop of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let \(\mathcal{A} =\Lambda_{\text{glob}} (\kappa,\alpha, 0)\) and \(\mathcal{B} =\Lambda_{\text{glob}} (\zeta,\beta, 0)\) be drift-diffusion generators on \(\mathbb{R}^d\). Then the Markovian transport derivative is given by
\begin{align}
    \theta_2(x, y; \mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B}) =  (\kappa-\zeta)^\top (x-y)+ \mathcal{W}_{\mathcal{S}}(\alpha, \beta)^2,
\end{align}
where \(\mathcal{W}_{\mathcal{S}}(\alpha, \beta)\) is as defined in (equation D-def of the paper). Moreover, an optimal Markovian coupling of \(\mathcal{A}\) and \(\mathcal{B}\) is given by the drift diffusion generator \(\mathcal{J}=\Lambda_{\text{glob}} (\eta,\sigma, 0)\), where \(\sigma\) is defined as in (equation si-def of the paper) with \(K\) being a minimizer of the semidefinite program (equation posdef-prog of the paper), and $\eta=(\kappa,\zeta)\in\mathbb R^{2d}$.

