[Definition def.pyramid of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given $k \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, for every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_k$, we can construct a sequence partition of good cubes $(\mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h})_{0 \leqslant h \leqslant k-1}$ as follows. 
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{split}
				\mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{k-1}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}) &:= \mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{k-1}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}), \\
				\forall 0 \leqslant h \leqslant k-2, \qquad \mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}) &:= \bigcup_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}' \in \mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h+1}} \mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{h}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}').  
			\end{split}
		\end{equation}
		In the equation (equation e.pyrmid of the paper) above, for ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}' \in \mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h+1}$, we call the cubes in $\mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{h}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}')$ its \emph{children partition cubes}, and respectively ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}'$ is the unique \emph{parent partition cube} for $\mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{h}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}')$. For any $x \in {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}$, we denote by ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_{\mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h}}(x)$ the unique element in $\mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h}$ that contains $x$.

[Corollary 29 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] The $L^p$-norm of the vector of Riesz transforms when acting on complex-valued functions has the bounds 
\begin{equation}
\|R\|_{L^p(\R^d;\, \bC)}
\le
\begin{cases}
\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2}}\, \frac{1}{\sqrt{p-1}}\,\,\|H\|_p &1<p<2,\\ 
\sqrt{\pi}\,\,\, \|H\|_p, \,\,\,\,\, & 2\leq p<\infty. 
\end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lm:D_small of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] Fix $t \in (0,\infty) \cap \mathbb{Q}$. For any $\epsilon > 0$, there exist $M_\epsilon, N_{\epsilon} \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for every $N \in \mathbb{N}$ with $N \geq N_{\epsilon}$ and $tN \in \mathbb{N}$, one has  

\begin{equation*}
Q \left( e^{-\frac{\beta^2}{2} t} \mathbf{E}_{\tau^N} \left[ \mathbf{E}_{\gamma}\left[ \exp(\beta \mathscr{A}_t^N)\right] \mathbbm{1}_{n^N_t > M_\epsilon} \right] > \epsilon \right) < \epsilon. 
\end{equation*}

