body:
[Defination 9 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Consider a family $(\K(t))_{t\ge 0}$ of absolutely continuous adapted (w.r.t. the observable filtration) processes with values in the class of  symmetric positive definite $n \times n $ matrices and a family $(k(t))_{t\ge 0}$ of locally bounded deterministic functions with positive values. We will say that  a family $(A(t))_{t\ge 0}$  of measurable locally bounded process with values in the class $n \times n$ matrices,  is $(\K(t), k(t))_{t\ge 0}$-stable,  or in short, that $A$ is $(\K, k)$-stable, if  for all $t\ge 0$,
			\begin{equation} 
				\dot{\K}(t)\geqm A(t)\K(t) + \K(t)A^{\top}(t) + k(t)\K(t).
			\end{equation}

