[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] For any $0<H<\frac12$ and $1<\alpha<2$, there exists a positive constant $c_{H,\alpha}$ such that for all $t>0$ and $x\in \mathbb R$,
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^2 }\left|\Box(t,x,y,h)\right|^2|h|^{2H-2}|y|^{2H-2}dydh\le c_{H,\alpha}\left(t^{\frac{4H-4}{\alpha}}\wedge \frac{|x|^{2H-2}}{t^{\frac{2-2H}{\alpha}}}\right).
\end{equation}

