[Theorem th:path_localisation of arXiv:2608.06263, 'Almost sure path localisation for the derivative martingale of branching Brownian motion'] Let $a,b$ be functions $\mathbb{R}_{\ge0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ satisfying $a \downarrow 0$ and $b \uparrow \infty$.
Then, almost surely,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{r \to \infty} \lim_{t \to \infty} \sum_{u \in \mathcal{N}_t} X_u(t) \mathrm{e}^{-X_u(t)} \1_{\{\forall s \in [r,t], X_u(s) \in [a(s)\sqrt{s},b(s)\sqrt{s}]\}} = \begin{cases}
    Z_\infty &\text{ if (equation eq:integrability_conditions of the paper) holds,} \\ 0 &\text{ otherwise.}
\end{cases} 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:abstract-active-response-multiplicity of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The active response family satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal N_\mu(\Lambda)\text{ is a singleton}
