body:
[Cor c:dov-holder of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Fix $L\geqslant 1$ and $t_0\in (0,1]$, and fix $\gamma\in(0,\frac12)$.
    For all sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$ (depending only on $L,t_0,\gamma$), all $x\in[-L,L]$, and all {$r\in [\varepsilon^\gamma, t_0]$}, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(
            \sup_{\substack{z_1,z_2 \in [-L,L]\\|z_1-z_2| \leqslant 8\varepsilon\log^4(1/\varepsilon)}}    
            \left|\mathcal{L}(0,x;r,z_1) - \mathcal{L}(0,x;r,z_2)\right|
            \geqslant
            2^{1/3}\varepsilon^{1/2}\log^4(1/\varepsilon)
        \right) \leqslant  Ce^{-c\log^{9/4}(1/\varepsilon)},
    \end{align*}
    where $C,c>0$ depend only on $L,\gamma$.
    Similarly, for all $r\in[0, t_0-\varepsilon^\gamma]$,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(
            \sup_{\substack{z_1,z_2 \in [-L,L]\\|z_1-z_2| \leqslant 8\varepsilon\log^4(1/\varepsilon)}}    
            \left|\mathcal{L}(r,z_1; t_0,x) - \mathcal{L}(r,z_2;t_0,x)\right|
            \geqslant
            2^{1/3}\varepsilon^{1/2}\log^4(1/\varepsilon)
        \right) \leqslant  Ce^{-c\log^{9/4}(1/\varepsilon)}.
    \end{align*}

