there exist constants $c_1(M,g),c_2(M,g)>0$ such that if $\Delta \varphi =-\lambda^2 \varphi$, then
\begin{equation} 
c_1(M,g)\le \frac{\mathcal{L}_{\varphi}(M)}{\lambda} \le c_2(M,g),
\end{equation}
where we recall Equation (equation eq:vol1 of the paper). (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

