[Theorem Theorem of strongly cases of arXiv:2605.20800, 'On the maximal displacement of subcritical branching random walk in random environment'] Under (subcritical of the paper) and (Jump Assumption of the paper), assume $\alpha>1$ and $\varTheta(1)<0$, which implies that $\Lambda_e(1)<0$ and 
		\begin{equation}
			\varTheta(1) = \Lambda_e^\prime(1)+\Lambda_s(\lambda_1)-\lambda_1\Lambda_s^\prime(\lambda_1) <0,
		\end{equation}
		where $\lambda_1$ satisfies $ \Lambda_e(1)+\Lambda_s(\lambda_1) =0 $.
		In addition, we impose the following integrability condition
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E}\left( e^{X_1-\Lambda_e(1)} \log_+ \eta_1\right)<\infty,
		\end{equation}
		where $\log_+ x = \log (\max\{x,1\})$.
		Then there exists some positive constant $C_1 \in (0,1]$, such that
		\begin{equation}
			\lim\limits_{x\rightarrow\infty}e^{\lambda_1 x }\mathbb{P}(M\geqslant x ) = C_1.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

