[Definition 33 (Martingale transform norm) of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Let $A$ be a real $m\times n$ matrix. For $1<p<\infty$, define the operator norm
of the martingale transform induced by $A$ on $L^p(\Omega)$ by
\begin{equation}
\|A\|_{L^p(\Omega)}
:=
\sup_{K\not\equiv 0}
\frac{\|A*M\|_p}{\|M\|_p},
\qquad
M_t=\int_0^t K_s\cdot dB_s,
\end{equation}
where $B_s$ is  $n$--dimensional Brownian motion and $K$ ranges over predictable
$\R^n$--valued processes with $\int_0^t |K_s|^2\,ds<\infty,$ a.s.

