body:
[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2609.02837, '2609.02837'] Let $\vec{x},\vec{y} \in \R^n$, and let $I$ be an open interval in $\R$ containing the entries of $\vec{x}$ and $\vec{y}$. If $f$ is increasing and convex on $I$, then
\begin{equation*}
\vec{x} \prec_{\w} \vec{y}
\quad\implies\quad
f(\vec{x}) \prec_{\w} f(\vec{y}).
\end{equation*}

