[Lemma 31 (Lemma 3.3 of \cite{ks}, with $k=1$) of arXiv:2511.07350, 'Decoupling of clusters in independent sets in a percolated hypercube'] For $p \in (0,1)$,
\begin{equation}
    \sum_{\substack{I \sse \Q \\ |[I \cap \cE]|, |[I \cap \cO]| > \fr{3}{4} 2^{d-1}}}
    \P[I \text{ is independent in } \Qp]
    \leq \E[\Cnt] \cdot \Exp{-\Omega(2^d/d)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2607.21392, 'Gaussian Convexity Principles for Sharp Moderate Deviations of Gaussian Maxima and Critica'] The function $\widehat{\mathcal K}_N$ is finite and convex on $\mathbb R$, and
\begin{equation}
\Var(\mathcal F_N)
\ge
\widehat{\mathcal K}_N(1)-\widehat{\mathcal K}_N(-2)-\widehat{\mathcal K}_N'(1).
\end{equation}
Furthermore,
\begin{equation}
\Var(\mathcal F_N)
\ge
\frac N4+\frac12\log\E\mathcal Z_N^{-2}-B_N(\beta_c).
\end{equation}

