[Definition of arXiv:2609.02041, 'Sparse $k$-AP Covering Sets and the Arithmetic Kakeya Conjecture'] A subset $A\subseteq \NN_0$ is \textbf{\textcolor{BrickRed}{\boldmath $k$-AP covering}}
if there exists $n_0$ such that for all $x>n_0$,
there exists $d\in\NN_0$ such that 
 $x-d, x-2d,\dots,x-(k-1)d$ are all in $A$.

[Lemma lemmas7.2 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] For every \(T<\infty\), we can find $C_T>0$ depending on $T,c_g,[g]_{C^\beta},\beta,s,p$ such that 

\begin{equation}
\mathbb P(\tau_*^n\le T)
\le C_Tr_*^{-p}\mathcal{E}_n\rightarrow0,\quad n\to\infty.

\end{equation}

