[Lemma l.rescaled_Schauder of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $z_0$.  Suppose $g$ solves~(equation eq:linear_kinetic of the paper) in $Q_2(z_0)$ with coefficients satisfying~(equation defn:coercivity_assumption of the paper)-(equation defn:bounded_coefficient_assumption of the paper). Suppose that $g \in L^\infty_m$ for some $m \in \mathbb R$.  Assume, further, that there exists $\alpha\in (0,1)$ with $\mathcal A, \mathcal B, \mathcal C \in C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_2(z_0))$.  Then
    \begin{equation}
        [g]_{C^{2,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_{\frac{r}{2}}(z_0))}
        \lesssim \frac{1
        + r^{2+\alpha} [\mathcal A]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_{2r}(z_0))}^\frac{2+\alpha}{\alpha}
        + r^\frac{\alpha(2+\alpha)}{1+\alpha} [\mathcal B]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_{2r}(z_0))}^\frac{2+\alpha}{1+\alpha}
        + r^\alpha [\mathcal C]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_{2r}(z_0))}
        }{r^{2+\alpha}\left\langle v_0 \right\rangle^{m - 3 - \frac{3\alpha}{2}}}\left\|g\right\|_{L^\infty_m}.
    \end{equation}
The implicit constant above depends on $\alpha$, $\lambda$, $\Lambda$, $[\mathcal A]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}}$, $[\mathcal B]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}}$, and $[\mathcal C]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}}$.  Recall that $\tilde r = r \left\langle v_0 \right\rangle^{-\nicefrac32}$ and $r = \min\{1,\nicefrac{\sqrt{t_0}}2\}$.

