[Theorem 16 (Fast regret of online sparse variational GP) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Under the same assumption of \cref{thm:gp-statistical}, the sparse variational GP computed by \cref{alg:gp} with $J \gtrsim T^{d/(d+2\fs)}$  satisfies
    \begin{equation}
    \fR\del[1]{(Q_t^{(J)})_{t=0}^{T-1}}
    \lesssim T^{d/(d+2\fs)}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:local_boltzmann_gibbs of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For $\varepsilon>0$, define the map $\iota_\varepsilon^0:[0, 1]\to[0, \infty)$ as in Proposition~(prop:uniqueness_neg of the paper), namely $\iota_\varepsilon^0(u):=\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\boldsymbol{1}_{(0,\varepsilon]}(u)$. If (equation assumption:g_bdd of the paper) holds, then for every $t>0$,
\begin{equation*}
    \mylim_{N\to\infty} \mathbb{E}_{\bar\nu_N }\left[\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\int_0^t\sum_{x=1}^N \iota_\varepsilon^0\left(\frac{x}{N}\right)\tau_x V_N(\eta_s)\de s\right)^2\right]=0.
\end{equation*}
The same result holds with $\iota_\varepsilon^0$ replaced by $\iota_\varepsilon^1$, where $\iota_\varepsilon^1(u):=\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\boldsymbol{1}_{[1-\varepsilon,1)}(u)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma priori-25-6-27-2 of arXiv:2609.01488, 'Stabilization by a background magnetic field: global well-posedness of the full compressib'] Assume that all the conditions of Lemma (priori-4 of the paper) hold. Then there is a positive constant $\epsilon_1<1$, depending only on $\mathbb T^3$, $|\mathbf n|$, $M$, $N$, $\mu$, $\lambda$, $\gamma$, $\bar P$, $\underline{\rho}^{-1}$, $\bar\rho$, $M_0$, $r$ and $c$, with the following property. If
\begin{equation}
M_\rho^{\frac12}\|(\mathbf u_0,p_0,\mathbf h_0)\|_M^{\frac{N-M-r-1}{N-M}}\leq \eta_1,
\end{equation}
holds for some $\eta_1\in(0,\epsilon_1]$, then for every $t\in[0,T]$ there hold
\begin{equation}
\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\rho\|^2_{M}\leq 2\|\rho_0\|_{M}^2,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\frac{2}{3}\underline{\rho}\leq\rho\leq\frac32\bar\rho,\ \ \text{in}\ \mathbb T^3\times[0,T],
\end{equation}
\begin{align}
\sup_{\tau\in[0,t]}\|\rho\|^2_{N}\leq A_7\Big(1+t\int_0^t\|\mathbf u\|_{N+1}^2d\tau \Big),
\end{align}
 where $A_7\sim\|\rho_0\|^2_{N}.$

