[Cor c.positivity of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] For any deterministic $ 0\leq f\inL(\Gamma_{[s,t]})$ that is not $\operatorname{Wein}_{[s,t]}$-a.e.\ zero,
\begin{align}

	M^\theta_{[s,t]} f > 0
	\quad
	\text{a.s.}
\end{align}
In particular, for any deterministic $ 0\leq g,g'\inL(\mathbb{R}^2)$ that are not Lebesgue-a.e.\ zero,
\begin{align}

	Z^\theta_{s,t} \ g \otimes g'
	:=
	\int_{\mathbb{R}^4} Z^{\theta}_{s,t}(\mathrm{d} x, \mathrm{d} x')\ g(x) \, g'(x') > 0
	\quad
	\text{a.s.}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

