[Lem lem_ballVolume of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] The volume $\sigma(\mathcal{B}_r^{\mathcal{M}_\kappa}(O))$ with respect to the Riemannian measure $\sigma$ of the geodesic ball with radius $0<r<\inj(\mathcal{M}_\kappa)$ in the $d$-dimensional model space $\mathcal{M}_\kappa$ satisfies:
    \begin{align}
        c~\varepsilon^d \leq \sigma(\mathcal{B}_\varepsilon^{\mathcal{M}_\kappa}(O)) \leq C ~ \varepsilon^{d}
    \end{align}
    for constants $c,C>0$ depending on $\kappa$ and $r$ and all $0<\varepsilon<r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma past of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] \textup{(Past convolution bound.)}
For every $1\leq \alpha<2$, $\beta\geq 1$, $0\leq r<t\leq T$ and
$y\in\mathbb R$, we have
\begin{equation}

\int_0^r\int_{\mathbb R}
[K^{(p)}_{r-s}(y-y')]^\alpha
[\Phi^{(p)}_{t-s,R}(y')]^\beta
dy'ds
\lesssim
\varphi_{p(t+r),R}(y).
