[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. For $\eps_*>0$ sufficiently small,
        \begin{align}
                |\Theta(z)|^2\lesssim|z-E_*| 
        \end{align}
        for $|z-E_*|<\eps_*$ and $\Im z\geq0$, and
        \begin{align}
                \Theta^2 =-\frac{\mu_1}{\mu_2}(z-E_*)+O(|z-E_*|^{3/2}). 
        \end{align}
        Moreover,
        \begin{align}
                \rho(E) =\frac1\pi\sqrt{\avg{\Pi_{*,22}^2}_N} \left(\frac{\mu_1}{|\mu_2|}\right)^{1/2}(E_*-E)^{1/2} +O(E_*-E) 
        \end{align}
        for $E\in(E_*-\eps_*,E_*)$, while $\rho(E)=0$ for $E\in(E_*,E_*+\eps_*)$.

