[Theorem th:ex-solution of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Denote $g_{t,x}(s,y):=  p(t-s,x-y)$ and $H:=\sum_{j=1}^{d} H_j$. If the condition
  \begin{align}
     \alpha+\dfrac{\alpha}{\beta}\min\left(\gamma+H_0-1,0\right)>d-H
  \end{align}
  holds, then $\Vert g_{t,x} \Vert_\mathcal{H}<\infty$ for any $t\in[0,T]$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$. In this case, (equation e:fde of the paper) has a  unique solution
  $\{u(t,x);(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^d\}$ given by
  \begin{equation}
    u(t,x)=  \int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} p(t-s,x-y)W(\ensuremath{ \mathrm{d}}  s,\ensuremath{ \mathrm{d}}  y).
  \end{equation}

