[Lemma 4 ({\cite[Lemma~4.1) of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] {moench2026horizonProblem}}]

Let \(K\subset\mathbb R\setminus\{0\}\) be compact.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \PP(B_s>0\text{ for every }s\in K)>0.

\end{equation}
Fix \(t\neq0\), and let
\begin{equation}
  \xi_s^{(t)}
  :=B_s-\frac{K_H(s,t)}{|t|^{2H}}B_t

\end{equation}
be the centred fractional Brownian bridge obtained by conditioning at \(t\).
If in addition
\(t\notin K\), then
\begin{equation}
  \PP(\xi_s^{(t)}>0\text{ for every }s\in K)>0.

\end{equation}
The same assertions hold with all signs reversed. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lmm lmmObsInterpolationDyadic of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] Assume that $A, \delta>0$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}$.
Denote $D_{n} = \left\{k/2^n \, : \, k\in \mathbb{Z} \right\} \cap (x-\delta, x+\delta)$. 
Let $\mathrm{A}_n$ be the event
\begin{multline}
\mathrm{A}_n = \Biggl\{f \in C^1_{0,+}(\mathbb{R}) \, :\, \Big| \, \log \left[\obs{f}{s}{t}_{0}\right]+\log |t-s|\, \Big| < A \, |t-s|^{\alpha}, \\
\text{for all } s,t\in D_{n} \text{ such that } |t-s| \leq 100 \cdot 2^{-n/2} 
\Biggl\}.
\end{multline}
Then there exists $B=B(A, \delta, \alpha)>0$ such that for any $N>0$, there exists $\varepsilon=\varepsilon(N, A, \delta, \alpha)>0$ for which
\begin{equation}
\mathsf{LocH\ddot{o}lObs}^{\,\alpha} \! \left(x, \varepsilon, B \right) \supset (\cap_{n \geq N} \, \mathrm{A}_n).
\end{equation}

