[Lemma lem:omega-prop of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] We have, for each $m \in \mathbb{N}_0$,
\begin{equation}
\alpha_x \le \pi_x(m)\left(\alpha_x+m\right) = \pi_x(m+1) \left(m+1\right) \le \alpha_x\,e^{\alpha_x\sum_{j=1}^m \frac1j} \; \text{.}
\end{equation}
Moreover, for $m \ge m' \ge 1$,
\begin{equation}
1 \le \frac{ \pi_x(m)\,m } { \pi_x(m')\,m' }  \le e^{\alpha_x \sum_{j=m'}^{m-1}\frac1j}  \; \text{.}
\end{equation}

