body:
[Lemma lem:auc-min-vs-max:variance-difference of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] The difference between the variances of
  the two maximum AUC estimators
  $\widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*_1}$ and $\widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*_2}$
  is given by
  \begin{equation}
  \Var{\widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*_2}} - \Var{\widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*_1}}
  =
  \frac{1 - 2 \theta}{\theta^2 (1 - \theta)^2 n} 
  \E{\zeta |\zeta - \zeta'|}
  -
  \frac{1}{\theta^2 (1 - \theta)^2 n (n - 1)} 
  \E{\zeta \zeta' |\zeta - \zeta'|}
  \text{.}
  \end{equation}

