[Theorem thm:convergence-convex of arXiv:2608.29507, 'Denoising as Projection: Constrained Optimization with Gradient-Guided Diffusion'] Let Assumption~(assump:data-convex of the paper) and the assumptions of
Lemma~(lemma:one-step-descent-convex of the paper) hold. Consider the update in
(equation eq:projected-gradient-guidance-relaxed of the paper). Then, with $\rho$, $B_1$,
$B_2$, $M_\eta$, and $C_\eta$ defined as in
Lemma~(lemma:one-step-descent-convex of the paper), we have
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal V_0
    &\textstyle \le
    \rho^T\mathcal V_T+
    \left(
        B_1\|n_T\|
        +
        \epsilon M_\eta C_{\mathcal X}\sigma_T
    \right)
    \frac{
        \rho^T-(1-\epsilon)^T
    }{
        \rho-(1-\epsilon)
    }+
    \left(
        B_2\|n_T\|^2
        +
        2\epsilon^2C_\eta C_{\mathcal X}^2\sigma_T^2
    \right)
    \frac{
        \rho^T-(1-\epsilon)^{2T}
    }{
        \rho-(1-\epsilon)^2
    }.
\end{align*}
Consequently,
\begin{align*}
     \|p_0\!-\!x^\star\|^2
    &\textstyle\!\le\!
    2\eta
    \Bigg[\!
        \rho^T\mathcal V_T\!+\!
        \left(
            B_1\|n_T\|
            \!+\!
            \epsilon M_\eta C_{\mathcal X}\sigma_T
        \right)
        \frac{
            \rho^T\!\!-\!(1\!-\!\epsilon)^T
        }{
            \rho-(1\!-\!\epsilon)
        }\!+\!
        \left(
            B_2\|n_T\|^2
           \! + \!
            2\epsilon^2C_\eta C_{\mathcal X}^2\sigma_T^2
        \right)
        \frac{
            \rho^T\!-\!(1\!-\!\epsilon)^{2T}
        }{
            \rho-(1-\epsilon)^2
        }
    \!\Bigg]\!.
\end{align*}
Moreover,~
    $\|n_0\|
    \le
    (1-\epsilon)^T\|n_T\|.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

