[Lemma lem2.3 of arXiv:2411.13266, '\bf A new maximal regularity for parabolic equations and an application'] Let ${\mathcal K}$ satisfy conditions (i) and (ii) of Definition (def2.2 of the paper) and $\{{\mathbb Q}_k,\ k\in{\mathbb Z}\}$ be the filtration of dyadic cubes. Assume that ${\mathcal K}(t,r)$  is weakly differentiable in $r$ for $r\neq t$ and $\|\partial_r{\mathcal K}(t,r)\|_{L({\mathcal H};\widetilde{{\mathcal H}})}\leqslant C\phi(|t-r|)$ for all $r\neq t$, with a constant $C$ independent of $t,r$ and a function $\phi$ satisfying
\begin{eqnarray}
\iota\int\limits_\iota^{+\infty} \phi(\tau)d\tau\leqslant C<+\infty
\end{eqnarray}
for all $\iota>0$. Then ${\mathcal K}$ is an $L({\mathcal H};\widetilde{{\mathcal H}})$-valued Calder\'{o}n--Zygmund kernel relative to the filtration of dyadic cubes with constant $C_0$ in ((2.1 of the paper)) depending only on $C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

