[Definition eq:H+H- of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For $\alpha \in [0,1]$ and $H \in (0,1)$, we set
\begin{equation}
H_\alpha^+ := (1+\alpha)H \quad \text{ and } \quad H_\alpha^- := (1-\alpha)H    
\end{equation} 
and we define the Gaussian field $\{X^{\alpha,H}_{(x_1,x_2)}\}_{(x_1,x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2}$ by 
\begin{equation}
X^{\alpha,H}_{(x_1,x_2)} :=  \int_{\mathbb{R}^2}  \frac{(e^{i x_1 \xi_1}-1) (e^{i x_2 \xi_2}-1)}{\phi_{\alpha,H}(\xi_1,\xi_2)}  d\hat{\bf{W}}({\boldsymbol{\xi}}) 
\end{equation}
where the function
\[\phi_{\alpha,H}(\xi_1,\xi_2)=\min(\vert \xi_1 \vert, \vert \xi_2 \vert)^{H_\alpha^- +\frac{1}{2}}\max (\vert \xi_1 \vert, \vert \xi_2 \vert)^{H_\alpha^++\frac{1}{2} }\]
denotes the square root of the inverse of the spectral density of the field.

