body:
[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.06392, '2608.06392'] Let the assumptions of {\hyperref[AISRTh4]{Theorem~\ref{AISRTh4}}} hold, and suppose further that
    the inter-arrival distribution $F$ admits a density $f$. Assume, in addition, that the remainder
    $u(t)-{1/\mu}$ is ultimately monotone as $t\to\infty$. Then the renewal density $u(t)$
    admits the asymptotic representation
\begin{equation}
    u(t)=\frac{1}{\,\mu\,}+\frac{1}{\mu^2}\,\frac{L_2(t)}{t}
    \qquad \text{as} \quad t\to\infty,
\end{equation}
    where $L_2(t)\big/L(t)\to1$ as $t\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

