body:
[Lemma lem:ber-auc:bound:auc:bernstein of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For any
  $\delta \in (0, 1)$
  and
  $n \geq \frac{\log (2/\delta)}{9 \theta (1 - \theta)}$,
  with probability at least $1 - \delta$,
  it holds that
  \begin{equation}
    \abs{
      \widetilde{\mathrm{AUC}^*}
      -
      \mathrm{AUC}^*
    }
    \leq
    \abs{
      \widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*}
      -
      \mathrm{AUC}^*
    }
    \leq
    \sqrt{
      \frac{\log (2/\delta)}{\theta (1 - \theta) n}
    }
    \text{.}
  \end{equation}

