[Lem second_moment_interpol of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with $\int \xi(\Lambda_1)^2\mathsf{P}_i(d\xi)<\infty$ and  $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1).$ Set $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$ and  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$. Then for $0\leq t\leq 1$ and $n\in \IN$ 
    \begin{align*}
        \int \xi(\Lambda_n)^2\mathsf{P}_t(d\xi)\leq (1-t)\int \xi(\Lambda_n)^2\mathsf{P}_0(d\xi)+ t\int \xi(\Lambda_n)^2\mathsf{P}_1(\xi).
    \end{align*}

[Lemma lemma_fin_deg_to_unim of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Fix~$d \ge 2$. For~$G \in \{ \mathcal{G}_\mathrm{SGil}, \mathcal{G}_\mathrm{Del}, \mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab}$\} we have that
