[Prop two-pt classification of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta > 0$. Assume that for every pair of neighbours $x,y \in \mathbb Z^d$,
\begin{equation} 
\langle \tau_x \tau_y\rangle_\beta^+ = \langle \tau_x \tau_y \rangle_\beta. 
\end{equation}
Then,
\begin{equation}
\Psi^1_\beta = \Psi^0_\beta.
\end{equation}

[Prop EHI:p:EHIbigm2 of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$, satisfying (equation EHI:e:regularJumps of the paper). Suppose there exist $c>0$, and a set $E \subseteq (0, \infty)$ such that
    \begin{equation} 
        m_2(r) \geq c r^2 \lambda(r) \qquad\mbox{for all $r \in E$}.
    \end{equation}
    Let $L_{(EHI:l:G0lowerbound of the paper)}$ be the constant from Lemma (EHI:l:G0lowerbound of the paper). For all $L \geq L_{(EHI:l:G0lowerbound of the paper)}$ and $M>1$, if $S :=  \bigcup_{r \in E} [100Lr, 100MLr]$, then $X$ satisfies $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \in S)$.

