[Lemma 20 (Summability of \(\Theta_j(h)\)) of arXiv:2609.01436, '2609.01436'] For every fixed $h>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \omega_k(h)
 \asymp_{h,\eta}
 b_0^{-1/2}(1+k)
 \varepsilon_k^{(1-\eta)/2}
 \qquad \text{as }k\to\infty.
\end{equation}
Consequently, if $\eta<1$, then for every $j\geq k_0$,
