{"artifact_digest":"sha256:68318555edbdcaa5b7e7e0ab9c5beb088cb910d62732df3ff87fe8d478243ccd","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/68/68318555edbdcaa5b7e7e0ab9c5beb088cb910d62732df3ff87fe8d478243ccd.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:4fdcb3f1e4e754bd3175d7ee52ddc467eda8b3e5280ec6e96db3321d262dff1d","bundle_entry_key":"2607-06242-lemma-29-lem-29","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_065","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_065.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-06242-lem-29-lem-29","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The proof is parallel to the Navier--Stokes case, with $\mathcal E$ replacing $\|u\|^2$. Put $f(\sigma):=1+\|F(\sigma)\|^2$ and $\gamma:=\frac{c_0}{2}.$
  By \eqref{e.060404}, one has
  \begin{align*}
    \|Q(\sigma)\|_{\mathcal L_2(\Rb^{\mathbf d},H)}^2\leq \mathbf d Q_{0,\infty}^2,\qquad m\text{-a.s.}.
  \end{align*}
  From \eqref{e.060410},
  \begin{align}
    d\mathcal E(U(t))+c_0\mathcal E(U(t))dt\leq C f(\beta_t\sigma)dt+C\eps dt+dM_t,
  \end{align}
  and
  \begin{align}
