body:
[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Let $P_{u_1},P_{u_2}$ be two smooth, volume-preserving diffeomorphisms on $\TT^2$, and $\tau_{u_1},\tau_{u_2}$ two non-negative smooth functions. Then, there exists $k\in\NN$, and a constant $C>0$ depending only on $P_{u_1}, \tau_{u_1},\|P_{u_1}-P_{u_2}\|_{C^k}, \|P_{u_1}^{-1}-P_{u_2}^{-1}\|_{C^k}$ and $\|\tau_{u_1}-\tau_{u_2}\|_{C^k}$, so that 
\begin{align*}
&\left \|\begin{pmatrix}
DP_{u_1}(P_{u_1}^{-1}) & 0 \\
-D \tau_{u_1}(P_{u_1}^{-1}) & 1
\end{pmatrix} B(P_{u_1}^{-1})- \begin{pmatrix}
DP_{u_2}(P_{u_2}^{-1}) & 0 \\
-D \tau_{u_2}(P_{u_2}^{-1}) & 1
\end{pmatrix} B(P_{u_2}^{-1})\right \|_{\mathcal Y}\\
&\leq C(\|P_{u_1}-P_{u_2}\|^{\delta}_{C^k}+\|\tau_{u_1}-\tau_{u_2}\|_{C^k}+\|P_{u_1}^{-1}-P_{u_2}^{-1}\|^{\delta}_{C^k})\|B\|_{\mathcal X}.
\end{align*}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b073f77079d24e234cb7b4264fa134aa053cce76b3beb275276bab1ab614ebba","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b0/b073f77079d24e234cb7b4264fa134aa053cce76b3beb275276bab1ab614ebba.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1487614b8e47ab623233c0ea96fc1e3c580d2cc695216aa8441be660cf051550","bundle_entry_key":"2609-04153-lemma-31-first-perturbation-u","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_169","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_169.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-04153-lemma-31-first-perturbation-u","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Write $B=\overline B+(b,b_v)$. We begin by estimating the first two components. Recall crucially that $(\Id-\PP) (DP_u \PP b)\circ P_u^{-1}=0$ for any volume-preserving diffeomorphism $P_u$. Hence, the only contribution that must be estimated in positive regularity is 
