[Lemma Lem: 1226 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Given $X_1,X_2\in \mathcal{H}^d$ on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$, let $\Gamma_i$ such that $X_i\sim \Gamma_i$, $i=1,2$. For any $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with Lipschitz constant $l_\phi$, define $v_i(t,x):=\sup_{y\in \Gamma_i}\phi(x+ty)$, $i=1,2$. Then for any $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_+\times \mathbb R^d$,
		\begin{equation*}
			|v_1(t,x)-v_2(t,x)|\leq tl_{\phi}\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_1-X_2|].
		\end{equation*}

