[Theorem 110 (cf. Theorem \ref{T:length} and {\cite[Theorem 1.4) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {Mak24}}]
Let $K_n$ be the complete graph and assume that $(\omega_e)_{e \in E}$ are independently uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$. Then for $\beta = \beta(n)$, we have with high probability (and in $\P$-expectation) that
\begin{equation*}
        \bE^\omega_{n,\beta}\big[ L(\cT) \big] = 
        \begin{dcases}
             (1 + o(1)) \frac{n}{\beta} \cdot \frac{1 - \beta e^{-\beta} - e^{-\beta}}{1- e^{-\beta}} & \text{ if } 0 < \beta \ll n/\log n, \\
            (1 + o(1)) \zeta(3) & \text{ if } \beta \gg n (\log n)^5,
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation*}
    where $\zeta(3) = \sum_{k=1}^\infty k^{-3} = 1.202\dots$ is Apéry's constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

