body:
[Theorem 5 (Polymers starting uniformly from a small ball) of arXiv:2608.13359, 'Fractional moments of the Stochastic Heat Flow and\\2D Directed Polymers'] There are constants \(c,C>0\) such that, for all \(p\in (0,1)\) all \(N\in \N\), 
  all \(\beta\in (0,1)\), and all \(0\leq R \leq \sqrt{N}\), we have
  \begin{equation}

    \EE\bigl[ Z_{N}^{\beta,\w}(U_R)^p \bigr]
    \leq C\, \EE\bigl[ Z_{N}^{\beta,\w}(U_R)^2 \bigr]^{c\, p(p-1)} \,  .
  \end{equation}
  More explicitly, let \(\th(N,\beta)\) be defined as in \eqref{def:theta-N-beta}.
  Then there are constants \(c',C'\) such that, for all \(p\in (0,1)\), all \(N\in \N\), all \(\beta\in (0,1)\), and all \(0\leq R \leq \sqrt{N}\), we have
  \begin{equation}

    \EE\bigl[ Z_{N}^{\beta,\w}(U_R)^p \bigr]
    \leq C'\, \Bigl(1+\log \Bigl(1+\frac{N}{1+R^2}\Bigr)\, \cV\bigl(\e^{\th(N,\beta)}\bigr) \Bigr)^{c'\, p(p-1)} \,,
  \end{equation}
  where \(\cV(T) \coloneqq \int_0^{\infty} \frac{T^s}{\Gamma(s+1)} \dd s\) is the Volterra function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 41 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] Let $(w_{N})_{N \in \N}$ and $(z_{N})_{N \in \N}$ be two sequences in $L^{1}(\R^{d}\times[a,b])$ which have an approximate temporal modulus of continuity $\om$. Then for all compact $D \subset \R^{d}$, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\norm{w_{N} - z_{N}}_{L^{1}(D\times (a,b))} \xrightarrow{} 0 \text{ if and only if, for all } t \in [a,b], \norm{w_{N}(\cdot,t) - z_{N}(\cdot,t)}_{L^{1}(D)} \xrightarrow{} 0.
	\end{equation*}

