\(|\alpha| + |\beta| + j\leqslant s\),
\begin{equation*}
  \bigl| \partial_a^\alpha\partial_\theta^\beta
  \partial_\sigma^j F(\zeta;a,\varphi(\theta),\sigma) \bigr|
  \leqslant C_{\alpha,\beta,j} (1+\|\zeta\|^n) \Gamma_{c_0}(\zeta;a).
\end{equation*}
By (lem:admissibility_of_growing_cutoff of the paper), derivatives of \(1-\vartheta_\sigma\) satisfy
polynomial bounds. More precisely, every term produced by Leibniz' rule in an admissible derivative
