[Theorem thm:main-finite-r-annular of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Let \(0<s<1\), \(r>1\), and \(\delta>0\).  Let \(U\ge0\) satisfy \(\mathbb{E} U=1\) and (equation eq:finite-r-witnessed-gap of the paper).  Then there exist constants \(C,c,\eta>0\), depending only on \(s,r,\delta\) and the law of \(U\), such that, for every \(n\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(
\sup_{2^n\le \lvert\xi\rvert\le 2^{n+1}}
\lvert\widehat{\nu_\circ}(\xi)\rvert>C2^{-sn/2}
\right)
\le
C\exp(-c2^{\eta n})+C2^{-cn}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
\lvert\widehat{\nu_\circ}(\xi)\rvert=O(\lvert\xi\rvert^{-s/2})
\qquad (\lvert\xi\rvert\to\infty)
\end{equation}
almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

