[Proposition 4 (One-block contraction) of arXiv:2608.29501, 'Disorder Thresholds and Free Energy of Brownian Directed Polymers with\\ Product and Radia'] The constants \(K,R,A\) can be chosen, independently of \(\beta\), so
that there exist \(\rho<1\) and \(\beta_0>0\) satisfying
\begin{equation*}
  \rho_\beta\le\rho,
  \qquad 0<\beta\le\beta_0.
\end{equation*}

