[Corollary 30 (Gamma limit) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] For every $\xi\in E_\eta$,
\begin{equation}

    Q_R(\xi)
    \dto \frac{s_\eta(\xi)}{q}\,\Gamma(q,1).
\end{equation}
Here $\Gamma(q,1)$ has shape $q$ and scale $1$; its mean and variance are both
$q$. If $\eta$ is a point process of positive intensity, then
\begin{equation}

    \frac{Q_R(\xi)}{\rho_\eta}
    \dto \frac{S_\eta(\xi)}{q}\,\Gamma(q,1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

