[Definition def: Skorohod-l2 of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Suppose $u\in L^2(\Xi;\mathcal{H})$, that is, $u$ is an $\mathcal{H}$-valued square-integrable random variable. We say that  $u$ is ($L^2$-)Skorohod integrable  if there exists an $L^2$-integrable random variable denoted by $\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)$ such that for any $F\in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)F\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\langle DF, u\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\right] 
\end{align}
with $|\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)F\right]|\leq c\Vert F\Vert_{L^2({\mathbb P})}$, where $c$ is a constant depending on u. We call $\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)$ the $L^2$-Skorohod integral of $u$ or the divergence of $u$.

[Lemma lemma_steinmethod_xlessthanl_gendif of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Fix  $x\leq \ell$ and $k\in \mathbb{N}$. Let the function $h$ in the ODE (equation equation_stein of the paper) be 
    \begin{align*}
        h(y):=\mathds{1}_{\{y\leq x\}}\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)},\quad y\in \mathbb{R}\setminus \left\{y\in(-\infty,x]:b(y)=0 \right\}.
    \end{align*} 
Then a solution $g_x: \mathbb{R}\setminus \brac{\left\{y\in(\ell,u)^\complement:a(y)=0 \right\}\cup\left\{y\in(\ell,u)\cup (-\infty,x]:b(y)=0 \right\}}\to\mathbb{R}$ to (equation equation_stein of the paper) exists and satisfies for every $y$ in its domain, 
\begin{align}
     \left\vert  g_x(y) \right\rvert&\leq \mathcal{V}_3(y):= \mathds{1}_{\{y\leq \ell\}} \frac{\left\vert -2a(y)+b'(y) \right\rvert}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert\left\vert 2a(y) \right\rvert }\,;  
    \end{align}
and
\begin{align}
    \left\vert  g'_x(y) \right\rvert&\leq \mathcal{V}_4(y):= \mathds{1}_{\{y\leq \ell\} } \brac{\abs{\frac{(1+b''(y))b(y)-(-2a(y)+b'(y))b'(y) }{b(y)^2a(y)}}+\abs{\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)4a(y)^2} }}. 
\end{align}

