[Proposition thm:cluster-process of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let   $ \mathsf{S}$ the spectral measure of $ \mathsf{P}$ . Assume $\mathbf E \#\mathsf{P}_{ 1}^{ 2}<\infty  $. Let the random Fourier-Stieljes transform $ \varphi (u) = \int_{}e^{ iu\cdot t}d\mathsf{P}_{ 1}(t)$. Then $ \mathsf{P}^{ \mu }$ is locally square integrable and has the spectral measure 
\begin{align*}
 \mathsf{S}_{ \mu } = \left(
\mathbf E  | \varphi (u) | ^{ 2}- | \mathbf E \varphi (u) | ^{ 2}
\right)\Leb(du) + \mathbf E  | \varphi (u) |^{ 2} \mathsf{S}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

