[Lemma LEM:coer2 of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] There exists $\lambda_0, d_0>0$ such that, under the separation condition $\min_{i \neq j}|\xi_i-\xi_j| \ge d_0$, the coercivity 
\begin{align*}
\jb{\mathcal{L}_{\xi_1,\dots, \xi_k}v,v }_{L^2(\mathbb{R})}  \ge \lambda_0  \| v\|_{H^1(\mathbb{R})}^2  
\end{align*}

\noindent
holds for every $v \in H^1(\mathbb{R})$  with $\jb{v,  \partial_{\xi_j} m_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k} }_{L^2(\mathbb{R})}=0$, $j=1,\dots, k$.

[Theorem T:polar:suff of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Let Assumptions (a:X of the paper) and (a:var of the paper) hold. If
\begin{align}
\lim_{r\to 0^+} \frac{r^N}{\sigma^d\left(r\left( \log\log\frac{1}{r}\right)^{-1/N}\right)} = \infty,
\end{align}
then points are polar for $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma L:PXLB of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Let $\varepsilon \in (0, \delta_0)$ and $n = 2^p$, where $p \ge 1$. For $0 \le k < p$, let $F_k = \{t_1, \dots, t_{2^k}\}$.
Suppose $\sigma(|t_1|) \ge c_0 2^{-p}\varepsilon$ and $\sigma(d(t_i, F_k)) \ge c_0 2^{k-p} \varepsilon$ for $0 \le k < p$ and $2^k < i \le 2^{k+1}$.
Then there exists a positive constant $C$ such that for all $p \ge 1$,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb P}\left\{ |X(t_i)| \le \varepsilon \text{ for all } i \le n \right\} \ge C^n \varepsilon^{nd} \frac{1}{\sigma^d(|t_1|)} \prod_{0 \le k < p} \prod_{2^k < i \le 2^{k+1}} \frac{1}{\sigma^d(d(t_i, F_k))}.
\end{align}

