[Lem harmonic of arXiv:2411.08796, 'Optimal stopping for Markov processes \\ with positive jumps'] For any Borel set $B$, the Green kernel satisfies;
\begin{equation*}
G_{\alpha}(x,H)=\Ex{x}{\ea{\mathpzc{h}_{B}}G_{\alpha}(X_{\mathpzc{h}_{B}},H )},
\end{equation*}
for all $x$ in $\mathds{R}$ and for all Borel set $H\subseteq B$.

In other words, for every $x\in \mathds{R}$, both $G_{\alpha}(x,dy)$ and $\Ex{x}{\ea{\mathpzc{h}_{B}}G_{\alpha}(X_{\mathpzc{h}_{B}},dy)}$, are the same measure in $B$.

