body:
[Thm GirsanovHTransform of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume that \textup{(Assumption:SDEsolution of the paper)} holds for the SDE (equation ReferenceLevyIto of the paper) and $(\left\{ X_t \right\}_{[0,T]},\mathbf{P})$ is the solution to (equation ReferenceLevyIto of the paper) that is a strong Markov process with $X_0\sim\rho_0$. Let $h$ be a non-negative harmonic function and satisfies the mean-value property (equation Equation:MeanValueProperty of the paper). 
    Let $\left\{ Z_t \right\}_{[0,T]}$ be the process given by 

    \begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned} Z_t:=\exp\bigg(-\int_0^tu(s)dB_s-\frac{1}{2}\int_0^t&|u(s)|^2ds+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}^\ell}\log(1-\theta(s,z))\tilde{N}(ds,dz) \\    &+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}^\ell}\left[\log(1-\theta(s,z))+\theta(s,z)\right]\nu(dz)ds\bigg)
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
     with
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{cases}
            u(t):=-\mathbbm{1}_{\set{\tau_n^0\geq t\textup{ ev.}}}\sigma^T\nabla\log h(t,X_{t})\textup{ for }t\in[0,T], \\
            \displaystyle \theta(t,z) := 1-\mathbbm{1}_{\set{\tau_n^0\geq t\textup{ ev.}}}\frac{h(t,X_{t-}+\gamma(t,X_{t-},z))}{h(t,X_{t-})}\textup{ for }t\in[0,T],\,z\in\mathbb{R}^\ell,
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation}  
    where  $\set{\tau_n^0\geq t\textup{ ev.}}:=\bigcup_{n\geq 1}\left\{ \tau_n^0\geq t \right\}$ for $\left\{ \tau_n^0 \right\}_{n\geq 1}$ being the sequence of stopping times defined in (equation def_tau_n of the paper). Then, $\left\{ Z_t \right\}_{[0,T]}$ is a $\left\{ \mathcal F_t \right\}$-local-martingale under $\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ X_0\in A_0 \right\}}}{r_0}\mathbf{P}$. 

   Further, if $\mathbf{P}^h$ is the $h$-transform of $\mathbf{P}$ as defined in (equation Definition:h-transform,general case with tau0 of the paper), then \begin{equation}  \mathbf{P}^h=Z_T\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ \tau_0>T \right\}}}{r_0}\mathbf{P}.
    \end{equation}
   Hence if $\mathbf{P}(\tau^0>T)=r_0$, then $\mathbf{P}^h$ is the Girsanov transform of $\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ \tau^0>T \right\}}}{r_0}\mathbf{P}$ with the above coefficients $u(t),\theta(t,z)$.

