[Lemma exp of arXiv:2411.17104, 'Two-barriers-reflected BSDE with Rank-based Data'] For any fixed positive constant $A$, there is a positive $C$ and a function $\phi (x):=(\frac{1}{2}\log(1+|x|^{2})+1)^{2}$ such that
 \begin{equation}

 \psi(t,x):=e^{(A+C(T-t))\phi (x)},
 \end{equation}
satisfies
\begin{equation*}
-\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial t}(t,x)-
\mathcal{L}\psi(t,x)-c\big(\psi(t,x)+|\sigma \triangledown \psi(t,x) |\big)>0, \quad (t,x)\in [t_{1},T]\times \Pi^{n},
\end{equation*}
in which $c$ is the Lipschitz constant of $G$ and $t_{1}:=(T-\frac{A}{C})^{+}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop prop_no_g2 of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] There exists a consistent APS $S$ satisfying the following conditions:
