[Lem 11 of arXiv:2603.05174, 'Regularization of the superposition principle: Potential theory meets Fokker-Planck equati'] Assume that conditions $\mathbf{H_{a,b}^{\sqrt{u}}}$ and $\mathbf{H_{\sf \lesssim u}}$ are fulfilled. 
Also, let $\left(\nu_t:=v(t,x)dx\right)_{t\in [0,N)}\subset \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be a weakly continuous solution to the linear Fokker-Planck equation \eqref{eq:LFPshort} on $[0,N)$ such that  $v\in\mathcal{A}_{\lesssim u}^{0,N}$.
Then for every $0<s<N<\infty$ we have the identification
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}^N_{\delta_s\otimes \nu_s}\circ \left(X_2^N(t)\right)^{-1}= \nu_{t+s}, \quad 0\leq t<N-s.
    \end{equation}
Moreover, there exists a unique solution $\eta^N\in\mathcal{P}\left(C([0,N];\mathbb{R}^d)\right)$ to the canonical MP associated to $\left({\sf L}_t\right)_{t\in [0,T]}$ such that for every $\varepsilon\in (0,N)$
\begin{equation*}
    \eta^N|_{C([\varepsilon,N);\mathbb{R}^d)}=\mathbb{P}^N_{\delta_\varepsilon\otimes \nu_\varepsilon}\circ \left[\left(X_2^N(t-\varepsilon)\right)_{t\in[\varepsilon, N)}\right]^{-1} \quad \mbox{as distributions on } C([\varepsilon,N);\mathbb{R}^d).
\end{equation*}

