body:
[Lemma le:laplace-tail-bound2 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ c, q \in (0,\infty) $, $ \beta \in (0, 1) $, $ n_0, n \in {\mathbb N} $ with $ n_0 < n $.
Let $ V_n^* $ be a nonnegative random variable which satisfies for all $ \lambda \in [0,\infty) $ that
\bas{
  - \ln
  \mathbb{E}\bigl[
    e^{ - \lambda V_n^* }
  \bigr]
  \ge
  \sum_{ k = n_0 + 1 }^n
  \min\Bigl\{ q, c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \Bigr\} .
}
Then 
\bas{
{\mathbb P}\Bigl(V_n^*\le \frac c2\,\frac{1-\beta^{n-n_0}}{1-\beta^n}\Bigr)
\le \exp\Bigl(-\frac q2\,\frac{1-\beta^{n-n_0}}{1-\beta}\Bigr).
}
If, in addition, $n-n_0\ge \frac12(1-\beta)^{-1}$, then
\bas{
{\mathbb P}\Bigl(V_n^*\le \frac c2\,(1-e^{-1/2})\Bigr)
\le \exp\Bigl(-\frac q2\,\frac{1-e^{-1/2}}{1-\beta}\Bigr).
}

