[Proposition condition_explained of arXiv:2608.13716, 'Graph Causal Optimal Transport \\ and Wasserstein Distances'] Let $G$ be a sorted DAG. Then the following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*)]
        \item $G$ is perfect;
        \item For all $i, j \in V$ such that $i \in \mathrm{pa}_{j}$, we have that $i$ is an ancestor of $j$ in $\mathrm{prox}(G)$ and $i \in \mathrm{pa}_{v}$ for all vertices $v \neq i$ of the proximal path between $i$ and $j$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Let $T\leq\infty$. There exists a lower semicontinuous function $b_T:[0,T)\to[1/2,1]$ such that the continuation region is given by
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{C}_T=\{(t,x)\in\mathcal{S}_T : 1-b_T(t)<x<b_T(t)\}.
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, $b_T(t)\geq\gamma(t)$ for any $t\in[0,T)$.

