[Lemma lem: adding external field in sle continuity of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $\mathcal{F}_i$ be the
$\sigma$-algebra generated by $H^i$.

There exists a constant $c_3>0$  

such that for any $1\le i\le n$, we have \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb{P}}\Big(\max\{|\mathsf{a}_i|,|\mathsf{a}_i^+|,|\mathsf{a}_i^-|\}\ge \frac{1}{2}\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\Big)\le c_3^{-1}\exp\Big(-c_3\big({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}}\big)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\Big).
\end{equation}
In addition, we have \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb{E}}\Big(\max\{|\mathsf{a}_i|,|\mathsf{a}_i^+|,|\mathsf{a}_i^-|\}\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\Big)\le 1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2506.22213, 'No arbitrage assumption implies the differentiability of derivative pricing function'] Assume that $f(t,X_t)=A_t+M_t$ is a semimartingale with finite variation process $A$ and local martingale $M$ satisfying:
\begin{align}
	\bbE\edg{( Var A)_T^2+\ang{M}}<\infty
\end{align}

     for any $T$, and that $X$ satisfies Assumption \ref{sde assumption} and \ref{differentiable assumption}.  Then $f(t,X_t)$ is Malliavin differentiable, that is for almost every $t$, $f(t,X_t)\in\bbD^{1,2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2605.04168, 'Error analysis for learning fractional stochastic differential equations with applications'] Let $s,s_2\in (0,1)$ be arbitrary. Let $q>\frac{d}{1-s}$ and $q_2 > \frac{1}{1-s_2}$. Suppose $\sigma$ is supported on a compact set $[0,T] \times \mathcal{K}$ and that partial weak derivatives exists.     
    Then we have 
   \begin{align*}
       |\sigma(r,x)-\sigma(u,z)| &\lesssim |x-z|^{s} \left[\Vert\partial_t\nabla_z\sigma\Vert_{(q_2,q)} + \Vert\nabla_z\sigma\Vert_{(q_2,q)}\right] \\
       &+|r-u|^{s_2}\left[ \Vert\partial_t\nabla_z\sigma\Vert_{(q_2,q)}+ \Vert\partial_t\sigma\Vert_{(q_2,q)}\right].
   \end{align*}

