[Lemma lem:lienIetR of arXiv:2606.24793, '\LARGE Random sequential nearest-neighbor coloring on trees'] For any $n\ge 1$, we have the following properties:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $W_n$ is a connected subset of $\mathcal{T}$. 
        \item $\mathcal{T}_{V_n}\cap W_n=\{V_n\}$. 
    \end{itemize} Moreover, for any $n\ge 2$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{I_n}{K+1}\le K^{R_n}\le K I_n.
    \end{equation}

[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] For any $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$, the $L^{p}$-spectral radii $\lambda_{p}(\theta\mu)$ are independent of $p \in [1, \infty]$. That is, we have
  \begin{align*}
    -\lambda_{\infty}(\theta\mu) = -\lambda_{2}(\theta\mu) = C(\theta).
  \end{align*}

[Lemma l:65 of arXiv:2508.21658, 'Infinite-dimensional stochastic differential equations for Coulomb random point fields'] We obtain 
