[Lemma lem:perc_diagram-p1 of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 11$, 
$p \le p_c$, $\mu \in {\mathbb R^d}$, and $a\in [0,\frac{d-4}2)$.
Suppose there are constants $r < 1$ and $\kappa >0$ such that
\begin{equation} 
e^{\norm \mu_\infty}
\tilde {\sf T}^{(\mu)}(p)
	(1 + 2 {\sf T}^{(\mu)}(p) )
	\le r < 1
\end{equation}
Then
there is a constant $K_{a,1}$ (depending on $r, \kappa$) such that
\begin{equation} 
\bignorm{ \abs x^a  \Pi_p ^{(\mu)}(x) }_1  \; \le  K_{a,1} .
\end{equation}

