[Proposition 20 (Associated local system to a covering map) of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f:X \longrightarrow Y$ be a covering map of Hausdorff, path-connected, locally contractible 
      	and locally compact topological spaces of degree $n$. Then in $\operatorname{Sh}(Y)$, we have 
      	\begin{align}
      		f_{\ast} \underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{X} \cong \underline{\mathbb{Q}}_Y \oplus \mathcal{L},
      	\end{align}
      	where $\mathcal{L}$ is a local system of rank $n-1$.

