[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2506.16260, 'Fractional Compound Poisson Random Fields on Plane'] Let $\{H_\beta(t),\ t\ge0\}$ be one parameter stable subordinator as defined in Section \ref{sub} which is independent of the time fractional CPRF $\{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}(t_1,t_2),\ (t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+\}$ with exponential compounding. Then, the following time-changed relationship holds:
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}^\beta(t_1,t_2)\overset{d}{=}H_\beta(\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}(t_1,t_2)).
	\end{equation*}

