[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2605.30560, 'Projected McKean--Vlasov Dynamics for Entropic Weak Optimal Transport'] Suppose $(\X_n)_{n \in \mathbb N} \in \rm FP_2(\mu,\nu)$. If $\AW_2(\X_n, \mathbb X) \to 0$ for some $\mathbb X \in \rm FP_2(\mu,\nu)$, then we have 
    \begin{align*}
       \liminf_{n\to \infty} \tilde I(\X_n) \geq \tilde I(\mathbb X). 
    \end{align*}
In particular, $t \mapsto \tilde I(\pi_t)$ is l.s.c. where $(\pi_t)_{t \geq 0}$ is the solution to \eqref{eq:SDE}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

