body:
[Lemma lem:invardist of arXiv:2508.03577, 'Phase Transitions in a Particle Model\\ for the Self-Adaptive Response to Cancer Dynamics'] Let $\alpha$ the rate at which we add ones to the system, i.e.,  for $k\in \left\{0, \ldots,M\right\}$
    \begin{equation}
    Q(k,k+1)=\alpha q(1-\tfrac{k}{M})\quad\text{and}\quad Q(k,0)=p\1\left\{k>0\right\}-\alpha q\1\left\{k=0\right\}\, .
\end{equation}
We then have for the invariant distribution $\left(\pi_k\right)_{k=0}^M$
\begin{equation}
    \pi_k=\frac{\Gamma(M+1)}{\Gamma(M+1-k)}\frac{\Gamma(\beta+ M-k)}{\Gamma(\beta+ M)}\frac{p}{p+\alpha q}\, ,
\end{equation}
where $\beta=pM/(\alpha q)$.

