[Definition 3 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] For $s\in\mathbb{R}$, the standard homogeneous Sobolev spaces $\dot{H}^{s}$ and inhomogeneous Sobolev spaces $H^{s}(\R^{d})$ are defined by
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\dot{H}^{s}(\mathbb{R}^{d}):=\left\{u\in\mathcal{S}':\|u\|_{\dot{H}^{s}(\R^{d})}^{2}:=\int_{\R^{d}}|\xi|^{2s}|\hat{u}(\xi)|^{2}d\xi<\infty\right\},\\
&H^{s}(\mathbb{R}^{d}):=\left\{u\in\mathcal{S}':\|u\|_{H^{s}(\R^{d})}^{2}:=\int_{\R^{d}}(1+|\xi|^{2})^{s}|\hat{u}(\xi)|^{2}d\xi<\infty\right\}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:entropy-production of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Let $\mathbb{Q}^N$ be the law of $N$ independent copies of the limit diffusion (equation eq:limit-sde of the paper), so that $Q_t^N = p_t^{\otimes N}$. Let $\mathbb{P}^N$ be the law of the interacting particle system (equation eq:particle-system of the paper) on the canonical path space $C([0,T]; (\mathbb R^d)^N)$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{i\le N} \mathbb E_{\mathbb{P}^N} \sup_{s\le T} |X_s^{i,N}|^2 < \infty,
\end{equation}
the particle system admits a unique weak solution, and the marginal relative entropy satisfies
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Ent}(P_t^N \mid Q_t^N) \le \frac14 \int_0^t \mathbb E_{P_s^N} |b_s^N - \bar b_s|^2 \,\mathrm d s,
\end{equation}
where $b^N$ and $\bar b$ are the interacting and reference drifts, respectively.

