[Proposition pr:ghf_tightness_hoelder_approx of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $\mathcal {K}_{\alpha,C;r}$ be given as above. Let $(\mathbf{P}_n)$ be a sequence of probability measures on the space of non-empty compact metric spaces equipped with bounded functions, equipped with the GHf topology. Fix $\alpha > 0$. Suppose that for every $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $C>0$ such that for any $r > 0$ there is $N \in \mathbf{N}$ such that
 \begin{equation}
  \sup_{n \ge N} \mathbf{P}_n[\mathcal {K}_{\alpha,C;r}^c] < \varepsilon .
 \end{equation}
 Then there is a subsequence $(\mathbf{P}_{n_k})$ that converges in the Prokhorov metric to a probability measure supported on $\bigcup_{C>0} \mathcal {K}_{\alpha,C}$.

