[Lemma Lem-commu of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Assume $v \in L_{\mathrm{loc}}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d}, \mathbb{R}^{d}), \,\operatorname{div} v \in L_{\mathrm{loc}}^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\, g \in L_{\mathrm{loc}}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})$. If there exists $\beta \in(0,1)$ such that $v \in C_{\mathrm{loc}}^{\beta}(\mathbb{R}^{d}, \mathbb{R}^{d})$, then for any $\rho \in C_{r}^{\infty}$ and for sufficiently small $\ensuremath{\varepsilon}$, we have, for $p\geq 1$,
\begin{align}
\left|\int_{\mathbb R^d} \mathcal{R}_{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}[v, g](x) \rho(x) d x\right|\leq  C_{r} \Vert g\Vert_{L_{r+1}^{\infty}}\left(\Vert\rho\Vert_{L_{r}^{\infty}}\Vert\operatorname{div} v\Vert_{L_{r+1}^{1}}+[v]_{C_{r+1}^{\beta}}[\rho]_{W_{r}^{1-\beta, p}}\right).
\end{align}

