[Proposition prop:loca3 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] There exists $C^\star>0$ such that for $t\in [0,1)$  and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying \begin{equation*}
1-t^2\leq C_\star^{-1}\log(\epsilon^{-1})^{-C_\star} \text{ and } \|x\|^2\leq \log(\epsilon^{-1}),
\end{equation*} 
we have
\begin{align*}
\|tX_t(x)\|^2 \leq 1-C_2^{-1}\log(\epsilon^{-1}+1)^{-K}.
\end{align*}

