[Theorem thm:sc-sdp-large of arXiv:2606.14687, 'Lehner's operator norm formulas, semidefinite programming, and spiked matrix models'] For any $\bm A_0, \bm A_1, \dots, \bm A_n \in \mathbb{C}^{d \times d}_{\mathsf{herm}}$,
    \begin{align*}
      &\Lambda_{\mathsf{sc}}(\bm A_0, \bm A_1, \dots, \bm A_n) \\
      &= \left\{\begin{array}{ll} \text{minimum of} & c \\ \text{subject to} & \left[\begin{array}{ccccc} c\bm I_d - \bm A_0 - \bm Z & \bm A_1 & \bm A_2 & \cdots & \bm A_n \\ \bm A_1 & \bm Z & \bm 0 & \cdots & \bm 0 \\ \bm A_2 & \bm 0 & \bm Z & \cdots & \bm 0 \\
                                                                                       \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ \bm A_n & \bm 0 & \bm 0 & \cdots & \bm Z \end{array}\right] \succeq \bm 0, \\ & c \in \mathbb{R}, \bm Z \in \mathbb{C}^{d \times d}_{\mathsf{herm}} \end{array}\right\} \addtocounter{equation}{1}\tag{\theequation}  \\
      \intertext{}
      &= \left\{\begin{array}{ll} \text{maximum of} & \left\langle \left[\begin{array}{cccc} \bm A_0 & -\bm A_1 & \cdots & -\bm A_n \\ -\bm A_1 & \bm 0 & \cdots & \bm 0 \\ \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ -\bm A_n & \bm 0 & \cdots & \bm 0 \end{array}\right], \left[\begin{array}{cccc} \bm \Gamma^{[0, 0]} & \bm \Gamma^{[0, 1]} & \cdots & \bm \Gamma^{[0, n]} \\ \bm \Gamma^{[1, 0]} & \bm \Gamma^{[1, 1]} & \cdots & \bm\Gamma^{[1, n]} \\ \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ \bm\Gamma^{[n, 0]} & \bm\Gamma^{[n, 1]} & \cdots & \bm \Gamma^{[n, n]} \end{array}\right]\right\rangle
\\ \text{subject to} & \bm\Gamma^{[i, j]} \in \mathbb{C}^{d \times d} \text{ and } (\bm\Gamma^{[i, j]})^* = \bm\Gamma^{[j, i]} \text{ for all } 0 \leq i, j \leq n, \\ & \bm \Gamma = [\bm \Gamma^{[i, j]}]_{i, j = 0}^n \succeq \bm 0, \\ & \bm \Gamma^{[0, 0]} = \sum_{i = 1}^n \bm \Gamma^{[i, i]}, \\ & \Tr(\bm \Gamma^{[0, 0]}) = 1 \end{array}\right\}. \addtocounter{equation}{1}\tag{\theequation} 
    \end{align*}
    The two SDPs are Lagrangian duals of one another.
    The minimum in~(equation eq:sc-sdp-large-primal of the paper) and the maximum in~(equation eq:sc-sdp-large-dual of the paper) are both always achieved. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def.Kreg of arXiv:2509.21253, '\bf Capacity in high dimensional percolation'] \rm{
			Let $x\in \partial \ball{0}{r}$. We call $x$ an $s$-(locally) good point if $\mathcal{T}_s(x)$ (resp.\ $\mathcal{T}_s^\textrm{loc}(x)$) holds. Otherwise we call it an $s$-(locally) bad point. 
			We call $x$ a $K$-regular point if it is $s$-good for all $s\geq K$ and connected to the origin inside $B(0,r)$. Otherwise, if $x$ is connected to the origin in $B(0,r)$ but not $K$-regular, we call $x$ a $K$-irregular point. We denote by $X_r^{K-\textrm{reg}}$ (resp.\ $X_r^{K-\textrm{irr}}$) the number of $K$-regular (resp.\ irregular) points on $\partial \ball{0}{r}$. }

