[Thm dyadic-LqlogL-sparse of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] Let \(1<q<\infty\), let
\(\Omega\in L^{q,1}\log L(S^{d-1})\) satisfy
(equation eq:Omega-global-cancellation of the paper), and let \(q'\leq p<\infty\).  Then the
dyadic maximal truncation associated with the kernel family
\(\{K_k^\Omega\}_{k\in\mathbb Z}\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
    \|T_{\Omega,\ast}\|_{(1,p)\text{-}\mathrm{sparse}}
    \lesssim_{d,q}
    (p')^4
    \|\Omega\|_{L^{q,1}\log L(S^{d-1})}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2606.24599, '\bf Perron--Frobenius theorem for a general tree-valued growth-fragmentation-isolation pro'] The limiting distribution $\pi$ satisfies
        \begin{align}

            \Lb^*\pi=\lab\pi,\qquad \langle\pi,|\cdot|^2\rangle<+\infty,
        \end{align}
        and $\pi(\tt) > 0$ for all $\tt \in \TT$.

