{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b632f3d0980e0f1f38d5808e39796f13129cf097893cf3337342154b2523d224","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b6/b632f3d0980e0f1f38d5808e39796f13129cf097893cf3337342154b2523d224.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:edf376dbfdf522128272a2b03189c07982b91dacd62d6e89f20a0923fbc40c5c","bundle_entry_key":"2512-09219-lemma-38-9","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_044","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_044.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2512-09219-lemma-38-9","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \emph{Step 0.\ Overview.} Let $v=\xi_{\eta}^l(L/2)$ be the midpoint of $\xi_{\eta}^l$ where $L = \ell(\xi_{\eta}^{l} ; D_h)$. It suffices to produce a metric ball of radius $L/512$ lying entirely inside $V_\eta$. If $\overline{\mathcal{B}_{L/8}(v)}\cap \partial V_\eta=\emptyset$, then we have already produced a metric ball of radius $L/8$ lying inside $V_\eta$, so for the entire proof, we shall assume that
  \begin{equation}

   \overline{\mathcal{B}_{L/8}(v)}\cap \partial V_\eta\neq \emptyset.
  \end{equation}
