body:
[Defn def-PPP of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] For any  $\Lambda\Subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and any boundary condition ${\rm bc}\in\{ {\rm per}, 0, {\rm par}\}$, we write ${{\tt Q}}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\Lambda,\rm bc}})}}}$ for the distribution of the Poisson point process (PPP) $\omega_{\rm P}$ on $\Lambda\times{\mathcal C }^{\ssup\circlearrowleft}$  with intensity measure 
\begin{equation}
	\nu_\Lambda^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm bc}})}}}({\rm d} x,{\rm d} f)\vcentcolon= \sum_{k\in\mathbb{N}}\frac{1}{k}\,{\rm d} x\otimes \mu_{x,x}^{\ssup{k,\Lambda,{\rm bc}}}({\rm d} f)\,\qquad x\in \Lambda, f\in {\mathcal C }^{\ssup\circlearrowleft}.
\end{equation}
For $\Lambda$ replaced by $\mathbb{R}^d$, we write ${{\tt Q}}$ for the PPP on $\mathbb{R}^d\times {\mathcal C }^{\ssup\circlearrowleft}$ with intensity measure $\nu({\rm d} x,{\rm d} f)=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{N}}\frac 1k {\rm d} x\otimes\mu_{x,x}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({k}})}}}({\rm d} f)$.

