body:
[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2607.10725, 'From the Airy line ensemble to the Gaussian free field'] Let $H_T$ be as in (\ref{Eq.HeightFunction}) and assume the same notation as in Definition \ref{Def.ITs}. Fix $m \geq 1$,  $x_1, \ldots, x_m \in \mathbb{R}$ and pairwise distinct $t_1,\ldots,t_m \in \mathbb{R}$. Then for all $T > 0$, we have
\begin{equation}
\E\bigl[H_T(t_1,x_1)\cdots H_T(t_m,x_m)\bigr] =
\sum_{\substack{\sigma\in S_m\\ \sigma\textup{ has no fixed points}}}
\sign(\sigma) \prod_{\substack{(i_1\,\cdots\, i_\ell)\\ \textup{cycle of }\sigma}} \calI_T(t_{i_1},x_{i_1};\ldots;t_{i_\ell},x_{i_\ell}),
\end{equation}
where the product is taken over cycles in the cycle decomposition of $\sigma$.

