[Corollary Cor.JumpDeg2 of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a constant $C(c_{-},c_{+})$ such that, for any bond $b\in(\mathbb{Z})^*$ and $\lambda\in(0,1)$,  we have the following uniform bound for $\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda$:
		\begin{equation*}
			\norm{\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda}_{L^\infty}\leqslant C m 3^{3m}\lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}},\qquad\forall b\in(\mathbb{Z})^*,\ \lambda\in(0,1),\quad\forall m\in\mathbb{N}
		\end{equation*}
		\begin{proof}
			Suppose $b=\{x,x+1\}\in\overline{(z+{\scaleobj{1.2}{\square}}_m)^*}$, we can compute $\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda(\eta)$ explicitly as:
