[Defi 19 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] For a bundle morphism $\Psi\colon A\to A'$ between Banach Lie algebroids over $\psi\colon M\to M'$ denote by $\psi^\ast A'$ the pull-back of $A'$ over $M$,
\begin{itemize}
\item $\Gamma(\psi^\ast A'_U)$ the $\mathcal{F}(U)$-module of sections of $\psi^\ast A'_U$,
\item $\Gamma_\Psi(A_U)$, the $\mathcal{F}(U)$-sub-module defined as the finite $C^\infty(U)$-linear span of the set $\left\{ \mathfrak{u}'\circ \psi, \;\; \mathfrak{u}'\in  \Gamma(\psi^\ast A'_{U'})\right\}.$
\end{itemize}

