[Lem lem-kmsw-left of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $l , n \in \mathbbm N$. The KMSW procedure restricts to a bijection between the following two sets:
\begin{itemize}
\item Walks $\mathfrak Z^{{\operatorname{b}}}_{l}$ with increments in $\{(1,-1) , (-1,0) , (1,0)\}$ and $n$ total steps, which start at $(l-1,0)$ and end at $(0 , 0 )$, and stay in $[0,\infty) \times [0,\infty)$.
\item Maps $\mathfrak m'$ of $\mathcal M_{l,1}^{\operatorname{b}}$ having $n-1$ non-boundary edges, i.e.\ $N=n+l$ total edges, with all of its left boundary edges except for the left boundary edge whose terminal vertex is the sink vertex declared to be missing.
\end{itemize}

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.26944, 'Improved bounds on the inradius and inverse inradius process of the convex hull of planar '] Consider the exit time $\tau_{m,b}$ of the hourglass domain $\mathbb{H}_{m,b}$, as defined by~\eqref{eq:exit_time} and~\eqref{eq:hourglass}. Then for any $m>1+\sqrt{2}$ and $b>0$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\E _{(x,y)}\mleft[\tau_{m,b}^2\mright] =\frac{\E _{(x,y)}[\tau_{m,b}]}{3(m^4-6m^2+1)}\mleft(\frac{m^2(m^2-5)}{m^2-1}\Big((5m^2-1)b^2-(m^2-1)x^2\Big)+(5m^2-1)y^2\mright)
\end{equation*}
for all $(x,y)\in\mathbb{H}_{m,b}$, where $\E_{(x,y)}[\tau_{m,b}]$ is explicitly calculated in~\eqref{eq:defn_u(x,y)_expectation}.

