[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{eq:integrability condition} hold for $\rho > 0$ and $I$ be a positive solution to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} that admits a measurable locally integrable function $u\colon\R_{+}\rightarrow\R$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\limsup_{t\uparrow\infty} \frac{1}{t^{\rho}}\int_{0}^{t}u(s)\,\mathrm{d}s < 0\quad\text{and}\quad \limsup_{s\uparrow\infty} \frac{1}{s^{\rho - 1}}(h(s,I_{s},N(s),\mathcal{L}(I_{s})) - u(s))\leq 0.
\end{equation*}
Then $I$ becomes extinct with exponential rate $\rho$, that is,~\eqref{eq:extinction with an exponential rate} holds. If in addition $\rho = 1$ and there is $h_{\infty}\in\R$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{(s,x,\nu)\rightarrow (\infty,0,\delta_{0})} h(s,x,N(s),\nu) = h_{\infty},
\end{equation}
then $\lim_{t\uparrow\infty}\frac{1}{t}\log(I_{t}) = h_{\infty}$ a.s.~and $h_{\infty} < 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

