[Lemma 8 ({cf. \cite[Proposition 4.1) of arXiv:2608.27398, 'Strict Stability and Strict Minimality of Regular Area-Minimizing Hypercones: A Quantitati'] {de2014sharp}}]
Let $F$ be a set of locally finite perimeter with
$F\mathbin\triangle E\Subset B_1$.  Then
\begin{align}
    D_1(F)
    &=\int_{\partial^*F\cap B_1}
      (1-X\cdot\nu_F)\,d\cH^n\\
    &=\frac12\int_{\partial^*F\cap B_1}
      |\nu_F-X|^2\,d\cH^n.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:SpectralAuxChain of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There exists a constant $c = c(C, d, m) > 0$ such that for all $\delta \in (0, 1/2]$ and $\emptyset \ne A \subseteq \mathrm{Centre}(C)$ with $\left\lvertA\right\rvert \leqslant \delta \left\lvert\mathrm{Centre}(C)\right\rvert$, and $\ell = |A|$ in the definition of $\mathbf{Y}^{\textup{aux}}$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \Lambda^{\textup{aux}}_{n}(A) \geqslant c
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n$ sufficiently large.

