\noindent
\textbf{Step 1.} Equations for \(Z^{(n)}\), \(Y^{(n)}\), and \(Q^{(n)}\).
Subtracting the two position equations in \eqref{regu-coup} gives \(\d Z_t^{(n)}=Y_t^{(n)}\,\d t\).
Since \(Y_t^{(n)}=\gamma Q_t^{(n)}
-2\gamma Z_t^{(n)}\),
we obtain
\begin{equation}
\d Z_t^{(n)}=\left[\gamma Q_t^{(n)}-2\gamma Z_t^{(n)}\right]\d t.
\end{equation}
Subtracting the two velocity equations gives
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
