body:
[Lemma 47 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $\eta\in (0,1)$ and $b\geq v + 2\lambda + 2\log(2)\pi$.
Then
\begin{multline*}
\int_{D^{2}}
e^{-(b-v-2\lambda)^{2}/(2\log(2)/\pi + 2 G_{D}(z,w))}
\LK_{\eta}(\vert w-z\vert)
\,d^{2}z\,d^{2}w
\\
\leq 
e^{-((2\pi\eta)\wedge 1)(b-v-2\lambda - 2\log(2)/\pi)}
(c_{\eta}\vert D\vert \diam(D)^{2\eta} +
\Vert 1_{D} \Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}
),
\end{multline*}
where $\vert D\vert$ is the Lebesgue measure (area) of $D$,
and $c_{\eta}>0$ is a constant depending only on $\eta$.

