[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $\hat \tau\in \hat{\mathcal T}^F$. Let $M\in \mathcal M$ be a minimal class. The following properties are satisfied:
\begin{itemize}	
\item[i)] $\hat\tau$ contains no edges going out from $M$, if $\hat \tau$ is rooted inside $M$;
\item[ii)] $\hat\tau$ contains only one edge (necessarily slow) going out from $M$, if $\hat \tau$ is not rooted inside $M$;
\item[iii)] $\hat \tau$ contains no slow edges connecting two vertices of $M$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:pointwise_three_point of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] If $d=3\alpha<6$ then
\begin{align*}
  \mathbb P_{\beta_c}(x\leftrightarrow y) \asymp \|x-y\|^{-d+\alpha} \;\; \text{ and } \;\;
\mathbb P_{\beta_c}(x\leftrightarrow y \leftrightarrow z) \asymp \sqrt{\frac{\|x-y\|^{-d+\alpha}\|y-z\|^{-d+\alpha}\|z-x\|^{-d+\alpha}}{\log(1+\min\{\|x-y\|,\|y-z\|,\|z-x\|\})}}
\end{align*}
for every triple of distinct points $x,y,z\in \mathbb Z^d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition lower bound spectrum H of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] The spectrum of $\mathbf H$ is bounded from below, i.e.\
