body:
[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.04644, 'Khinchin's and Chung's Laws of the Iterated Logarithm at Time Zero for the Linear Stochast'] Recall that $H$ is defined in \eqref{def:H}. Suppose that  Condition \ref{hypo}  holds  and that $H<1$.  Then, for every fixed $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$, the following assertions hold.
\begin{itemize}
	\item[(1)] For every $t\ge0$,
	\begin{equation}
		\|u(t,x)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}^2
		=
		\textcolor{black}{\widetilde{\kappa}}^2 t^{2H},
	\end{equation}
	where $\textcolor{black}{\widetilde{\kappa}}$ is given by \eqref{def:tilde:kappa}.

	\item[(2)] The process $\{u(t,x)\}_{t\ge0}$ is a centered Gaussian self-similar process with Hurst index $H$.
\end{itemize}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5189b9b9a10224a177d888357e5d4d8214db049596b415da082ce23c84e99c70","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/51/5189b9b9a10224a177d888357e5d4d8214db049596b415da082ce23c84e99c70.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:525324556e029776aaf256b6359ed9507f55e22fdca10d1761994a9a4555386e","bundle_entry_key":"2608-04644-lemma-6-pro","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_087","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_087.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-04644-lemma-6-pro","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \textcolor{black}{Assertion (1) follows from \cite[Theorem 4.1(i)]{CLX2026}.} 
We now prove assertion (2). Since $\{u(t,x)\}_{t\ge0}$ is a centered Gaussian
process, it is enough to verify the corresponding scaling property of its
covariance function. We give the proof for $H_0\in(1/2,1)$; the case
$H_0=1/2$ is analogous.

Let $\rho>0$ and $t,s\ge0$. By \eqref{e:covariance-noise-1} and
\eqref{eq Fourier p}, we have
\[
\begin{aligned}
&\mathbb E\left[
	\rho^{-H}u(\rho t,x)\,
	\rho^{-H}u(\rho s,x)
\right]  \\
&=
c_{H_0}\rho^{-2H}
\int_0^{\rho t}\!\!\int_0^{\rho s}
|r_1-r_2|^{2H_0-2}
