[Proposition 7 (Pull-back of the Aldous--Pitman identity) of arXiv:2607.16833, 'Dynamical Equations for Poisson Galton--Watson Trees and Component Densities of Sparse Inh'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:eigenfunction}, for $0<u\leq1/\rho$ the finite-tree
laws satisfy
\begin{equation}
 \bP_{x,u}^{\mathrm{fin}}(\dd t)
 =\frac1u\int_0^u
 T(t)(1-\rho s)
 \exp\{(s-u)(A(t)-\rho T(t))\}
 \bP_{x,s}^{\mathrm{fin}}(\dd t)\dd s.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every root law $\alpha$, the finite total-progeny laws obey
\begin{equation}
 P_{\alpha,u}^{\Lambda}(\dd\mu)
 =\frac1u\int_0^u T(\mu)(1-\rho s)
 \exp\{(s-u)(A(\mu)-\rho T(\mu))\}
 P_{\alpha,s}^{\Lambda}(\dd\mu)\dd s,
\end{equation}
where $T(\mu)=\mu(S)$ and $A(\mu)=\ip{\mu}{M\one}$.

