[Lemma lema_pomocna_za_pomocnu_dzamic of arXiv:2607.13302, 'Extending an Order-Statistic Characterization of the Exponential Distribution'] For $1\leq m\leq N$ and all feasible real $x$, it holds that
    \[
\sum_{i=0}^{N-m}
\binom{N-m}{i}m^{\overline{i}}
\frac{x^{i}}{\prod_{q=1}^{m+i}(1-qx)}
=
\frac{1}{\prod_{q=N-m+1}^{N}(1-qx)},
\]
where $m^{\overline{i}}=m(m+1)\cdots(m+i-1)$ is the rising factorial.

[Prop 36 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $M^N$ be the martingale from \eqref{mfield}. Given two probability measure $
u_1,
