[Lem 22 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $s\geq0$ and $p_0,p_1,p_2,p_1',p_2'>1$ such that $\frac{1}{p_1}+\frac{1}{p_2}=\frac{1}{p_0}=\frac{1}{p_1'}+\frac{1}{p_2'}$. Then there exists a constant $C$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \Vert (1+D^2)^\frac{s}{2}(fg)\Vert_{L^{p_0}}\leq C\Vert (1+D^2)^\frac{s}{2}f\Vert_{L^{p_1}}\Vert g\Vert_{L^{p_2}}+C\Vert (1+D^2)^\frac{s}{2}g\Vert_{L^{p_1'}}\Vert f\Vert_{L^{p_2'}}
    \end{align*}
    for all functions $f\in W^{s,p_1}\cap L^{p_2'}$ and $g\in W^{s,p_1'}\cap L^{p_2}$.

[Lemma 20 (Rectangular Gaussian Khintchine inequality) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $U,V$ be finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces, let
$A_1,\ldots,A_N\in\cL(U,V)$, and let $\xi_1,\ldots,\xi_N$ be independent
standard real Gaussian variables or independent standard circular complex
Gaussian variables.  Then, for every $p\ge2$ and $2\le r<\infty$,
\begin{equation}

 \left(\E
 \norm{\sum_k\xi_k A_k}_{\Sch_r(U,V)}^p\right)^{1/p}
 \le C\sqrt{p+r}\,
 \max\left\{
 \norm{\left(\sum_k A_kA_k^*\right)^{1/2}}_{\Sch_r(V)},
 \norm{\left(\sum_k A_k^*A_k\right)^{1/2}}_{\Sch_r(U)}
 \right\}.
\end{equation}
Consequently the same upper bound controls the $L^p(\Omega;\cL(U,V))$ norm of the series.

