body:
[Theorem thm:DARCMasLL of arXiv:2603.16824, 'Age-dependent random connection models with arc reciprocity: clustering and connectivity'] Let \(H\) be a non-negative functional that acts on rooted digraphs and their root and that only depends on a bounded graph neighbourhood of the root in the undirected sense. Assume further that the family
    	\begin{equation*} 
    		\Big(\frac{1}{\sharp \mathscr{V}(\mathscr{D}_t)}\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}\in \mathscr{D}_t}H(\boldsymbol{x},\mathscr{D}_t)\Big)_{t\geq 0}
    	\end{equation*} 
    	is uniformly integrable. Then, we have in probability and in \(L^1\),
		\begin{equation}
			\frac{1}{\sharp \mathscr{V}(\mathscr{D}_t)}\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}\in \mathscr{D}_t}H(\boldsymbol{x},\mathscr{D}_t) \longrightarrow \mathbb{E}_o[H(\0,\mathscr{D}_o)],
		\end{equation}
		as \(t\to\infty\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

