[Lemma lem: bub-trunc of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Let $\epsilon > 0$ be fixed. There exists a $C = C(\epsilon) > 0$ such that, uniformly in $M \geq 1$, in all $n \geq 2 M/ \epsilon$, and all $x_1, x_2 \in G(\epsilon, n)$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \sum_{f \not\in B(M)} \widetilde{\mathbb{P}}( 0\iff\underline{f},\,0\leftrightarrow x_1,\overline{f}\leftrightarrow x_2\,\text{off}\,\widetilde{C}(\underline{f}), \mathcal{P}(0,x_1)\cap\mathcal{P}(\overline{f},x_2)=\varnothing) \leq C n^{4-2d} M^{6-d} \ .
\end{equation}

[Theorem lem:explicit-left-M of arXiv:2602.07920, 'On the position matrix of single-shelf shuffle and card guessing'] Let $n\ge 2$ and let $i\in \mathcal E_n$. For each
$1\le a\le n$, the $a$th coordinate of the left eigenvector
$\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}=(\widetilde{w}^{(i)})^\top B^{-1}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}(a)
= \frac{1}{i!(n-i)}\Bigl[
   (-1)^{\,i-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1}
 + (-1)^{\,n-1-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1-(n-i)}
 \Bigr],
\end{equation}
where, as usual, $\binom{m}{r}=0$ if $r<0$ or $r>m$.

