[Proposition thm|Necessary2AMinus of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] Assume that $a$ is an integer multiple of $b-a$. If $S=\{i,j\}$ and if $\omega\in A_S^-$, then every geodesic on
$\sigma_i^a\sigma_j^a(\omega)$
contains both $i$ and $j$ and there is a path $\bar\gamma$ from source to sink that contains neither $i$ nor $j$ 
such that \begin{eqnarray}
T\left(\bar\gamma,\omega\right)&=&f\left(\sigma_i^a\sigma_j^a(\omega)\right)+(b-a). 

\end{eqnarray}

