[Lem 9 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] For $m\ge 2$ and $\delta>-m$, let $\beta:=(m+\delta)/(2m+\delta)$. Then for all $t\ge 1, k\ge 1$ we have
 \begin{align*}
 \E\psi_t^k &=\frac{\gC(m+\delta+k)}{\gC(m+\delta)}\cdot \frac{\gC((2m+\delta)t-2m)}{\gC((2m+\delta)t-2m+k)},\\
 \E(1-\psi_t)^k &= \frac{\gC((2m+\delta)(t-1)-m +k)}{\gC((2m+\delta)(t-1)-m)}\cdot \frac{\gC((2m+\delta)t-2m)}{\gC((2m+\delta)t-2m+k)}.
\end{align*}
In particular, we have $\norm{\theta_{ij}}_2 \cong \norm{\theta_{ij}}_1 \cong i^{\beta-1} j^{-\beta}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

