[Proposition no_big_jumps of arXiv:2606.27357, '\textbf{Typical distances in high-genus triangulations}'] For any $\varepsilon,\eta > 0$, we have 
 \begin{align}
\mathbb{P}\bigg(\exists r \in \{\log(n)^{\frac{1}{2}},\ldots,(1-\varepsilon)D_{\theta}\log(n)-1\}:\ |B_{r}^{\bullet}| \le n^{1-\varepsilon+\eta},\ |B_{r+1}^{\bullet}| \ge n^{1-\varepsilon+2\eta}\bigg) \underset{n \to +\infty}{\longrightarrow}0.
 \end{align}

