[Lem 13 of arXiv:2604.13387, 'Multiradial Schramm-Loewner evolution: \\ Infinite-time large deviations and transience'] The stopping times $\rhittingtime[\bgamma]^j(\vee)$ in~\eqref{eqn:escape-event-time} satisfy the deterministic bounds
\begin{align}
\vee - \log(4) \le n\rhittingtime[\bgamma]^j(\vee) \le \vee + \tfrac{\log(n)}{2} , \qquad \vee \ge 0 ,
\end{align}
uniformly for all curves $\bgamma \in \commonpaths[\infty]$, starting points $\btheta_0 \in \chamber$, and $j \in \{1,\ldots,n\}$.

