[Definition def:guerra-interpolation of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] Let $\{H_0(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ and $\{H_1(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ be two independent Gaussian processes. Then, the Guerra-interpolated Gaussian process $\{H_t(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ is given as
    \begin{equation}
        H_t(\sigma) = \sqrt{1-t}H_0(\sigma) + \sqrt{t}H_1(\sigma)\, ,        
    \end{equation}
    for $t \in [0,1]$.

[Lemma unregu of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] For any $g\in{\rm Lip}(1)$ and let $f_{g}$ be the solution to equation (equation stablestein of the paper), then for any $y\in(-\infty,\infty)$, we have
\begin{align}
\|f'_{g}\|_{\infty}\leq\alpha, \qquad \|f''_{g}\|_{\infty}\leq4\eta_{2,\alpha,\delta},
\end{align}
where $\|f\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}}|f(x)|$ for any function $f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$.

