[Lem 14 of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] For any $a \in \R$, the function $f_a$ belongs to $L^2(\R) \cap L^{\infty}(\R)$ and we have
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{a \in \R}\norm{f_a}_{L^{\infty}(\R)} \leq 1 \qquad \text{and} \qquad  \sup_{a \in \R} \norm{f_a}_{L^2(\R)} \leq \sqrt{5}.
\end{equation}

