body:
[Lemma 39 (Holley--Stroock) of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Let~$(\mathcal X, \mathcal B, m)$ be a measure space, and let~$\tilde p_1, \tilde p_2$ be non-negative measurable functions such that $\tilde p_1, \tilde p_2 \in L^1(m)$ and do not vanish simultaneously. Define probability measures~$\pi_i$ by $d\pi_i/dm \propto \tilde p_i$, and let~$P_i(x,dy)$ be the transition kernels of Metropolis chains with stationary measures~$\pi_i$ and a common proposal kernel~$Q(x,dy)$.

Assume that the proposal kernel is symmetric in the following sense: for each~$x \in \mathcal X$, $Q(x,dy)$ admits a density~$q(x,y)$ on~$\mathcal X \setminus \{x\}$ with respect to~$m(dy)$, and $q(x,y) = q(y,x)$ for all~$x,y \in \mathcal X$.

If there exist constants~$a,b>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    a \leq \frac{\tilde p_1(x)}{\tilde p_2(x)} \leq b\,, \quad \forall x \in \mathcal X,
\end{equation}
then
\begin{equation}
   (b^{-1}a)^2\,\gap(P_2) \leq \gap(P_1) \leq (a^{-1}b)^2\,\gap(P_2)\,.
\end{equation}

