[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2604.10820, 'A Strict Gap Between Relaxed and Partition-Constrained\\ Spectral Compression in a Six-Sta'] If $T$ is positive self-adjoint with eigenvalues
\begin{equation*}
\lambda_1(T)\ge \lambda_2(T)\ge \lambda_3(T)\ge \cdots \ge 0,
\end{equation*}
then
\begin{equation*}
\mathfrak D^{\mathrm{rel}}_3(T)=\lambda_1(T)\lambda_2(T)\lambda_3(T).
\end{equation*}

