[Corollary cor:upper_lower_general of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{X}$ be in the domain of non-normal attraction of an $\alpha$-stable process $\bm{Z}$.\\ 
{\normalfont(a)} Let $\alpha\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}$ and Assumption~(\nameref{asm:C}) hold for some $\delta>0$ and $p\ne\alpha-1$. Suppose $G$ is $C^1$ with derivative $\widetilde{G}(t)/t$, where $|\widetilde{G}|\in\mbox{SV}_0$. Further suppose there exists some $\phi\in\mbox{SV}_0\cap\mbox{SV}_\infty$ satisfying $\phi(x)\geqslant\sup_{t>0,y\in[x\wedge 1,x\vee1]}\widetilde{G}(yt)/\widetilde{G}(t)$ for $x>0$. Define $L(t)\coloneqq |\widetilde{G}(t)|/G(t)$, then, for any $q\in(0,1]\cap(0,\alpha)\setminus\{\alpha/(p+1),\alpha/(\alpha\delta+1)\}$ with $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^q]<\infty$, we have $\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t,\bm{Z})=\mathcal{O}(L(t)^q)$ as $t \downarrow 0$ and
\begin{align*}
    \max\{\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t_1,\bm{Z}_1)
    ,\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^{2t}_1,\bm{Z}_1)\}
    \geqslant \frac{q\log 2}{3}\mathds{E}\big[|\bm{Z}_1|^q\big]\cdot L(t),
    \quad \text{for all sufficiently small }t >0.
\end{align*}
{\normalfont(b)} Define iteratively the functions $\ell_1(t)=\log(e+t)$ and $\ell_{n+1}(t)=\log(e+\ell_n(t))$ for $t\geqslant 0$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$. Suppose $G(t)$ is eventually equal to $\ell_n(1/t)^{q_n}\cdots\ell_m(1/t)^{q_m}$ where $1\leqslant n\leqslant m$ in $\mathbb{N}$ and either $q_n,\ldots,q_m\geqslant 0$ with $q_n,q_m>0$ or $q_n,\ldots,q_m\leqslant 0$ with $q_n,q_m<0$. Then $G$ satisfies the assumptions of Part (a). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

