[Prop Prop_TotallyReal=>UniformlyFredholm of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let $({\mathbf{B}},f,{\mathbf{V}})$ be a family of local residue conditions such that
  for every $b \in {\mathbf{B}}$, $x \in Z_b$, and $v \in T_xZ_b {\backslash}\set{0}$
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{V}}_{(b,x)} \oplus J_{{\mathbf{p}}_b}\gamma(v) {\mathbf{V}}_{(b,x)} = \check S_{{\mathbf{p}}_b,x}.
  \end{equation*}
  Denote by $({\mathbf{B}},f,{\mathbf{R}})$ the corresponding family of residue conditions.
  If ${\mathfrak a} \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace f^*\mathbf{F} \to f^*\mathbf{F}$ is a map of tame Fréchet bundles of order zero,
  then
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{D}}_{\mathbf{R}} + {\mathfrak a} \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{R}} \to f^*\mathbf{F}
  \end{equation*}
  is uniformly Fredholm.
  Moreover,
  for every $b_0 \in {\mathbf{B}}$
  the maps $\pi \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{R}}|_\mathscr{U} \to \mathrm{Def}$ and $\iota \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \mathrm{Ob} \hookrightarrow f^*\mathbf{F}|_\mathscr{U}$ in (Def_LinearUniformlyFredholm of the paper) can be chosen such that there is a compact subset $K \subseteq X$ such that for every
  $b \in \mathscr{U}$
  the following hold:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item
    $K \subseteq X{\backslash} Z_b$;
  \item
    if $\phi \in \mathbf{E}_{{\mathbf{R}},b}$ has $\supp(\phi) \cap K = \varnothing$, then $\pi(\phi) = 0$; and
  \item  
    $\supp(\iota(o)) \subseteq K$ for every $o \in \mathrm{Ob}_b$.
  \end{enumerate}

