[Lemma no_skip_large_interval_small_escape_prob of arXiv:2411.04795, 'Metastable Distributions of Semi-Markov Processes'] Suppose that assumptions (a) - (c) and (f) from section (Reduction to a process with nearly independent transition times and transition probabilities of the paper) hold. If the states $\{1, \dots, M'\} $ form one ergodic class with respect to $P_{ij}^0$, then for every $\delta > 0,$ there are $L, \varepsilon_0 > 0$ such that $$ \mathbb P \left({ X_t^{x, \varepsilon} \in S_i, X_s^{x, \varepsilon} \in S_i  \ {\rm for \ every} \ s \in [t , t + L ] }\right)  < \delta,  $$
 $$ \begin{aligned} \mathbb P \left({X_t^{x, \varepsilon} \in S_i, \ {\rm the \ next \ state \ visited \ is \ in \ } S \setminus S' }\right) < \delta  \end{aligned} $$
 for every $1 \le i \le  M', x \in S, \varepsilon \le \varepsilon_0, $ and $ t \ge 0.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 12 (Bruhat--Schwartz space) of arXiv:2609.03647, 'Extension Problems for the Vladimirov--Taibleson Operator and the Hierarchical Laplacian'] The Bruhat--Schwartz space $\mathcal{S}(X)$ is the set of locally constant
    functions with compact support. Its zero-mean subspace is defined by
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{S}_0(X)=\left\{f\in \mathcal{S}(X)\ \middle|\
        \int_Xf(x)dm(x)=0\right\}.
    \end{align*}

[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $X$ be a centered Volterra Gaussian process satisfying the Decreusefond--\"Ust\"unel conditions (Definition~(def:DU of the paper)), with operator triple $(D,\delta,\Pi)$ satisfying Assumptions~(ass:chain of the paper)--(ass:energy of the paper) (verified in Proposition~(prop:voltverify of the paper)). Let $\varphi\in C^3_b(\mathbb{R})$. Then for all $t\in[0,T]$,
\begin{equation}
\varphi(X_t) = \varphi(0) + \delta(\varphi'(X)\Pi DX\cdot\mathbf{1}_{[0,t]}) + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \varphi''(X_s)\,d\Gamma^X(s),
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma^X(s) = \left\|\Pi DX_s\right\|_\mathcal{H}^2 = R^X(s,s) = \mathbb{E}[X_s^2]$ is the (deterministic) energy function, the last integral is a Stieltjes integral against the bounded variation measure $d\Gamma^X$, and the equality holds in $L^2(\Omega)$. When $\Gamma^X$ is absolutely continuous with density $\dot{\Gamma}^X$, the correction reduces to $\frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \varphi''(X_s)\dot{\Gamma}^X(s)\,ds$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 3 (Moderate deviation principle) of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] Let $(a_n)_{n\geq 1}$ be any positive sequence satisfying
\begin{equation}
 a_n\to\infty,
 \qquad
 \frac{a_n}{\sqrt n}\to0.
\end{equation}
Then
\[
 \frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}
\]
satisfies on $\R$ a moderate deviation principle with speed $a_n^2$ and good rate function
\[
 I(x)=\frac{x^2}{2},\quad x\in\R.
\]
Equivalently, for every Borel set $B\subset\R$,
\begin{align*}
 -\inf_{x\in B^\circ}\frac{x^2}{2}
 &\le \liminf_{n\to\infty}\frac1{a_n^2}
 \log\Pp\left(\frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}\in B\right)\\
 &\le \limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac1{a_n^2}
 \log\Pp\left(\frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}\in B\right)
 \le-\inf_{x\in\overline B}\frac{x^2}{2}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 20 (Equivalence in the rational case) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Assume that there are $\M\in\N$ and a weak partition $(\sfM_s)_{s\in\sS}$ of $\{1,\dots,\M\}$ such that
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{N\to\infty}\lambda_{N,s} = |\sfM_s|/\M ,\quad\forall s \in \sS.
\end{align*}
Let $\bar F^\Vec_N$ be the free energy with $\bxi$ specified in~\eqref{e.bxi=mp}. For every $t\in\R_+$ and $q\in \mcl Q_\infty^\sS$, let $\bq^\Vec\in\mcl Q_\infty^\D$ be given as in~\eqref{e.a^vec=}. We have
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{N\to\infty}\Ll|  \bar F_N(t,q)- \M^{-1}\bar  F^\Vec_{\lceil N/\M\rceil}\Ll(t,\bq^\Vec\Rr)\Rr|=0.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem cA5 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] For any $q\in(0,p)$,
there exists $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}

 \sup_{t\in[0, T]}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^q\Big]
\leq C^{N+1}h_n^{\frac{p-q}{\chi}\wedge q}(1+2\|x\|^p) +(2N+1) C^{N+1}h_n^{\frac{q}{2}\wedge 1}
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
for $n$ large enough uniformly over
$N\in\mathbb{N}_0$ and $N$-tuples $\{t_1,\dots, t_N\}\in C^n_N$.

